ability and design\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0130\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein structural motifs and surfaces\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein folds and structural domains\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein disordered structure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3538\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein secondary structure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3542\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Protein stability, folding (in 3D space) and protein sequence-structure-function relationships.  This includes for example study of inter-atomic or inter-residue interactions in protein (3D) structures, the effect of mutation, and the design of proteins with specific properties, typically by designing changes (via site-directed mutagenesis) to an existing protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Proteins||Protein structure analysis||Protein folding, stability and design\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0078||topic_2814||topic_0130\"}, {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein folding, stability and design\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_0130\"}], \"name\": \"Protein folding, stability and design\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0130\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Protein design\", \"Protein folding\", \"Protein residue interactions\", \"Protein stability\", \"Rational protein design\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Structural features or common 3D motifs within protein structures, including the surface of a protein structure, such as biological interfaces with other molecules.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Proteins||Protein structure analysis||Protein structural motifs and surfaces\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0078||topic_2814||topic_0166\"}, {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein structural motifs and surfaces\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_0166\"}], \"name\": \"Protein structural motifs and surfaces\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Protein 3D motifs\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Protein structural features\", \"Protein structural motifs\", \"Protein surfaces\", \"Structural motifs\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein tertiary structural domains and folds in a protein or polypeptide chain.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Proteins||Protein structure analysis||Protein folds and structural domains\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0078||topic_2814||topic_0736\"}, {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein folds and structural domains\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_0736\"}], \"name\": \"Protein folds and structural domains\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Intramembrane regions\", \"Protein domains\", \"Protein folds\", \"Protein membrane regions\", \"Protein structural domains\", \"Protein topological domains\", \"Protein transmembrane regions\", \"Transmembrane regions\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Disordered structure in a protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Proteins||Protein structure analysis||Protein disordered structure\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0078||topic_2814||topic_3538\"}, {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein disordered structure\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_3538\"}], \"name\": \"Protein disordered structure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3538\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Protein features (disordered structure)\"], \"narrow_s