.org/topic_0166\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Protein 3D motifs\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Protein structural features\", \"Protein structural motifs\", \"Protein surfaces\", \"Structural motifs\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein tertiary structural domains and folds in a protein or polypeptide chain.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein folds and structural domains\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_0736\"}, \"name\": \"Protein folds and structural domains\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Intramembrane regions\", \"Protein domains\", \"Protein folds\", \"Protein membrane regions\", \"Protein structural domains\", \"Protein topological domains\", \"Protein transmembrane regions\", \"Transmembrane regions\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Disordered structure in a protein.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein disordered structure\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_3538\"}, \"name\": \"Protein disordered structure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3538\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Protein features (disordered structure)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Secondary structure (predicted or real) of a protein, including super-secondary structure.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Structure analysis||Protein structure analysis||Protein secondary structure\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0081||topic_2814||topic_3542\"}, \"name\": \"Protein secondary structure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3542\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Protein features (secondary structure)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Protein super-secondary structure\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The study of evolutionary relationships amongst organisms.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Phylogeny\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0084\"}, \"name\": \"Phylogeny\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0084\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic clocks\", \"Phylogenetic dating\", \"Phylogenetic simulation\", \"Phylogenetic stratigraphy\", \"Phylogeny reconstruction\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylogenetics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293\"}, {\"name\": \"Cladistics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3944\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The study of evolutionary relationships amongst organisms from analysis of genetic information (typically gene or protein sequences).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Phylogeny||Phylogenetics\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0084||topic_3293\"}, \"name\": \"Phylogenetics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The biological classification of organisms by categorizing them in groups (\\\"clades\\\") based on their most recent common ancestor.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Phylogeny||Cladistics\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0084||topic_3944\"}, \"name\": \"Cladistics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3944\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Tree of life\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The archival, detection, prediction and analysis of positional features such as functional and other key sites, in molecular sequences and the conserved patterns (motifs, profiles etc.) that may be used to describe them.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Computational biology||Sequence sites, features and motifs\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3307||topic_0160\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence sites, features and motifs\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narr