"DNA-Seq\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Chromosome walking\", \"Clone verification\", \"DNase-Seq\", \"High throughput sequencing\", \"High-throughput sequencing\", \"NGS\", \"NGS data analysis\", \"Next gen sequencing\", \"Next generation sequencing\", \"Panels\", \"Primer walking\", \"Sanger sequencing\", \"Targeted next-generation sequencing panels\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ChIP-seq\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3169\"}, {\"name\": \"RNA-Seq\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170\"}, {\"name\": \"Whole genome sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3673\"}, {\"name\": \"Exome sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3676\"}, {\"name\": \"Metagenomic sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3837\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The analysis of protein-DNA interactions where chromatin immunoprecipitation (ChIP) is used in combination with massively parallel DNA sequencing to identify the binding sites of DNA-associated proteins.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Sequencing||ChIP-seq\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3168||topic_3169\"}, {\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Immunoprecipitation experiment||ChIP-seq\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3656||topic_3169\"}], \"name\": \"ChIP-seq\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3169\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ChIP-sequencing\", \"Chip Seq\", \"Chip sequencing\", \"Chip-sequencing\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"ChIP-exo\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A topic concerning high-throughput sequencing of cDNA to measure the RNA content (transcriptome) of a sample, for example, to investigate how different alleles of a gene are expressed, detect post-transcriptional mutations or identify gene fusions.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Sequencing||RNA-Seq\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3168||topic_3170\"}], \"name\": \"RNA-Seq\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"RNA sequencing\", \"RNA-Seq analysis\", \"Small RNA sequencing\", \"Small RNA-Seq\", \"Small-Seq\", \"Transcriptome profiling\", \"WTSS\", \"Whole transcriptome shotgun sequencing\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"MicroRNA sequencing\", \"miRNA-seq\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Laboratory technique to sequence the complete DNA sequence of an organism\'s genome at a single time.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Sequencing||Whole genome sequencing\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3168||topic_3673\"}], \"name\": \"Whole genome sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3673\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genome sequencing\", \"WGS\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"De novo genome sequencing\", \"Whole genome resequencing\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Laboratory technique to sequence all the protein-coding regions in a genome, i.e., the exome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Sequencing||Exome sequencing\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3168||topic_3676\"}], \"name\": \"Exome sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3676\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Exome\", \"Exome analysis\", \"Exome capture\", \"Targeted exome capture\", \"WES\", \"Whole exome sequencing\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Approach which samples, in parallel, all genes in all organisms present in a given sample, e.g. to provide insight into biodiversity and function.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Sequencing||Metagenomic sequencing\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3168||topic_3837\"}], \"name\": \"Metagenomic sequencing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3837\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Shotgun metagenomic sequencing\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The visual representation of an object.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382\"}], \"name\": \"Imaging\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Diffraction experiment\", \"Microscopy\", \"Microscopy imaging\", \"Optical super resolution microscopy\", \"Photonic force microscopy\", \"Photonic microscopy\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"NMR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0593\"}, {\"name\": \"Electron microscopy\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0611\"}, {\"name\": \"X-ray diffraction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_2828\"}, {\"name\": \"Bioimaging\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3383\"}, {\"name\": \"Medical imaging\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3384\"}, {\"name\": \"Light microscopy\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3385\"}, {\"name\": \"MRI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3444\"}, {\"name\": \"Neutron diffraction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3448\"}, {\"name\": \"Tomography\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3452\"}, {\"name\": \"Echography\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3954\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"An analytical technique that exploits the magenetic properties of certain atomic nuclei to provide information on the structure, dynamics, reaction state and chemical environment of molecules.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||NMR\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_0593\"}, \"name\": \"NMR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0593\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"NMR spectroscopy\", \"Nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"HOESY\", \"Heteronuclear Overhauser Effect Spectroscopy\", \"NOESY\", \"Nuclear Overhauser Effect Spectroscopy\", \"ROESY\", \"Rotational Frame Nuclear Overhauser Effect Spectroscopy\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The study of matter by studying the interference pattern from firing electrons at a sample, to analyse structures at resolutions higher than can be achieved using light.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Electron microscopy\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_0611\"}, \"name\": \"Electron microscopy\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0611\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Electron crystallography\", \"SEM\", \"Scanning electron microscopy\", \"Single particle electron microscopy\", \"TEM\", \"Transmission electron microscopy\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The study of matter and their structure by means of the diffraction of X-rays, typically the diffraction pattern caused by the regularly spaced atoms of a crystalline sample.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||X-ray diffraction\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_2828\"}, \"name\": \"X-ray diffraction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_2828\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Crystallography\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"X-ray crystallography\", \"X-ray microscopy\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The use of imaging techniques to understand biology.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Bioimaging\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3383\"}], \"name\": \"Bioimaging\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3383\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Biological imaging\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The use of imaging techniques for clinical purposes for medical research.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Medical imaging\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3384\"}], \"name\": \"Medical imaging\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3384\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Neuroimaging\", \"Nuclear medicine\", \"Radiology\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The use of optical instruments to magnify the image of an object.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Light microscopy\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3385\"}], \"name\": \"Light microscopy\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3385\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Techniques that uses magnetic fields and radiowaves to form images, typically to investigate the anatomy and physiology of the human body.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||MRI\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3444\"}], \"name\": \"MRI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3444\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MRT\", \"Magnetic resonance imaging\", \"Magnetic resonance tomography\", \"NMRI\", \"Nuclear magnetic resonance imaging\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The study of matter by studying the diffraction pattern from firing neutrons at a sample, typically to determine atomic and/or magnetic structure.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Neutron diffraction\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3448\"}, \"name\": \"Neutron diffraction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3448\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Neutron diffraction experiment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Elastic neutron scattering\", \"Neutron microscopy\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Imaging in sections (sectioning), through the use of a wave-generating device (tomograph) that generates an image (a tomogram).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Tomography\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3452\"}], \"name\": \"Tomography\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3452\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"CT\", \"Computed tomography\", \"TDM\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Electron tomography\", \"PET\", \"Positron emission tomography\", \"X-ray tomography\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A diagnostic imaging technique based on the application of ultrasound.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Imaging||Echography\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3382||topic_3954\"}], \"name\": \"Echography\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3954\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Standardized echography\", \"Ultrasound imaging\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Diagnostic sonography\", \"Medical ultrasound\", \"Standard echography\", \"Ultrasonography\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Genotype experiment including case control, population, and family studies. These might use array based methods and re-sequencing methods.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Genotyping experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3516\"}], \"name\": \"Genotyping experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3516\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Microarray experiments including conditions, protocol, sample:data relationships etc.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Microarray experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3518\"}], \"name\": \"Microarray experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Microarrays\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression microarray\", \"Genotyping array\", \"Methylation array\", \"MicroRNA array\", \"Multichannel microarray\", \"One channel microarray\", \"Proprietary platform micoarray\", \"RNA chips\", \"RNA microarrays\", \"Reverse phase protein array\", \"SNP array\", \"Tiling arrays\", \"Tissue microarray\", \"Two channel microarray\", \"aCGH microarray\", \"mRNA microarray\", \"miRNA array\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PCR experiments, e.g. quantitative real-time PCR.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||PCR experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3519\"}], \"name\": \"PCR experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3519\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Polymerase chain reaction\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Quantitative PCR\", \"RT-qPCR\", \"Real Time Quantitative PCR\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Proteomics experiments.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Proteomics experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3520\"}], \"name\": \"Proteomics experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"2D PAGE experiment\", \"DIA\", \"Data-independent acquisition\", \"MS\", \"MS experiments\", \"Mass spectrometry\", \"Mass spectrometry experiments\", \"Northern blot experiment\", \"Spectrum demultiplexing\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"RNAi experiments.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||RNAi experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3523\"}], \"name\": \"RNAi experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3523\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Biological computational model experiments (simulation), for example the minimum information required in order to permit its correct interpretation and reproduction.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Simulation experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3524\"}], \"name\": \"Simulation experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3524\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Experimental techniques to purify a protein-DNA crosslinked complex.  Usually sequencing follows e.g. in the techniques ChIP-chip, ChIP-seq and MeDIP-seq.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Laboratory techniques||Immunoprecipitation experiment\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_3361||topic_3656\"}], \"name\": \"Immunoprecipitation experiment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_3656\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Chromatin immunoprecipitation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"n