gy or bioinformatics. This includes formal ontologies, controlled vocabularies, structured glossary, symbols and terminology or other related resource.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Informatics||Ontology and terminology\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_0605||topic_0089\"}], \"name\": \"Ontology and terminology\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0089\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Applied ontology\", \"Ontologies\", \"Ontology\", \"Ontology relations\", \"Terminology\", \"Upper ontology\"], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0091\": {\"definition\": \"The archival, curation, processing and analysis of complex biological data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Informatics||Bioinformatics\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_0605||topic_0091\"}], \"name\": \"Bioinformatics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0607\": {\"definition\": \"Laboratory management and resources, for example, catalogues of biological resources for use in the lab including cell lines, viruses, plasmids, phages, DNA probes and primers and so on.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Informatics||Laboratory information management\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_0605||topic_0607\"}], \"name\": \"Laboratory information management\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0607\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Laboratory resources\"], \"children\": []}, \"topic_2258\": {\"definition\": \"The application of information technology to chemistry in biological research environment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Topic||Informatics||Cheminformatics\", \"key\": \"topic_0003||topic_0605||topic_2258\"}], \"name\": \"Cheminformatics\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_2258\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Chemical informatics\", \"Chemoinformatics\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_3063\": {\"definition\": \"The application of information technology to health, disease 