ology.org/operation_3938\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Virtual screening is used in drug discovery to identify potential drug compounds.  It involves searching libraries of small molecules in order to identify those molecules which are most likely to bind to a drug target (typically a protein receptor or enzyme).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Design||Small molecule design||Virtual screening\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2430||operation_4009||operation_3938\"}, \"name\": \"Virtual screening\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3938\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Ligand-based screening\", \"Ligand-based virtual screening\", \"Structure-based screening\", \"Structured-based virtual screening\", \"Virtual ligand screening\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compare two or more entities, typically the sequence or structure (or derivatives) of macromolecules, to identify equivalent subunits.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2928\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2928\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Alignment construction\", \"Alignment generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292\"}, {\"name\": \"Structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0295\"}, {\"name\": \"Fold recognition\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align (identify equivalent sites within) molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Alignment||Sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2928||operation_0292\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence alignment construction\", \"Sequence alignment ge