ative data as set of different profiles, where each profile is plotted versus different entities or samples on the X-axis.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Expression data visualisation||Clustering profile plotting\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_0571||operation_2935\"}, \"name\": \"Clustering profile plotting\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2935\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Clustered quantitative data plotting\", \"Clustered quantitative data rendering\", \"Wave graph plotting\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Microarray cluster temporal graph rendering\", \"Microarray wave graph plotting\", \"Microarray wave graph rendering\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Generate a plot of distances (distance or correlation matrix) between expression values.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Expression data visualisation||Proximity map plotting\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_0571||operation_2937\"}, \"name\": \"Proximity map plotting\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2937\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Distance map rendering\", \"Distance matrix plotting\", \"Distance matrix rendering\", \"Proximity map rendering\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Correlation matrix plotting\", \"Correlation matrix rendering\", \"Microarray distance map rendering\", \"Microarray proximity map plotting\", \"Microarray proximity map rendering\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Visualise clustered expression data using a tree diagram.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Expression data visualisation||Dendrogram visualisation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_0571||operation_2938\"}, \"name\": \"Dendrogram visualisation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2938\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Dendrogram plotting\", \"Dendrograph plotting\", \"Dendrograph visualisation\", \"Expression data tree or dendrogram rendering\", \"Expression data tree visualisation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Microarray 2-way dendrogram rendering\", \"Microarray checks view rendering\", \"Microarray matrix tree plot rendering\", \"Microarray tree or dendrogram rendering\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Visualise gene expression data after hierarchical clustering for representing hierarchical relationships.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Expression data visualisation||Treemap visualisation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_0571||operation_2942\"}, \"name\": \"Treemap visualisation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2942\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Expression data tree-map rendering\", \"Treemapping\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Microarray tree-map rendering\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Analyse a known network of gene regulation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Gene regulatory network analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_1781\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Network analysis||Gene regulatory network analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3927||operation_1781\"}], \"name\": \"Gene regulatory network analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_1781\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Gene regulatory network comparison\", \"Gene regulatory network modelling\", \"Regulatory network comparison\", \"Regulatory network modelling\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify classes of genes or proteins that are over or under-represented in a large set of genes or proteins.  For example analysis of a set of genes corresponding to a gene expression profile, annotated with Gene Ontology (GO) concepts, where eventual over-/under-representation of certain GO concept within the studied set of genes is revealed.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Gene-set enrichment analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_2436\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Enrichment analysis||Gene-set enrichment analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3501||operation_2436\"}], \"name\": \"Gene-set enrichment analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Functional enrichment analysis\", \"GSEA\", \"Gene-set over-represenation analysis\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Gene set analysis\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Predict a network of gene regulation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Gene regulatory network prediction\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_2437\"}, \"name\": \"Gene regulatory network prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2437\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Combine classical quantitative trait loci (QTL) analysis with gene expression profiling, for example, to describe describe cis- and trans-controlling elements for the expression of phenotype associated genes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||Gene expression QTL analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_3232\"}], \"name\": \"Gene expression QTL analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3232\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression QTL profiling\", \"Gene expression quantitative trait loci profiling\", \"eQTL profiling\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Analyze data from RNA-seq experiments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||RNA-Seq analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_3680\"}, \"name\": \"RNA-Seq analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"RNA-seq read count analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3563\"}, {\"name\": \"RNA-seq time series data analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3565\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Analyze read counts from RNA-seq experiments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||RNA-Seq analysis||RNA-seq read count analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_3680||operation_3563\"}, \"name\": \"RNA-seq read count analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3563\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Analyze time series data from an RNA-seq experiment.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||RNA-Seq analysis||RNA-seq time series data analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_3680||operation_3565\"}, \"name\": \"RNA-seq time series data analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3565\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The analysis of microRNAs (miRNAs) : short, highly conserved small noncoding RNA molecules that are naturally occurring plant and animal genomes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Expression analysis||miRNA expression analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2495||operation_3792\"}], \"name\": \"miRNA expression analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3792\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"miRNA expression profiling\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Analyse a genetic variation, for example to annotate its location, alleles, classification, and effects on individual transcripts predicted for a gene model.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197\"}], \"name\": \"Genetic variation analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3197\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genetic variation annotation\", \"Sequence variation analysis\", \"Variant analysis\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Transcript variant analysis\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Genotyping\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196\"}, {\"name\": \"Variant classification\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3225\"}, {\"name\": \"Variant prioritisation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3226\"}, {\"name\": \"Variant calling\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227\"}, {\"name\": \"Structural variation detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3228\"}, {\"name\": \"Variant pattern analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3504\"}, {\"name\": \"Reference identification\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3703\"}, {\"name\": \"Collapsing methods\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3791\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Analyse DNA sequence data to identify differences between the genetic composition (genotype) of an individual compared to other individual\'s or a reference sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Genotyping\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3196\"}], \"name\": \"Genotyping\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Multilocus sequence typing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3840\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Genotyping of multiple loci, typically characterizing microbial species isolates using internal fragments of multiple housekeeping genes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Genotyping||Multilocus sequence typing\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3196||operation_3840\"}], \"name\": \"Multilocus sequence typing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3840\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MLST\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Classify variants based on their potential effect on genes, especially functional effects on the expressed proteins.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant classification\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3225\"}, \"name\": \"Variant classification\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3225\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify biologically interesting variants by prioritizing individual variants, for example, homozygous variants absent in control genomes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant prioritisation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3226\"}], \"name\": \"Variant prioritisation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3226\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Detect, identify and map mutations, such as single nucleotide polymorphisms, short indels and structural variants, in multiple DNA sequences. Typically the alignment and comparison of the fluorescent traces produced by DNA sequencing hardware, to study genomic alterations.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227\"}, \"name\": \"Variant calling\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Variant mapping\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Allele calling\", \"Exome variant detection\", \"Genome variant detection\", \"Germ line variant calling\", \"Mutation detection\", \"Somatic variant calling\", \"de novo mutation detection\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0265\"}, {\"name\": \"Indel detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0452\"}, {\"name\": \"SNP detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Detect frameshifts in DNA sequences, including frameshift sites and signals, and frameshift errors from sequencing projects.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||Frameshift detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0265\"}, \"name\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0265\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Frameshift error detection\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify insertion, deletion and duplication events from a sequence alignment.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||Indel detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0452\"}, \"name\": \"Indel detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0452\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Indel discovery\", \"Sequence alignment analysis (indel detection)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Find single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) - single nucleotide change in base positions - between sequences. Typically done for sequences from a high-throughput sequencing experiment that differ from a reference genome and which might, especially by reference to population frequency or functional data, indicate a polymorphism.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||SNP detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0484\"}, \"name\": \"SNP detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"SNP calling\", \"SNP discovery\", \"Single nucleotide polymorphism detection\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Detect large regions in a genome subject to copy-number variation, or other structural variations in genome(s).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228\"}], \"name\": \"Structural variation detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3228\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structural variation discovery\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Copy number variation detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3961\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Identify where sections of the genome are repeated and the number of repeats in the genome varies between individuals.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961\"}], \"name\": \"Copy number variation detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3961\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"CNV detection\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Copy number estimation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3233\"}, {\"name\": \"Deletion detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3962\"}, {\"name\": \"Duplication detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3963\"}, {\"name\": \"Complex CNV detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3964\"}, {\"name\": \"Amplification detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3965\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Estimate the number of copies of loci of particular gene(s) in DNA sequences typically from gene-expression profiling technology based on microarray hybridisation-based experiments. For example, estimate copy number (or marker dosage) of a dominant marker in samples from polyploid plant cells or tissues, or chromosomal gains and losses in tumors.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Copy number estimation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3233\"}], \"name\": \"Copy number estimation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3233\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Transcript copy number estimation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify deletion events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Deletion detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3962\"}], \"name\": \"Deletion detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3962\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify duplication events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Duplication detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3963\"}], \"name\": \"Duplication detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3963\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify copy number variations which are complex, e.g. multi-allelic variations that have many structural alleles and have rearranged multiple times in the ancestral genomes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Complex CNV detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3964\"}], \"name\": \"Complex CNV detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3964\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify amplification events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Amplification detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3965\"}], \"name\": \"Amplification detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3965\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify and map patterns of genomic variations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant pattern analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3504\"}], \"name\": \"Variant pattern analysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3504\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identification of the best reference for mapping for a specific dataset from a list of potential references, when performing genetic variation analysis.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Reference identification\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3703\"}], \"name\": \"Reference identification\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3703\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A method whereby data on several variants are \\\"collapsed\\\" into a single covariate based on regions such as genes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic var