enetic tree generation (quartet methods)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Construct a phylogenetic tree by using artificial-intelligence methods, for example genetic algorithms.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Phylogenetic inference||Phylogenetic inference (method centric)||Phylogenetic inference (AI methods)\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0323||operation_0539||operation_0549\"}, \"name\": \"Phylogenetic inference (AI methods)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0549\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree construction (AI methods)\", \"Phylogenetic tree generation (AI methods)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Construct a phylogenetic species tree, for example, from a genome-wide sequence comparison.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Phylogenetic inference||Species tree construction\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0323||operation_0544\"}, \"name\": \"Species tree construction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0544\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic species tree construction\", \"Phylogenetic species tree generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Construct a \\\"gene tree\\\" which represents the evolutionary history of the genes included in the study.  This can be used to predict families of genes and gene function based on their position in a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Phylogenetic inference||Gene tree construction\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0323||operation_0553\"}, \"name\": \"Gene tree construction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0553\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree analysis (gene family prediction)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compare two or more phylogenetic trees to produce a consensus tree.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Phylogenetic inference||Consensus tree construction\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0323||operation_0555\"}, \"name\": \"Consensus tree construction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0555\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree construction (consensus)\", \"Phylogenetic tree generation (consensus)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Reconstructing the inner node labels of a phylogenetic tree from its leafes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Phylogenetic inference||Phylogenetic reconstruction\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0323||operation_3478\"}, \"name\": \"Phylogenetic reconstruction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3478\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree reconstruction\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Gene tree reconstruction\", \"Species tree reconstruction\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align RNA secondary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||RNA secondary structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0502\"}, \"name\": \"RNA secondary structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0502\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"RNA secondary structure alignment construction\", \"RNA secondary structure alignment generation\", \"Secondary structure alignment (RNA)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Generate a heat map of expression data from e.g. microarray data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Heat map generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_0531\"}, \"name\": \"Heat map generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0531\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Heat map construction\", \"Heatmap generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Calculate a 3D-1D scoring matrix from analysis of protein sequence and structural data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||3D-1D scoring matrix generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2239\"}, \"name\": \"3D-1D scoring matrix generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2239\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"3D-1D scoring matrix construction\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compare two or more entities, typically the sequence or structure (or derivatives) of macromolecules, to identify equivalent subunits.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928\"}, \"name\": \"Alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2928\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Alignment construction\", \"Alignment generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292\"}, {\"name\": \"Structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0295\"}, {\"name\": \"Fold recognition\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align (identify equivalent sites within) molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence alignment construction\", \"Sequence alignment generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Consensus-based sequence alignment\", \"Constrained sequence alignment\", \"Multiple sequence alignment (constrained)\", \"Sequence alignment (constrained)\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Structure-based sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0294\"}, {\"name\": \"Sequence profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0300\"}, {\"name\": \"Pairwise sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491\"}, {\"name\": \"Multiple sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492\"}, {\"name\": \"Local alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0495\"}, {\"name\": \"Global alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0496\"}, {\"name\": \"Tree-based sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0499\"}, {\"name\": \"Genome alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3182\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align molecular sequences using sequence and structural information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Structure-based sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0294\"}, \"name\": \"Structure-based sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0294\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence alignment (structure-based)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align molecular sequence(s) to sequence profile(s), or profiles to other profiles.  A profile typically represents a sequence alignment.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Sequence profile alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0300\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0300\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Profile-profile alignment\", \"Profile-to-profile alignment\", \"Sequence-profile alignment\", \"Sequence-to-profile alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align exactly two molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Pairwise sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0491\"}, \"name\": \"Pairwise sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Pairwise alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align more than two molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Multiple sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0492\"}, \"name\": \"Multiple sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Multiple alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Locally align two or more molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Local alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0495\"}, \"name\": \"Local alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0495\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Local sequence alignment\", \"Sequence alignment (local)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Smith-Waterman\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Globally align two or more molecular sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Global alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0496\"}, \"name\": \"Global alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0496\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Global sequence alignment\", \"Sequence alignment (global)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align multiple sequences using relative gap costs calculated from neighbors in a supplied phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Tree-based sequence alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_0499\"}, \"name\": \"Tree-based sequence alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0499\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Multiple sequence alignment (phylogenetic tree-based)\", \"Multiple sequence alignment construction (phylogenetic tree-based)\", \"Phylogenetic tree-based multiple sequence alignment construction\", \"Sequence alignment (phylogenetic tree-based)\", \"Sequence alignment generation (phylogenetic tree-based)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align two or more (tpyically huge) molecular sequences that represent genomes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Sequence alignment||Genome alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0292||operation_3182\"}, \"name\": \"Genome alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3182\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genome alignment construction\", \"Whole genome alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align (superimpose) molecular tertiary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0295\"}, \"name\": \"Structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0295\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structural alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"3D profile alignment\", \"3D profile-to-3D profile alignment\", \"Structural profile alignment\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Pairwise structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0503\"}, {\"name\": \"Multiple structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0504\"}, {\"name\": \"Local structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0509\"}, {\"name\": \"Global structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0510\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align (superimpose) exactly two molecular tertiary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Structure alignment||Pairwise structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0295||operation_0503\"}, \"name\": \"Pairwise structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0503\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structure alignment (pairwise)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Pairwise protein structure alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Align (superimpose) more than two molecular tertiary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Structure alignment||Multiple structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0295||operation_0504\"}, \"name\": \"Multiple structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0504\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structure alignment (multiple)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Multiple protein structure alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Locally align (superimpose) two or more molecular tertiary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Structure alignment||Local structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0295||operation_0509\"}, \"name\": \"Local structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0509\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structure alignment (local)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Local protein structure alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Globally align (superimpose) two or more molecular tertiary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Structure alignment||Global structure alignment\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0295||operation_0510\"}, \"name\": \"Global structure alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0510\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structure alignment (global)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Global protein structure alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Recognize (predict and identify) known protein structural domains or folds in protein sequence(s) which (typically) are not accompanied by any significant sequence similarity to know structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Fold recognition\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0303\"}, \"name\": \"Fold recognition\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Domain prediction\", \"Fold prediction\", \"Protein domain prediction\", \"Protein fold prediction\", \"Protein fold recognition\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Protein threading\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align molecular sequence to structure in 3D space (threading).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Fold recognition||Protein threading\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0303||operation_0302\"}, \"name\": \"Protein threading\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence-structure alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Sequence-3D profile alignment\", \"Sequence-to-3D-profile alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Link together a non-contiguous series of genomic sequences into a scaffold, consisting of sequences separated by gaps of known length.  The sequences that are linked are typically typically contigs; contiguous sequences corresponding to read overlaps.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Scaffolding\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3216\"}, \"name\": \"Scaffolding\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3216\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Scaffold construction\", \"Scaffold generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Scaffold gap completion\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3217\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Fill the gaps in a sequence assembly (scaffold) by merging in additional sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Scaffolding||Scaffold gap completion\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3216||operation_3217\"}, \"name\": \"Scaffold gap completion\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3217\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Generate a checksum of a molecular sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Sequence checksum generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3348\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence checksum generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3348\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Construct a bibliography from the scientific literature.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Bibliography generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3349\"}], \"name\": \"Bibliography generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3349\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Bibliography construction\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compute the covariance model for (a family of) RNA secondary structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||RNA structure covariance model generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3469\"}, \"name\": \"RNA structure covariance model generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3469\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Generate some data from a choosen probibalistic model, possibly to evaluate algorithms.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Probabilistic data generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3480\"}], \"name\": \"Probabilistic data generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3480\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Probabilistic sequence generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3481\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Generate sequences from some probabilistic model, e.g. a model that simulates evolution.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Probabilistic data generation||Probabilistic sequence generation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3480||operation_3481\"}, \"name\": \"Probabilistic sequence generation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3481\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Group together some data entities on the basis of similarities such that entities in the same group (cluster) are more similar to each other than to those in other groups (clusters).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432\"}], \"name\": \"Clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0291\"}, {\"name\": \"Expression profile clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0313\"}, {\"name\": \"Structure clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2844\"}, {\"name\": \"Document clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3279\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Build clusters of similar sequences, typically using scores from pair-wise alignment or other comparison of the sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering||Sequence clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432||operation_0291\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0291\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence cluster construction\", \"Sequence cluster generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Functional clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3459\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Clustering of molecular sequences on the basis of their function, typically using information from an ontology of gene function, or some other measure of functional phenotype.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering||Sequence clustering||Functional clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432||operation_0291||operation_3459\"}, \"name\": \"Functional clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3459\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Functional sequence clustering\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Perform cluster analysis of expression data to identify groups with similar expression profiles, for example by clustering.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering||Expression profile clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432||operation_0313\"}, \"name\": \"Expression profile clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0313\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression clustering\", \"Gene expression profile clustering\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Build clusters of similar structures, typically using scores from structural alignment methods.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering||Structure clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432||operation_2844\"}], \"name\": \"Structure clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_2844\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structural clustering\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Cluster (group) documents on the basis of their calculated similarity.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Clustering||Document clustering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3432||operation_3279\"}, \"name\": \"Document clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3279\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Convert a data set from one form to another.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Conversion\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3434\"}], \"name\": \"Conversion\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3434\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonym