y.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Sequencing quality control||Read pre-processing\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3218||operation_3219\"}, \"name\": \"Read pre-processing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3219\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence read pre-processing\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Variant filtering is used to eliminate false positive variants based for example on base calling quality, strand and position information, and mapping info.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Sequencing quality control||Variant filtering\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3218||operation_3675\"}, \"name\": \"Variant filtering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3675\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Estimate the frequencies of different species from analysis of the molecular sequences, typically of DNA recovered from environmental samples.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Species frequency estimation\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3221\"}], \"name\": \"Species frequency estimation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3221\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Detect, identify and map mutations, such as single nucleotide polymorphisms, short indels and structural variants, in multiple DNA sequences. Typically the alignment and comparison of the fluorescent traces produced by DNA sequencing hardware, to study genomic alterations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Variant calling\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3227\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227\"}], \"name\": \"Variant calling\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Variant mapping\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Allele calling\", \"Exome variant detection\", \"Genome variant detection\", \"Germ line variant calling\", \"Mutation detection\", \"Somatic variant calling\", \"de novo mutation detection\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0265\"}, {\"name\": \"Indel detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0452\"}, {\"name\": \"SNP detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Detect frameshifts in DNA sequences, including frameshift sites and signals, and frameshift errors from sequencing projects.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Variant calling||Frameshift detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3227||operation_0265\"}, \"name\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0265\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Frameshift error detection\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Identify insertion, deletion and duplication events from a sequence alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Variant calling||Indel detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3227||operation_0452\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||Indel detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0452\"}], \"name\": \"Indel detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0452\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Indel discovery\", \"Sequence alignment analysis (indel detection)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Find single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) - single nucleotide change in base positions - between sequences. Typically done for sequences from a high-throughput sequencing experiment that differ from a reference genome and which might, especially by reference to population frequency or functional data, indicate a polymorphism.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Variant calling||SNP detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3227||operation_0484\"}, {\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||SNP detection\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0484\"}], \"name\": \"SNP detection\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"SNP calling\", \"SNP discovery\", \"Single nucleotide polymorphism detection\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Analyse DNA sequences in order to determine an individual\'s DNA characteristics, for example in criminal forensics, parentage testing and so on.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||DNA profiling\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_2403||operation_2478||operation_3894\"}], \"name\": \"DNA profiling\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3894\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"DNA fingerprinting\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Detects chimeric sequences (chimeras) from a sequence alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Operation||Analysis||Sequence analysis||Nucleic acid sequence analysis||Genome analysis\", \"key\": \"operation_