ant sequence similarity to know structures.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Fold recognition\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0303\"}, \"name\": \"Fold recognition\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0303\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Domain prediction\", \"Fold prediction\", \"Protein domain prediction\", \"Protein fold prediction\", \"Protein fold recognition\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Protein threading\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Align molecular sequence to structure in 3D space (threading).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Alignment||Fold recognition||Protein threading\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_2928||operation_0303||operation_0302\"}, \"name\": \"Protein threading\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence-structure alignment\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Sequence-3D profile alignment\", \"Sequence-to-3D-profile alignment\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Link together a non-contiguous series of genomic sequences into a scaffold, consisting of sequences separated by gaps of known length.  The sequences that are linked are typically typically contigs; contiguous sequences corresponding to read overlaps.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Scaffolding\", \"key\": \"operation_0004||operation_3429||operation_3216\"}, \"name\": \"Scaffolding\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3216\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Scaffold construction\", \"Scaffold generation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Scaffold gap completion\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3217\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Fill the gaps in a sequence assembly (scaffold) by merging in additional sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Operation||Generation||Scaffolding||Scaffold gap completion\", \"key\": \"opera