fy differences between the genetic composition (genotype) of an individual compared to other individual\'s or a reference sequence.\", \"n\": \"Genotyping\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3196\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Multilocus sequence typing\", \"u\": \"operation_3840\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Genotyping\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3196\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Genotyping of multiple loci, typically characterizing microbial species isolates using internal fragments of multiple housekeeping genes.\", \"n\": \"Multilocus sequence typing\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3840\", \"es\": [\"MLST\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Genotyping||Multilocus sequence typing\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3196||operation_3840\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Classify variants based on their potential effect on genes, especially functional effects on the expressed proteins.\", \"n\": \"Variant classification\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3225\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant classification\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3225\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify biologically interesting variants by prioritizing individual variants, for example, homozygous variants absent in control genomes.\", \"n\": \"Variant prioritisation\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3226\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant prioritisation\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3226\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Detect, identify and map mutations, such as single nucleotide polymorphisms, short indels and structural variants, in multiple DNA sequences. Typically the alignment and comparison of the fluorescent traces produced by DNA sequencing hardware, to study genomic alterations.\", \"n\": \"Variant calling\", \"ns\": [\"Allele calling\", \"Exome variant detection\", \"Genome variant detection\", \"Germ line variant calling\", \"Mutation detection\", \"Somatic variant calling\", \"de novo mutation detection\"], \"u\": \"operation_3227\", \"es\": [\"Variant mapping\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"u\": \"operation_0265\"}, {\"n\": \"Indel detection\", \"u\": \"operation_0452\"}, {\"n\": \"SNP detection\", \"u\": \"operation_0484\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Detect frameshifts in DNA sequences, including frameshift sites and signals, and frameshift errors from sequencing projects.\", \"n\": \"Frameshift detection\", \"ns\": [\"Frameshift error detection\"], \"u\": \"operation_0265\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||Frameshift detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0265\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify insertion, deletion and duplication events from a sequence alignment.\", \"n\": \"Indel detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_0452\", \"es\": [\"Indel discovery\", \"Sequence alignment analysis (indel detection)\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||Indel detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0452\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Find single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) - single nucleotide change in base positions - between sequences. Typically done for sequences from a high-throughput sequencing experiment that differ from a reference genome and which might, especially by reference to population frequency or functional data, indicate a polymorphism.\", \"n\": \"SNP detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_0484\", \"es\": [\"SNP calling\", \"SNP discovery\", \"Single nucleotide polymorphism detection\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant calling||SNP detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3227||operation_0484\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Detect large regions in a genome subject to copy-number variation, or other structural variations in genome(s).\", \"n\": \"Structural variation detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3228\", \"es\": [\"Structural variation discovery\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Copy number variation detection\", \"u\": \"operation_3961\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify where sections of the genome are repeated and the number of repeats in the genome varies between individuals.\", \"n\": \"Copy number variation detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3961\", \"es\": [\"CNV detection\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Copy number estimation\", \"u\": \"operation_3233\"}, {\"n\": \"Deletion detection\", \"u\": \"operation_3962\"}, {\"n\": \"Duplication detection\", \"u\": \"operation_3963\"}, {\"n\": \"Complex CNV detection\", \"u\": \"operation_3964\"}, {\"n\": \"Amplification detection\", \"u\": \"operation_3965\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Estimate the number of copies of loci of particular gene(s) in DNA sequences typically from gene-expression profiling technology based on microarray hybridisation-based experiments. For example, estimate copy number (or marker dosage) of a dominant marker in samples from polyploid plant cells or tissues, or chromosomal gains and losses in tumors.\", \"n\": \"Copy number estimation\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3233\", \"es\": [\"Transcript copy number estimation\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Copy number estimation\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3233\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify deletion events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"n\": \"Deletion detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3962\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Deletion detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3962\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify duplication events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"n\": \"Duplication detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3963\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Duplication detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3963\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify copy number variations which are complex, e.g. multi-allelic variations that have many structural alleles and have rearranged multiple times in the ancestral genomes.\", \"n\": \"Complex CNV detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3964\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Complex CNV detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3964\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify amplification events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals.\", \"n\": \"Amplification detection\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3965\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Structural variation detection||Copy number variation detection||Amplification detection\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3228||operation_3961||operation_3965\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identify and map patterns of genomic variations.\", \"n\": \"Variant pattern analysis\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3504\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Variant pattern analysis\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3504\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Identification of the best reference for mapping for a specific dataset from a list of potential references, when performing genetic variation analysis.\", \"n\": \"Reference identification\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"operation_3703\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Operation||Analysis||Genetic variation analysis||Reference identification\", \"k\": \"operation_0004||operation_2945||operation_3197||operation_3703\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A method whereby data on several variants are \\\"collapsed\\\" into a single covariate based on regions such as genes.\", \"n\": \"Collapsing methods\", \"ns\": [], \"u\"