montology.org/data_3870\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Dynamic information of a structure molecular system coming from a molecular simulation: XYZ 3D coordinates (sometimes with their associated velocities) for every atom along time.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Forcefield parameters\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3871\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Force field parameters: charges, masses, radii, bond lengths, bond dihedrals, etc. define the structural molecular system, and are essential for the proper description and simulation of a molecular system.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Topology data\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3872\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Static information of a structure molecular system that is needed for a molecular simulation: the list of atoms, their non-bonded parameters for Van der Waals and electrostatic interactions, and the complete connectivity in terms of bonds, angles and dihedrals.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Data coming from molecular simulations, computer \\\"experiments\\\" on model molecules. Tipically formed by two separated but indivisible pieces of information: topology data (static) and trajectory data (dynamic).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}]}','2025-08-27 12:52:46.256511');
