rix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_2855||data_1546\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Molecular property||Protein property||Protein interaction data||Protein distance matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2087||data_0897||data_0906||data_1546\"}], \"name\": \"Protein distance matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1546\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Distances (values representing similarity) between a group of molecular structures.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Distance matrix||Structural distance matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_2855||data_2856\"}], \"name\": \"Structural distance matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2856\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The final processed (normalised) data for a set of hybridisations in a microarray experiment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Gene expression matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_3112\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Expression data||Gene expression matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2603||data_3112\"}], \"name\": \"Gene expression matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3112\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression data matrix\", \"Normalised microarray data\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A HMM transition matrix contains the probabilities of switching from one HMM state to another.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Transition matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_3354\"}], \"name\": \"Transition matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3354\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"HMM transition matrix\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A HMM emission matrix holds the probabilities of choosing the four nucleotides (A, C, G and T) in each of the states of a HMM.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Emission matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_3355\"}], \"name\": \"Emission matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3355\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"HMM emission matrix\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Multiple gene identifiers in a specific order.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Gene order\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_3479\"}], \"name\": \"Gene order\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3479\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A table of unnormalized values representing summarised read counts per genomic region (e.g. gene, transcript, peak).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Matrix||Count matrix\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2082||data_3917\"}], \"name\": \"Count matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3917\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Read count matrix\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A report on the physical (e.g. structural) or chemical properties of molecules, or parts of a molecule.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Molecular property\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2087\"}], \"name\": \"Molecular property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2087\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Physicochemical property\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Protein property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0897\"}, {\"name\": \"Nucleic acid property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0912\"}, {\"name\": \"Atomic property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1917\"}, {\"name\": \"Amino acid property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2016\"}, {\"name\": \"Molecular property (general)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2050\"}, {\"name\": \"Peptide property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2979\"}, {\"name\": \"Carbohydrate property\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3425\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"A report of primarily non-positional data describing intrinsic physical, chemical or other 