nd-user. Typically an EMBL or Swiss-Prot feature label.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features metadata||Sequence feature label\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2914||data_1022\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence feature label\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1022\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence feature name\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data (typically biological or biomedical) that has been rendered into an image, typically for display on screen.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Image\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2968\"}], \"name\": \"Image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2968\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Image data\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Heat map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1636\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1707\"}, {\"name\": \"RNA secondary structure image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1708\"}, {\"name\": \"Structure image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1710\"}, {\"name\": \"Sequence alignment image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1711\"}, {\"name\": \"Fate map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1713\"}, {\"name\": \"Sequence image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2969\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3153\"}, {\"name\": \"Raw image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3424\"}, {\"name\": \"Cell migration track image\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3449\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"A graphical 2D tabular representation of expression data, typically derived from an omics experiment. A heat map is a table where rows and columns correspond to different features and contexts (for example, cells or samples) and the cell colour represents the level of expression of a gene that context.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Data||Image||Heat map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2968||data_1636\"}, \"name\": \"Heat map\"