mous codon usage statistic plot\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The differences in codon usage fractions between two codon usage tables.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage fraction difference\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_1602\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage fraction difference\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1602\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A numerical measure of differences in the frequency of occurrence of synonymous codons in DNA sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage bias\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_2865\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage bias\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2865\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A biological model represented in mathematical terms.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950\"}], \"name\": \"Mathematical model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0950\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Biological model\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Dirichlet distribution\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1347\"}, {\"name\": \"Hidden Markov model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1364\"}, {\"name\": \"DNA substitution model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1439\"}, {\"name\": \"Kinetic model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3241\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Dirichlet distribution used by hidden Markov model analysis programs.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Dirichlet distribution\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1347\"}], \"name\": \"Dirichlet distribution\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1347\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A statistical Markov model of a system which is assumed to be a Markov process with unobserved (hidden) states.  For example, a hidden Markov model representation of a set or alignment of sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Hidden Markov model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1364\"}], \"name\": \"Hidden Markov model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1364\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"HMM\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Profile HMM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3949\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"A profile HMM is a variant of a Hidden Markov model that is derived specifically from a set of (aligned) biological sequences. Profile HMMs provide the basis for a position-specific scoring system, which can be used to align sequences and search databases for related sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Hidden Markov model||Profile HMM\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1364||data_3949\"}, \"name\": \"Profile HMM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3949\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A model of DNA substitution that explains a DNA sequence alignment, derived from phylogenetic tree analysis.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||DNA substitution model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1439\"}], \"name\": \"DNA substitution model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1439\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree report (DNA substitution model)\", \"Sequence alignment report (DNA substitution model)\", \"Substitution model\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Mathematical model of a network, that contains biochemical kinetics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Kinetic model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_3241\"}], \"name\": \"Kinetic model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3241\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An index of data of bio