ion data||Enzyme kinetics data\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2978||data_2024\"}], \"name\": \"Enzyme kinetics data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2024\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Vmax\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0909\"}, {\"name\": \"Km\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0910\"}, {\"name\": \"Michaelis Menten plot\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2025\"}, {\"name\": \"Hanes Woolf plot\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2026\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The maximum initial velocity or rate of a reaction. It is the limiting velocity as substrate concentrations get very large.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Molecular property||Protein property||Enzyme kinetics data||Vmax\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2087||data_0897||data_2024||data_0909\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Reaction data||Enzyme kinetics data||Vmax\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2978||data_2024||data_0909\"}], \"name\": \"Vmax\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0909\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Km is the concentration (usually in Molar units) of substrate that leads to half-maximal velocity of an enzyme-catalysed reaction.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Molecular property||Protein property||Enzyme kinetics data||Km\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2087||data_0897||data_2024||data_0910\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Reaction data||Enzyme kinetics data||Km\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2978||data_2024||data_0910\"}], \"name\": \"Km\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A plot giving an approximation of the kinetics of an enzyme-catalysed reaction, assuming simple kinetics (i.e. no intermediate or product inhibition, allostericity or cooperativity). It plots initial reaction rate to the substrate concentration (S) from which the maximum rate (vmax) is apparent.\