netic continuous quantitative data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1426\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative characters\", \"Quantitative traits\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylogenetic gene frequencies data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2873\"}]}, \"data_2873\": {\"definition\": \"Gene frequencies data that may be read during phylogenetic tree calculation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic character data||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative data||Phylogenetic gene frequencies data\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_0871||data_1426||data_2873\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic gene frequencies data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2873\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1427\": {\"definition\": \"Character data with discrete states that may be read during phylogenetic tree calculation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic character data||Phylogenetic discrete data\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_0871||data_1427\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic discrete data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1427\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Discrete characters\", \"Discretely coded characters\", \"Phylogenetic discrete states\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0872\": {\"definition\": \"The raw data (not just an image) from which a phylogenetic tree is directly generated or plotted, such as topology, lengths (in time or in expected amounts of variance) and a confidence interval for each length.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic tree\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_0872\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0872\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogeny\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Gene tree\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3271\"}, {\"name\": \"Species tree\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3272\"}]}, \"data_3271\": {\"definition\": \"A phylogenetic tree that is an estimate of the character\'s phylogeny.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic tree||Gene tree\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_0872||data_3271\"}], \"name\": \"Gene tree\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3271\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3272\": {\"definition\": \"A phylogenetic tree that reflects phylogeny of the taxa from which the characters (used in calculating the tree) were sampled.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic tree||Species tree\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_0872||data_3272\"}], \"name\": \"Species tree\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3272\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1428\": {\"definition\": \"One or more cliques of mutually compatible characters that are generated, for example from analysis of discrete character data, and are used to generate a phylogeny.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic character cliques\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_1428\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic character cliques\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1428\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic report (cliques)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1429\": {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic invariants data for testing alternative tree topologies.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Phylogenetic data||Phylogenetic invariants\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2523||data_1429\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic invariants\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1429\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic report (invariants)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1442\": {\"definition\": \"Distances, such as Branch Score distance, between two or more phylogenetic trees.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||