e bias plot\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1600\"}, {\"name\": \"Codon usage fraction difference\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1602\"}, {\"name\": \"Codon usage bias\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2865\"}]}, \"data_1597\": {\"definition\": \"Table of codon usage data calculated from one or more nucleic acid sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage table\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_1597\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage table\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1597\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1598\": {\"definition\": \"A genetic code for an organism.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Genetic code\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_1598\"}], \"name\": \"Genetic code\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1598\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1600\": {\"definition\": \"A plot of the synonymous codon usage calculated for windows over a nucleotide sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage bias plot\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_1600\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage bias plot\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1600\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Synonymous codon usage statistic plot\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1602\": {\"definition\": \"The differences in codon usage fractions between two codon usage tables.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage fraction difference\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_1602\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage fraction difference\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1602\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_2865\": {\"definition\": \"A numerical measure of differences in the frequency of occurrence of synonymous codons in DNA sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Codon usage data||Codon usage bias\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0914||data_2865\"}], \"name\": \"Codon usage bias\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2865\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0950\": {\"definition\": \"A biological model represented in mathematical terms.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950\"}], \"name\": \"Mathematical model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0950\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Biological model\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Dirichlet distribution\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1347\"}, {\"name\": \"Hidden Markov model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1364\"}, {\"name\": \"DNA substitution model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1439\"}, {\"name\": \"Kinetic model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3241\"}]}, \"data_1347\": {\"definition\": \"Dirichlet distribution used by hidden Markov model analysis programs.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Dirichlet distribution\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1347\"}], \"name\": \"Dirichlet distribution\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1347\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1364\": {\"definition\": \"A statistical Markov model of a system which is assumed to be a Markov process with unobserved (hidden) states.  For example, a hidden Markov model representation of a set or alignment of sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Hidden Markov model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1364\"}], \"name\": \"Hidden Markov model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1364\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"HMM\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Profile HMM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3949\"}]}, \"data_1439\": {\"definition\": \"A model of DNA substitution that explains a DNA sequence alignment, derived from phylogenetic tree analysis.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||DNA substitution model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_1439\"}], \"name\": \"DNA substitution model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1439\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phylogenetic tree report (DNA substitution model)\", \"Sequence alignment report (DNA substitution model)\", \"Substitution model\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3241\": {\"definition\": \"Mathematical model of a network, that contains biochemical kinetics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Mathematical model||Kinetic model\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0950||data_3241\"}], \"name\": \"Kinetic model\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3241\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0955\": {\"definition\": \"An index of data of biological relevance.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Data index\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0955\"}], \"name\": \"Data index\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0955\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Genome index\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3210\"}]}, \"data_3210\": {\"definition\": \"An index of a genome sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Data index||Genome index\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0955||data_3210\"}], \"name\": \"Genome index\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3210\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0968\": {\"definition\": \"Keyword(s) or phrase(s) used (typically) for text-searching purposes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Keyword\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0968\"}], \"name\": \"Keyword\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0968\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Phrases\", \"Term\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"UniProt keyword\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2007\"}]}, \"data_2007\": {\"definition\": \"A word or phrase that can appear in the keywords field (KW line) of entries from the UniProt database.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Keyword||UniProt keyword\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_0968||data_2007\"}], \"name\": \"UniProt keyword\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1255\": {\"definition\": \"Annotation of positional features of molecular sequence(s), i.e. that can be mapped to position(s) in the sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence features\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1255\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Feature record\", \"Features\", \"General sequence features\", \"Sequence features report\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Feature table\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1270\"}, {\"name\": \"Nucleic acid features\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1276\"}, {\"name\": \"Protein features\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1277\"}, {\"name\": \"Annotation track\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3002\"}]}, \"data_1270\": {\"definition\": \"Annotation of positional sequence features, organised into a standard feature table.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features||Feature table\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255||data_1270\"}], \"name\": \"Feature table\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1270\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Sequence feature table\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1276\": {\"definition\": \"An informative report on intrinsic positional features of a nucleotide sequence, formatted to be machine-readable.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features||Nucleic acid features\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255||data_1276\"}], \"name\": \"Nucleic acid features\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1276\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Feature table (nucleic acid)\", \"Nucleic acid feature table\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"Genome features\", \"Genomic features\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Gene transcript report\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3134\"}]}, \"data_3134\": {\"definition\": \"An informative report on features of a messenger RNA (mRNA) molecules including precursor RNA, primary (unprocessed) transcript and fully processed molecules. This includes reports on a specific gene transcript, clone or EST.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features||Nucleic acid features||Gene transcript report\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255||data_1276||data_3134\"}], \"name\": \"Gene transcript report\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3134\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Clone or EST (report)\", \"Gene transcript annotation\", \"Nucleic acid features (mRNA features)\", \"Transcript (report)\", \"mRNA (report)\", \"mRNA features\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1277\": {\"definition\": \"An informative report on intrinsic positional features of a protein sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features||Protein features\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255||data_1277\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Report||Protein report||Protein features\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2048||data_0896||data_1277\"}], \"name\": \"Protein features\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1277\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Feature table (protein)\", \"Protein feature table\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3002\": {\"definition\": \"Annotation of one particular positional feature on a biomolecular (typically genome) sequence, suitable for import and display in a genome browser.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Sequence features||Annotation track\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1255||data_3002\"}], \"name\": \"Annotation track\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3002\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genome annotation track\", \"Genome track\", \"Genome-browser track\", \"Genomic track\", \"Sequence annotation track\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1274\": {\"definition\": \"A map of (typically one) DNA sequence annotated with positional or non-positional features.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274\"}], \"name\": \"Map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1274\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"DNA map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Genetic map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1278\"}, {\"name\": \"Physical map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1280\"}]}, \"data_1278\": {\"definition\": \"A map showing the relative positions of genetic markers in a nucleic acid sequence, based on estimation of non-physical distance such as recombination frequencies.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Genetic map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1278\"}], \"name\": \"Genetic map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1278\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Linkage map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"DNA transduction map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1284\"}, {\"name\": \"QTL map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1860\"}, {\"name\": \"Haplotype map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1863\"}]}, \"data_1284\": {\"definition\": \"A gene map showing distances between loci based on relative cotransduction frequencies.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Genetic map||DNA transduction map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1278||data_1284\"}], \"name\": \"DNA transduction map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1284\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1860\": {\"definition\": \"A genetic map which shows the approximate location of quantitative trait loci (QTL) between two or more markers.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Genetic map||QTL map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1278||data_1860\"}], \"name\": \"QTL map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1860\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Quantitative trait locus map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1863\": {\"definition\": \"A map of haplotypes in a genome or other sequence, describing common patterns of genetic variation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Genetic map||Haplotype map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1278||data_1863\"}], \"name\": \"Haplotype map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1863\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1280\": {\"definition\": \"A map of DNA (linear or circular) annotated with physical features or landmarks such as restriction sites, cloned DNA fragments, genes or genetic markers, along with the physical distances between them.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280\"}], \"name\": \"Physical map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1280\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1279\"}, {\"name\": \"Cytogenetic map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1283\"}, {\"name\": \"Radiation hybrid map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2870\"}]}, \"data_1279\": {\"definition\": \"A map of genetic markers in a contiguous, assembled genomic sequence, with the sizes and separation of markers measured in base pairs.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Sequence map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1279\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1279\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Gene map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1285\"}, {\"name\": \"Plasmid map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1286\"}, {\"name\": \"Genome map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1288\"}, {\"name\": \"Restriction map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1289\"}]}, \"data_1285\": {\"definition\": \"Sequence map of a single gene annotated with genetic features such as introns, exons, untranslated regions, polyA signals, promoters, enhancers and (possibly) mutations defining alleles of a gene.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Sequence map||Gene map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1279||data_1285\"}], \"name\": \"Gene map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1285\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1286\": {\"definition\": \"Sequence map of a plasmid (circular DNA).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Sequence map||Plasmid map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1279||data_1286\"}], \"name\": \"Plasmid map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1286\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1288\": {\"definition\": \"Sequence map of a whole genome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Sequence map||Genome map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1279||data_1288\"}], \"name\": \"Genome map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1288\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1289\": {\"definition\": \"Image of the restriction enzyme cleavage sites (restriction sites) in a nucleic acid sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Sequence map||Restriction map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1279||data_1289\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Report||Sequence report||Sequence image||Restriction map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2048||data_2955||data_2969||data_1289\"}, {\"name\": \"Data||Image||Sequence image||Restriction map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_2968||data_2969||data_1289\"}], \"name\": \"Restriction map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1289\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1283\": {\"definition\": \"A map showing banding patterns derived from direct observation of a stained chromosome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Cytogenetic map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1283\"}], \"name\": \"Cytogenetic map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1283\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Chromosome map\", \"Cytogenic map\", \"Cytologic map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Deletion map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1859\"}]}, \"data_1859\": {\"definition\": \"A cytogenetic map showing chromosome banding patterns in mutant cell lines relative to the wild type.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Cytogenetic map||Deletion map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_1283||data_1859\"}], \"name\": \"Deletion map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1859\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Deletion-based cytogenetic map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_2870\": {\"definition\": \"A map showing distance between genetic markers estimated by radiation-induced breaks in a chromosome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Map||Physical map||Radiation hybrid map\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1274||data_1280||data_2870\"}], \"name\": \"Radiation hybrid map\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2870\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"RH map\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1352\": {\"definition\": \"Regular expression pattern.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Regular expression\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1352\"}], \"name\": \"Regular expression\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1352\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1772\": {\"definition\": \"A numerical value, that is some type of scored value arising for example from a prediction method.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772\"}], \"name\": \"Score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0865\"}, {\"name\": \"Structure similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0888\"}, {\"name\": \"Statistical estimate score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0951\"}, {\"name\": \"Alignment score or penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1394\"}, {\"name\": \"Localisation score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3756\"}]}, \"data_0865\": {\"definition\": \"A value representing molecular sequence similarity.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Sequence similarity score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0865\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0865\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence identity\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1412\"}, {\"name\": \"Sequence similarity\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1413\"}]}, \"data_1412\": {\"definition\": \"Sequence identity is the number (%) of matches (identical characters) in positions from an alignment of two molecular sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Sequence similarity score||Sequence identity\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0865||data_1412\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence identity\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1412\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1413\": {\"definition\": \"Sequence similarity is the similarity (expressed as a percentage) of two molecular sequences calculated from their alignment, a scoring matrix for scoring characters substitutions and penalties for gap insertion and extension.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Sequence similarity score||Sequence similarity\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0865||data_1413\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence similarity\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1413\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Bit score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2335\"}]}, \"data_2335\": {\"definition\": \"A score derived from the alignment of two sequences, which is then normalised with respect to the scoring system.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Sequence similarity score||Sequence similarity||Bit score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0865||data_1413||data_2335\"}], \"name\": \"Bit score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2335\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0888\": {\"definition\": \"A value representing molecular structure similarity, measured from structure alignment or some other type of structure comparison.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Structure similarity score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0888\"}], \"name\": \"Structure similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0888\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Root-mean-square deviation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1497\"}, {\"name\": \"Tanimoto similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1498\"}]}, \"data_1497\": {\"definition\": \"Root-mean-square deviation (RMSD) is calculated to measure the average distance between superimposed macromolecular coordinates.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Structure similarity score||Root-mean-square deviation\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0888||data_1497\"}], \"name\": \"Root-mean-square deviation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1497\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"RMSD\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1498\": {\"definition\": \"A measure of the similarity between two ligand fingerprints.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Structure similarity score||Tanimoto similarity score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0888||data_1498\"}], \"name\": \"Tanimoto similarity score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1498\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_0951\": {\"definition\": \"A value representing estimated statistical significance of some observed data; typically sequence database hits.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Statistical estimate score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0951\"}], \"name\": \"Statistical estimate score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_0951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"E-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1667\"}, {\"name\": \"Z-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1668\"}, {\"name\": \"P-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1669\"}, {\"name\": \"Q-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3932\"}]}, \"data_1667\": {\"definition\": \"A simple floating point number defining the lower or upper limit of an expectation value (E-value).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Statistical estimate score||E-value\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0951||data_1667\"}], \"name\": \"E-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1667\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Expectation value\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1668\": {\"definition\": \"The z-value is the number of standard deviations a data value is above or below a mean value.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Statistical estimate score||Z-value\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0951||data_1668\"}], \"name\": \"Z-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1668\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1669\": {\"definition\": \"The P-value is the probability of obtaining by random chance a result that is at least as extreme as an observed result, assuming a NULL hypothesis is true.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Statistical estimate score||P-value\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0951||data_1669\"}], \"name\": \"P-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1669\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3932\": {\"definition\": \"A score derived from the P-value to ensure correction for multiple tests. The Q-value provides an estimate of the positive False Discovery Rate (pFDR), i.e. the rate of false positives among all the cases reported positive: pFDR = FP / (FP + TP).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Statistical estimate score||Q-value\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_0951||data_3932\"}], \"name\": \"Q-value\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3932\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Adjusted P-value\", \"FDR\", \"Padj\", \"pFDR\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1394\": {\"definition\": \"A simple floating point number defining the penalty for opening or extending a gap in an alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment score or penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1394\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Match reward score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1401\"}, {\"name\": \"Mismatch penalty score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1402\"}, {\"name\": \"Drop off score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1403\"}, {\"name\": \"Gap penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2137\"}]}, \"data_1401\": {\"definition\": \"The score for a \'match\' used in various sequence database search applications with simple scoring schemes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Match reward score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_1401\"}], \"name\": \"Match reward score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1401\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1402\": {\"definition\": \"The score (penalty) for a \'mismatch\' used in various alignment and sequence database search applications with simple scoring schemes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Mismatch penalty score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_1402\"}], \"name\": \"Mismatch penalty score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1402\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1403\": {\"definition\": \"This is the threshold drop in score at which extension of word alignment is halted.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Drop off score\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_1403\"}], \"name\": \"Drop off score\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1403\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_2137\": {\"definition\": \"A penalty for introducing or extending a gap in an alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137\"}], \"name\": \"Gap penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_2137\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Gap opening penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1397\"}, {\"name\": \"Gap extension penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1398\"}, {\"name\": \"Gap separation penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1399\"}]}, \"data_1397\": {\"definition\": \"A penalty for opening a gap in an alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty||Gap opening penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137||data_1397\"}], \"name\": \"Gap opening penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1397\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Terminal gap opening penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1410\"}]}, \"data_1410\": {\"definition\": \"A number defining the penalty for opening gaps at the termini of an alignment, either from the N/C terminal of protein or 5\'/3\' terminal of nucleotide sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty||Gap opening penalty||Terminal gap opening penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137||data_1397||data_1410\"}], \"name\": \"Terminal gap opening penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1410\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1398\": {\"definition\": \"A penalty for extending a gap in an alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty||Gap extension penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137||data_1398\"}], \"name\": \"Gap extension penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1398\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Terminal gap extension penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1411\"}]}, \"data_1411\": {\"definition\": \"A number defining the penalty for extending gaps at the termini of an alignment, either from the N/C terminal of protein or 5\'/3\' terminal of nucleotide sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty||Gap extension penalty||Terminal gap extension penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137||data_1398||data_1411\"}], \"name\": \"Terminal gap extension penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1411\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_1399\": {\"definition\": \"A penalty for gaps that are close together in an alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Score||Alignment score or penalty||Gap penalty||Gap separation penalty\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_1772||data_1394||data_2137||data_1399\"}], \"name\": \"Gap separation penalty\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_1399\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3756\": {\"definition\": \"Score for localization of one or more post-translational modific