 coming from molecular simulations, computer \\\"experiments\\\" on model molecules.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Molecular simulation data\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_3842\"}], \"name\": \"Molecular simulation data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3842\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3869\": {\"definition\": \"Data coming from molecular simulations, computer \\\"experiments\\\" on model molecules. Tipically formed by two separated but indivisible pieces of information: topology data (static) and trajectory data (dynamic).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Simulation\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_3869\"}], \"name\": \"Simulation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3869\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Trajectory data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3870\"}, {\"name\": \"Forcefield parameters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3871\"}, {\"name\": \"Topology data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3872\"}]}, \"data_3870\": {\"definition\": \"Dynamic information of a structure molecular system coming from a molecular simulation: XYZ 3D coordinates (sometimes with their associated velocities) for every atom along time.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Simulation||Trajectory data\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_3869||data_3870\"}], \"name\": \"Trajectory data\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3870\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"data_3871\": {\"definition\": \"Force field parameters: charges, masses, radii, bond lengths, bond dihedrals, etc. define the structural molecular system, and are essential for the proper description and simulation of a molecular system.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Data||Simulation||Forcefield parameters\", \"key\": \"data_0006||data_3869||data_3871\"}], \"name\": \"Forcefield parameters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/data_3871\", \"exact_synonyms\": [],