tructure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"PSF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"RST\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"data\": {\"uri\":