own) and its lower-case \'masking\'.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BioYAML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BpForms\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\":