\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3789\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"XML Query\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"XQuery (XML Query) is a query language (format of queries) for querying and manipulating structured and unstructured data, usually in the form of XML, text, and with vendor-specific extensions for other data formats (JSON, binary, etc.).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"SPARQL\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3790\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"SPARQL (SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language) is a semantic query language for querying and manipulating data stored in Resource Description Framework (RDF) format.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GEN\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3812\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genotype file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The GEN file format contains genetic data and describes SNPs.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"SAMPLE file format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3813\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The SAMPLE file format contains information about each individual i.e. individual IDs, covariates, phenotypes and missing data proportions, from a GWAS study.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"SDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"SDF is one of a family of chemical-data file formats developed by MDL Information Systems; it is intended especially for structural information.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Molfile\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"An MDL Molfile is a file format for holding information about the atoms, bonds, connectivity and coordinates of a molecule.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Mol2\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Complete, portable representation of a SYBYL molecule. ASCII file which contains all the information needed to reconstruct a SYBYL molecule.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"latex\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3817\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"LaTeX format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"format for the LaTeX document preparation system\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"ELAND format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ELAND\", \"eland\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text file format used by Eland - the read-mapping program distributed by Illumina with its sequencing analysis pipeline - which maps short Solexa sequence reads to the human reference genome.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GML format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"GML (Graph Modeling Language) is a text file format supporting network data with a very easy syntax. It is used by Graphlet, Pajek, yEd, LEDA and NetworkX.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"FASTG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"FASTG assembly graph format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"FASTG is a format for faithfully representing genome assemblies in the face of allelic polymorphism and assembly uncertainty.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"proBED\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3827\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \". proBED is an adaptation of BED (format_3003), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GPR\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3829\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"GenePix Results (GPR) text file format developed by Axon Instruments that is used to save GenePix Results data.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"JCAMP-DX\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3859\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"A standardized file format for data exchange in mass spectrometry, initially developed for infrared spectrometry.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"XYZ\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"mdcrd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GROMACS top\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"AMBER top\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"PSF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"RST\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3888\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER frcmod (Force field Modification) is a file format to store any modification to the standard force field needed for a particular molecule to be properly represented in the simulation.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"AMBER off\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3889\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Object File Format\", \"AMBER lib\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"AMBER Object File Format library files (OFF library files) store residue libraries (forcefield residue parameters).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"NMReDATA\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3906\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"MReData is a text based data standard for processed NMR data. It is relying on SDF molecule data and allows to store assignments of NMR peaks to molecule features.  The NMR-extracted data (or \\\"NMReDATA\\\") includes: Chemical shift,scalar coupling, 2D correlation, assignment, etc.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BpForms\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"trr\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"MTX\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The Matrix Market matrix (MTX) format stores numerical or pattern matrices in a dense (array format) or sparse (coordinate format) representation.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BcForms\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"N-Quads\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3956\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. It includes information about the graph each triple belongs to.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"BNGL\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3972\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioNetGen Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"BioNetGen is a format for the specification and simulation of rule-based models of biochemical systems, including signal transduction, metabolic, and genetic regulatory networks.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GFA 1\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3975\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"GFA 2\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3976\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"CONTIG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3978\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The CONTIG format used for output of the SOAPdenovo alignment program. It contains contig sequences generated without using mate pair information.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"CHAIN\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3982\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The CHAIN format describes a pairwise alignment that allow gaps in both sequences simultaneously and is used by the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"NET\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3983\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"The NET file format is used to describe the data that underlie the net alignment annotations in the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"QMAP\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3984\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format of QMAP files generated for methylation data from an internal BGI pipeline.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"gxformat2\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3985\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Galaxy workflow format\", \"GalaxyWF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"An emerging format for high-level Galaxy workflow description.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"CIGAR format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3992\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"CIGAR\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Compact Idiosyncratic Gapped Alignment Report format is a compressed (run-length encoded) pairwise alignment format. It is useful for representing long (e.g. genomic) pairwise alignments.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Python script\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3996\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Python\", \"Python program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format for scripts writtenin Python - a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Perl script\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3998\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Perl\", \"Perl program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format for scripts written in Perl - a family of high-level, general-purpose, interpreted, dynamic programming languages.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"R script\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3999\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"R\", \"R program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format for scripts written in the R language - an open source programming language and software environment for statistical computing and graphics that is supported by the R Foundation for Statistical Computing.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"R markdown\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4000\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"A file format for making dynamic documents (R Markdown scripts) with the R language.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"Configuration file format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4005\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"A configuration file used by various programs to store settings that are specific to their respective software.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"MATLAB script\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4007\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MATLAB\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definitio