 to efficiently hold large omics datasets. Typically, such data takes the form of a large matrix of numbers, along with metadata for the rows and columns.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"h5\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"HDF5 is a data model, library, and file format for storing and managing data, based on Hierarchical Data Format (HDF).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"netCDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3650\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ANDI-MS\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"HDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3873\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"HDF is the name of a set of file formats and libraries designed to store and organize large amounts of numerical data, originally developed at the National Center for Supercomputing Applications at the University of Illinois.\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"PCAzip\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3874\"}, \"children\": [], \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"replaced_by\": [], \"consider\": [], \"definition\": \"PCAZip format is a binary compressed file to store atom coordinates based on Essential Dynamics (ED) and Principal Component Analysis (PCA).\", \"has_input\": [], \"has_output\": [], \"has_topic\": []}, {\"text\": \"XTC\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3875\"}, \"c