_3655\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||pepXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3655\"}], \"name\": \"pepXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3655\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Pathway Markup Language (GPML) is an XML format used for exchanging biological pathways.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||GPML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3657\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GPML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3657\"}], \"name\": \"GPML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3657\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"imzML metadata is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging metadata.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||imzML metadata file\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3682\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||imzML metadata file\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3682\"}], \"name\": \"imzML metadata file\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3682\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||qcML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3683\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||qcML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3683\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||qcML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3683\"}], \"name\": \"qcML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3683\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||PRIDE XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3684\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||PRIDE XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3684\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||PRIDE XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3684\"}], \"name\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3684\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Simulation Experiment Description Markup Language (SED-ML) is an XML format for encoding simulation setups, according to the MIASE (Minimum Information About a Simulation Experiment) requirements.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||SED-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3685\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||SED-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3685\"}], \"name\": \"SED-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3685\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Biological Connection Markup Language (BCML) is an XML format for biological pathways.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||BCML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3689\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BCML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3689\"}], \"name\": \"BCML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3689\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Biological Dynamics Markup Language (BDML) is an XML format for quantitative data describing biological dynamics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||BDML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3690\"}], \"name\": \"BDML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3690\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBGN-ML is an XML format for Systems Biology Graphical Notation (SBGN) diagrams of biological pathways or networks.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3692\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3692\"}], \"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Output format used by X! series search engines that is based on the XML language BIOML.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||X!Tandem XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3711\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||X!Tandem XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3711\"}], \"name\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3711\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Synthetic Biology Open Language (SBOL) is an XML format for the specification and exchange of biological design information in synthetic biology.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||SBOL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3725\"}], \"name\": \"SBOL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3725\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PMML uses XML to represent mining models. The structure of the models is described by an XML Schema.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||PMML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3726\"}], \"name\": \"PMML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3726\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A format for storage, exchange, and processing of protein identifications created from ms/ms-derived peptide sequence data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||protXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3747\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||protXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3747\"}], \"name\": \"protXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3747\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML file format for files containing information about peptide identifications from mass spectrometry data analysis carried out with OpenMS.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||idXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3764\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||idXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3764\"}], \"name\": \"idXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3764\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"UniProtKB XML sequence features format is an XML format available for downloading UniProt entries.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||UniProtKB XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3770\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence record format||uniprotkb-like format||UniProtKB XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1919||format_2547||format_3770\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence record format||Sequence record format (XML)||UniProtKB XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1919||format_2552||format_3770\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||uniprotkb-like format||UniProtKB XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2