rot-like (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2187\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"UniProtKB format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1963\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"UniProtKB entry sequence format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||uniprotkb-like format||UniProt-like (text)||UniProtKB format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_2547||format_2187||format_1963\"}, \"name\": \"UniProtKB format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1963\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"SwissProt format\", \"UniProt format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"UniProtKB XML sequence features format is an XML format available for downloading UniProt entries.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||uniprotkb-like format||UniProtKB XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_2547||format_3770\"}, \"name\": \"UniProtKB XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3770\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"UniProt XML\", \"UniProt XML format\", \"UniProtKB XML format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"UniProtKB RDF sequence features format is an RDF format available for downloading UniProt entries (in RDF/XML).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||uniprotkb-like format||UniProtKB RDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_2547||format_3771\"}, \"name\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3771\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"UniProt RDF\", \"UniProt RDF format\", \"UniProtKB RDF format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"UniProt RDF/XML\", \"UniProt RDF/XML format\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML format\"], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for a sequence feature table.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||Sequence feature table format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_2553\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence feature table format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2553\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"DASGFF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1978\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"DAS GFF (XML) feature format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||Sequence feature table format (XML)||DASGFF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_2553||format_1978\"}, \"name\": \"DASGFF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1978\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"DASGFF feature\", \"das feature\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BTrack is an HDF5-based binary format for genome or sequence feature tracks and their collections, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. BTrack is a binary, compressed alternative to the GTrack and GSuite formats.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence feature table format||BTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2548||format_3776\"}, \"name\": \"BTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3776\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BTrack (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"BTrack format\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BTrack\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite BTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack BTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a sequence annotation track.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence annotation track format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2919\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3003\"}, {\"name\": \"bigBed\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3004\"}, {\"name\": \"WIG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3005\"}, {\"name\": \"bigWig\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3006\"}, {\"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\"}, {\"name\": \"MAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3008\"}, {\"name\": \"genePred\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3011\"}, {\"name\": \"pgSnp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3012\"}, {\"name\": \"GTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3164\"}, {\"name\": \"bedgraph\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3583\"}, {\"name\": \"customtrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3588\"}, {\"name\": \"BTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3776\"}, {\"name\": \"GEN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3812\"}, {\"name\": \"proBED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3827\"}, {\"name\": \"TrackDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3991\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Browser Extensible Data (BED) format of sequence annotation track, typically to be displayed in a genome browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003\"}, \"name\": \"BED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3003\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"bedstrict\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3584\"}, {\"name\": \"chrominfo\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3587\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Browser Extensible Data (BED) format of sequence annotation track that strictly does not contain non-standard fields beyond the first 3 columns.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584\"}, \"name\": \"bedstrict\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3584\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"bed6\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3585\"}, {\"name\": \"bed12\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3586\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"BED file format where each feature is described by chromosome, start, end, name, score, and strand.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict||bed6\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584||format_3585\"}, \"name\": \"bed6\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3585\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ENCODE peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3612\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Human ENCODE peak format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict||bed6||ENCODE peak format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584||format_3585||format_3612\"}, \"name\": \"ENCODE peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3612\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ENCODE narrow peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3613\"}, {\"name\": \"ENCODE broad peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3614\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Human ENCODE narrow peak format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict||bed6||ENCODE peak format||ENCODE narrow peak format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584||format_3585||format_3612||format_3613\"}, \"name\": \"ENCODE narrow peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3613\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Human ENCODE broad peak format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict||bed6||ENCODE peak format||ENCODE broad peak format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584||format_3585||format_3612||format_3614\"}, \"name\": \"ENCODE broad peak format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3614\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A BED file where each feature is described by all twelve columns.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||bedstrict||bed12\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3584||format_3586\"}, \"name\": \"bed12\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3586\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tabular format of chromosome names and sizes used by Galaxy.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BED||chrominfo\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3003||format_3587\"}, \"name\": \"chrominfo\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3587\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"bigBed format for large sequence annotation tracks, similar to textual BED format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bigBed\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3004\"}, \"name\": \"bigBed\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3004\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Wiggle format (WIG) of a sequence annotation track that consists of a value for each sequence position. Typically to be displayed in a genome browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||WIG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3005\"}, \"name\": \"WIG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3005\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"bigWig format for large sequence annotation tracks that consist of a value for each sequence position. Similar to textual WIG format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bigWig\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3006\"}, \"name\": \"bigWig\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3006\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PSL format of alignments, typically generated by BLAT or psLayout. Can be displayed in a genome browser like a sequence annotation track.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||PSL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3007\"}, \"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Multiple Alignment Format (MAF) supporting alignments of whole genomes with rearrangements, directions, multiple pieces to the alignment, and so forth.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||MAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3008\"}, \"name\": \"MAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3008\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"genePred table format for gene prediction tracks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||genePred\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3011\"}, \"name\": \"genePred\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3011\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Personal Genome SNP (pgSnp) format for sequence variation tracks (indels and polymorphisms), supported by the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||pgSnp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3012\"}, \"name\": \"pgSnp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3012\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GTrack is a generic and optimised tabular format for genome or sequence feature tracks. GTrack unifies the power of other track formats (e.g. GFF3, BED, WIG), and while optimised in size, adds more flexibility, customisation, and automation (\\\"machine understandability\\\").\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||GTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3164\"}, \"name\": \"GTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3164\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD/GTrack GTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack GTrack\", \"GTrack format\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite GTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack GTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The bedGraph format allows display of continuous-valued data in track format. This display type is useful for probability scores and transcriptome data\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bedgraph\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3583\"}, \"name\": \"bedgraph\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3583\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Custom Sequence annotation track format used by Galaxy.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||customtrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3588\"}, \"name\": \"customtrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3588\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BTrack is an HDF5-based binary format for genome or sequence feature tracks and their collections, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. BTrack is a binary, compressed alternative to the GTrack and GSuite formats.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3776\"}, \"name\": \"BTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3776\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BTrack (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"BTrack format\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BTrack\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite BTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack BTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The GEN file format contains genetic data and describes SNPs.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||GEN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3812\"}, \"name\": \"GEN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3812\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genotype file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \". proBED is an adaptation of BED (format_3003), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||proBED\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3827\"}, \"name\": \"proBED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3827\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A declaration file format for UCSC browsers track dataset display charateristics.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||TrackDB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3991\"}, \"name\": \"TrackDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3991\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3772\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioYAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3773\"}, \"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||JSON||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3774\"}, {\