": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_2924||format_3820\"}, \"name\": \"Relaxed PHYLIP Sequential\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3820\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Relaxed PHYLIP non-interleaved\", \"Relaxed PHYLIP non-interleaved format\", \"Relaxed PHYLIP sequential format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Multiple Alignment Format (MAF) supporting alignments of whole genomes with rearrangements, directions, multiple pieces to the alignment, and so forth.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||MAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3008\"}, \"name\": \"MAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3008\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The A2M format is used as the primary format for multiple alignments of protein or nucleic-acid sequences in the SAM suite of tools. It is a small modification of FASTA format for sequences and is compatible with most tools that read FASTA.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||A2M\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3281\"}, \"name\": \"A2M\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3281\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A multiple alignment in vertical format, as used in the AMPS (Alignment of Multiple Protein Sequences) pacakge.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||BLC\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3313\"}], \"name\": \"BLC\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3313\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Block file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"EMBOSS simple sequence pair alignment format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||PO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3330\"}], \"name\": \"PO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3330\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Some format based on the GCG format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486\"}, \"name\": \"GCG format variant\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3486\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"GCG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1935\"}, {\"name\": \"GCG MSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1947\"}, {\"name\": \"RSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3485\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"GCG sequence file format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||GCG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_1935\"}, \"name\": \"GCG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1935\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCG SSF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GCG MSF (multiple sequence file) file format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||GCG MSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_1947\"}, \"name\": \"GCG MSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1947\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Rich sequence format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||RSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_3485\"}, \"name\": \"RSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3485\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCG RSF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Color space FASTA format sequence variant.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||csfasta\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3589\"}, \"name\": \"csfasta\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3589\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The A2M format is used as the primary format for multiple alignments of protein or nucleic-acid sequences in the SAM suite of tools. It is a small modification of FASTA format for sequences and is compatible with most tools that read FASTA.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||XMFA\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3811\"}, \"name\": \"XMFA\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3811\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"alignment format\", \"eXtended Multi-FastA format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for molecular sequence alignment information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2555\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BioXSD (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2352\"}, {\"name\": \"HSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3845\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"BioXSD-schema-based XML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, Web services, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)||BioXSD (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555||format_2352\"}, \"name\": \"BioXSD (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2352\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD XML\", \"BioXSD XML format\", \"BioXSD in XML\", \"BioXSD in XML format\", \"BioXSD+XML\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An alignment format generated by PRANK/PRANKSTER consisting of four elements: newick, nodes, selection and model.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)||HSAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555||format_3845\"}, \"name\": \"HSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3845\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for molecular sequence alignment information that can hold sequence alignment(s) of only 2 sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment format (pair only)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2920\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"srspair\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2003\"}, {\"name\": \"BAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2572\"}, {\"name\": \"SAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2573\"}, {\"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\"}, {\"name\": \"axt\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3013\"}, {\"name\": \"LAV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3014\"}, {\"name\": \"Pileup\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3015\"}, {\"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\"}, {\"name\": \"CRAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3462\"}, {\"name\": \"proBAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3826\"}, {\"name\": \"CHAIN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3982\"}, {\"name\": \"CIGAR format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3992\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Simple sequence pair (alignment) format for SRS.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||srspair\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2003\"}, \"name\": \"srspair\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2003\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BAM format, the binary, BGZF-formatted compressed version of SAM format for alignment of nucleotide sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). May contain base-call and alignment qualities and other data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||BAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2572\"}, \"name\": \"BAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2572\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Sequence Alignment/Map (SAM) format for alignment of nucleotide sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). May contain base-call and alignment qualities and other data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||SAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2573\"}, \"name\": \"SAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2573\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PSL format of alignments, typically generated by BLAT or psLayout. Can be displayed in a genome browser like a sequence annotation track.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||PSL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3007\"}, \"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"axt format of alignments, typically produced from BLASTZ.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||axt\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3013\"}, \"name\": \"axt\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3013\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"LAV format of alignments generated by BLASTZ and LASTZ.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||LAV\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3014\"}, \"name\": \"LAV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3014\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Pileup format of alignment of sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). Contains aligned bases per base of the reference sequence(s).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||Pileup\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3015\"}, \"name\": \"Pileup\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3015\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"EBI Application Result XML is a format returned by sequence similarity search Web services at EBI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||EBI Application Result XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3157\"}, \"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Reference-based compression of alignment format\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CRAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3462\"}, \"name\": \"CRAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3462\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \". proBAM is an adaptation of BAM (format_2572), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||proBAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3826\"}, \"name\": \"proBAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3826\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The CHAIN format describes a pairwise alignment that allow gaps in both sequences simultaneously and is used by the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CHAIN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3982\"}, \"name\": \"CHAIN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3982\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compact Idiosyncratic Gapped Alignment Report format is a compressed (run-length encoded) pairwise alignment format. It is useful for representing long (e.g. genomic) pairwise alignments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CIGAR format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3992\"}, \"name\": \"CIGAR format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3992\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"CIGAR\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"RNA Markup Language.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||RNAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3311\"}, \"name\": \"RNAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3311\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3772\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioYAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3773\"}, \"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3774\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3774\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Binary format used by the ARB software suite\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||ARB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3830\"}, \"name\": \"ARB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3830\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ARB binary format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A set of XML compliant markup components for describing multiple sequence alignments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||MSAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3849\"}, \"name\": \"MSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3849\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2006\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2556\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2557\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Text format for a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2556\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ClustalW dendrogram\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1424\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylip tree raw\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1425\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylip tree format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1435\"}, {\"name\": \"TreeBASE format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1436\"}, {\"name\": \"TreeFam format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1437\"}, {\"name\": \"newick\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1910\"}, {\"name\": \"TreeCon format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1911\"}, {\"name\": \"Nexus format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1912\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Dendrogram (tree file) format generated by ClustalW.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||ClustalW dendrogram\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1424\"}, \"name\": \"ClustalW dendrogram\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1424\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Raw data file format used by Phylip from which a phylogenetic tree is directly generated or plotted.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Phylip tree raw\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1425\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree raw\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1425\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree data format used by the PHYLIP program.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Phylip tree format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1435\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1435\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the TreeBASE database of phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeBASE format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1436\"}, \"name\": \"TreeBASE format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1436\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the TreeFam database of phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeFam format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1437\"}, \"name\": \"TreeFam format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1437\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree Newick (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||newick\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1910\"}, \"name\": \"newick\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"nh\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree TreeCon (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeCon format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1911\"}, \"name\": \"TreeCon format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1911\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree Nexus (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Nexus format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1912\"}, \"name\": \"Nexus format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1912\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2557\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"phyloXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3159\"}, {\"name\": \"NeXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3160\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"phyloXML is a standardised XML format for phylogenetic trees, networks, and associated data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)||phyloXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557||format_3159\"}, \"name\": \"phyloXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3159\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"NeXML is a standardised XML format for rich phyloinformatic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)||NeXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557||format_3160\"}, \"name\": \"NeXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3160\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a biological pathway or network.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013\"}], \"name\": \"Biological pathway or network format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2013\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"SBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2585\"}, {\"name\": \"BioPAX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3156\"}, {\"name\": \"CopasiML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3239\"}, {\"name\": \"CellML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3240\"}, {\"name\": \"sif\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3619\"}, {\"name\": \"GPML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3657\"}, {\"name\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3686\"}, {\"name\": \"SBtab\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3688\"}, {\"name\": \"BCML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3689\"}, {\"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\"}, {\"name\": \"VisML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3821\"}, {\"name\": \"GML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\"}, {\"name\": \"KGML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3847\"}, {\"name\": \"NeuroML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3971\"}, {\"name\": \"BNGL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3972\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Systems Biology Markup Language (SBML), the standard XML format for models of biological processes such as for example metabolism, cell signaling, and gene regulation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_2585\"}, \"name\": \"SBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2585\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioPAX is an exchange format for pathway data, with its data model defined in OWL.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BioPAX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3156\"}], \"name\": \"BioPAX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3156\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CopasiML, the native format of COPASI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||CopasiML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3239\"}, \"name\": \"CopasiML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3239\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CellML, the format for mathematical models of biological and other networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||CellML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3240\"}, \"name\": \"CellML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3240\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SIF (simple interaction file) Format - a network/pathway format used for instance in cytoscape.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||sif\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3619\"}], \"name\": \"sif\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3619\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Pathway Markup Language (GPML) is an XML format used for exchanging biological pathways.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GPML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3657\"}, \"name\": \"GPML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3657\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Open Modeling EXchange format (OMEX) is a ZIPped format for encapsulating all information necessary for a modeling and simulation project in systems biology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||COMBINE OMEX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3686\"}, \"name\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3686\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBtab is a tabular format for biochemical network models.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBtab\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3688\"}, \"name\": \"SBtab\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3688\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Biological Connection Markup Language (BCML) is an XML format for biological pathways.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BCML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3689\"}, \"name\": \"BCML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3689\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBGN-ML is an XML format for Systems Biology Graphical Notation (SBGN) diagrams of biological pathways or networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3692\"}, \"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Default XML format of VisANT, containing all the network information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||VisML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3821\"}, \"name\": \"VisML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3821\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"VisANT xml\", \"VisANT xml format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GML (Graph Modeling Language) is a text file format supporting network data with a very easy syntax. It is used by Graphlet, Pajek, yEd, LEDA and NetworkX.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3822\"}, \"name\": \"GML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GML format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The KEGG Markup Language (KGML) is an exchange format of the KEGG pathway maps, which is converted from internally used KGML+ (KGML+SVG) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||KGML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3847\"}, \"name\": \"KGML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3847\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"KEGG Markup Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A model description language for computational neuroscience.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||NeuroML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3971\"}, \"name\": \"NeuroML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3971\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioNetGen is a format for the specification and simulation of rule-based models of biochemical systems, including signal transduction, metabolic, and genetic regulatory networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BNGL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3972\"}, \"name\": \"BNGL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3972\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioNetGen Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a sequence-profile alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence-profile alignment format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2014\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1419\"}, {\"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1421\"}, {\"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1422\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format for alignment of molecular sequences to MEME profiles (position-dependent scoring matrices) as generated by the MAST tool from the MEME package.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1419\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1419\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format used by the HMMER package for an alignment of a sequence against a hidden Markov model database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1421\"}, \"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1421\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format used by the HMMER package for of an alignment of a hidden Markov model against a sequence database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1422\"}, \"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1422\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a full-text scientific article.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020\"}], \"name\": \"Article format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2020\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Literature format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"pmc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1739\"}, {\"name\": \"medline\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2194\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Article format of the PubMed Central database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format||pmc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020||format_1739\"}, \"name\": \"pmc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1739\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Abstract format used by MedLine database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format||medline\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020||format_2194\"}, \"name\": \"medline\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2194\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format of a report from text mining.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Text mining report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2021\"}], \"name\": \"Text mining report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2021\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"iHOP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1740\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The format of iHOP (Information Hyperlinked over Proteins) text-mining result.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Text mining report format||iHOP format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2021||format_1740\"}, \"name\": \"iHOP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1740\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for reports on enzyme kinetics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Enzyme kinetics report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2027\"}], \"name\": \"Enzyme kinetics report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2027\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"findkm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1582\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"A report format for the kinetics of enzyme-catalysed reaction(s) in a format generated by EMBOSS findkm. This includes Michaelis Menten plot, Hanes Woolf plot, Michaelis Menten constant (Km) and maximum velocity (Vmax).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Enzyme kinetics report format||findkm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2027||format_1582\"}, \"name\": \"findkm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1582\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on a chemical compound.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030\"}], \"name\": \"Chemical data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2030\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Chemical compound annotation format\", \"Chemical structure format\", \"Small molecule report format\", \"Small molecule structure format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"HET group dictionary entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1705\"}, {\"name\": \"SDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\"}, {\"name\": \"Molfile\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\"}, {\"name\": \"Mol2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\"}, {\"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the HET group dictionary (HET groups from PDB files).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||HET group dictionary entry format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_1705\"}, \"name\": \"HET group dictionary entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1705\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SDF is one of a family of chemical-data file formats developed by MDL Information Systems; it is intended especially for structural information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||SDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3814\"}, \"name\": \"SDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An MDL Molfile is a file format for holding information about the atoms, bonds, connectivity and coordinates of a molecule.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Molfile\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3815\"}, \"name\": \"Molfile\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Complete, portable representation of a SYBYL molecule. ASCII file which contains all the information needed to reconstruct a SYBYL molecule.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Mol2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3816\"}, \"name\": \"Mol2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3951\"}, \"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on a particular locus, gene, gene system or groups of genes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031\"}], \"name\": \"Gene annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2031\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene features format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"est2genome format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1316\"}, {\"name\": \"OrthoXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3850\"}, {\"name\": \"WEGO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3979\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on exon-intron structure generated by EMBOSS est2genome.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||est2genome format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_1316\"}, \"name\": \"est2genome format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1316\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"OrthoXML is designed broadly to allow the storage and comparison of orthology data from any ortholog database. It establishes a structure for describing orthology relationships while still allowing flexibility for database-specific information to be encapsulated in the same format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||OrthoXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_3850\"}, \"name\": \"OrthoXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3850\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"WEGO native format used by the Web Gene Ontology Annotation Plot application.   Tab-delimited format with gene names and others GO IDs (columns) with one annotation record per line.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||WEGO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_3979\"}, \"name\": \"WEGO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3979\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a workflow.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032\"}], \"name\": \"Workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2032\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Taverna workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1665\"}, {\"name\": \"KNIME datatable format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3765\"}, {\"name\": \"CWL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3857\"}, {\"name\": \"gxformat2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3985\"}, {\"name\": \"Python script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3996\"}, {\"name\": \"Perl script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3998\"}, {\"name\": \"R script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3999\"}, {\"name\": \"R markdown\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4000\"}, {\"name\": \"MATLAB script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4007\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Taverna workflows.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||Taverna workflow format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_1665\"}, \"name\": \"Taverna workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1665\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data table formatted such that it can be passed/streamed within the KNIME platform.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||KNIME datatable format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3765\"}], \"name\": \"KNIME datatable format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3765\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Common Workflow Language (CWL) format for description of command-line tools and workflows.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||CWL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3857\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||CWL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3857\"}], \"name\": \"CWL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3857\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Common Workflow Language\", \"CommonWL\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An emerging format for high-level Galaxy workflow description.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||gxformat2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3985\"}, \"name\": \"gxformat2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3985\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Galaxy workflow format\", \"GalaxyWF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for scripts writtenin Python - a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||Python script\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3996\"}, \"name\": \"Python script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3996\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Python\", \"Python program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for scripts written in Perl - a family of high-level, general-purpose, interpreted, dynamic programming languages.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||Perl script\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3998\"}, \"name\": \"Perl script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3998\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Perl\", \"Perl program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for scripts written in the R language - an open source programming language and software environment for statistical computing and graphics that is supported by the R Foundation for Statistical Computing.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||R script\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3999\"}, \"name\": \"R script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3999\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"R\", \"R program\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A file format for making dynamic documents (R Markdown scripts) with the R language.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||R markdown\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_4000\"}, \"name\": \"R markdown\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4000\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The file format for MATLAB scripts or functions.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||MATLAB script\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_4007\"}, \"name\": \"MATLAB script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MATLAB\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a molecular tertiary structure.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033\"}], \"name\": \"Tertiary structure format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2033\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PDB database entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1475\"}, {\"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\"}, {\"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\"}, {\"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\"}, {\"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\"}, {\"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\"}, {\"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\"}, {\"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\"}, {\"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of an entry (or part of an entry) from the PDB database.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475\"}], \"name\": \"PDB database entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1475\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PDB entry format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1476\"}, {\"name\": \"mmCIF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1477\"}, {\"name\": \"PDBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1478\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbatom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1950\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbatomnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1951\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbseqresnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1952\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbseqres\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1953\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in PDB format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||PDB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1476\"}, \"name\": \"PDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1476\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PDB format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in mmCIF format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||mmCIF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1477\"}, \"name\": \"mmCIF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1477\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in PDBML (XML) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||PDBML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1478\"}, \"name\": \"PDBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1478\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB sequence format (ATOM lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbatom\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1950\"}, \"name\": \"pdbatom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1950\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB nucleotide sequence format (ATOM lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbatomnuc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1951\"}, \"name\": \"pdbatomnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB nucleotide sequence format (SEQRES lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbseqresnuc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1952\"}, \"name\": \"pdbseqresnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1952\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB sequence format (SEQRES lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbseqres\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1953\"}, \"name\": \"pdbseqres\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1953\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||XYZ\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3877\"}, \"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||mdcrd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3878\"}, \"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3880\"}, \"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||AMBER top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3881\"}, \"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3882\"}, \"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3883\"}, \"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||RST\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3886\"}, \"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||CHARMM rtf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3887\"}, \"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||trr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3910\"}, \"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Text format of a chemical formula.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035\"}], \"name\": \"Chemical formula format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2035\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"SMILES\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1196\"}, {\"name\": \"InChI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1197\"}, {\"name\": \"mf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1198\"}, {\"name\": \"InChIKey\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1199\"}, {\"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified in Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System (SMILES) line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||SMILES\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1196\"}, \"name\": \"SMILES\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1196\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"smarts\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1200\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"SMILES ARbitrary Target Specification (SMARTS) format for chemical structure specification, which is a subset of the SMILES line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||SMILES||smarts\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1196||format_1200\"}, \"name\": \"smarts\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1200\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified in IUPAC International Chemical Identifier (InChI) line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||InChI\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1197\"}, \"name\": \"InChI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1197\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified by Molecular Formula (MF), including a count of each element in a compound.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||mf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1198\"}, \"name\": \"mf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1198\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The InChIKey (hashed InChI) is a fixed length (25 character) condensed digital representation of an InChI chemical structure specification. It uniquely identifies a chemical compound.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||InChIKey\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1199\"}, \"name\": \"InChIKey\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1199\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_3909\"}, \"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of raw (unplotted) phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic character data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2036\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2037\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2038\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2039\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2040\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic continuous quantitative character data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2037\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1430\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1432\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"PHYLIP file format for continuous quantitative character data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format||Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037||format_1430\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1430\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PHYLIP file format for phylogenetics character frequency data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format||Phylip character frequencies format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037||format_1432\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1432\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic discrete states data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2038\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2038\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1433\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of PHYLIP discrete states data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic discrete states format||Phylip discrete states format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2038||format_1433\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1433\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic cliques data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2039\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2039\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1434\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of PHYLIP cliques data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format||Phylip cliques format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2039||format_1434\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1434\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic invariants data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2040\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2040\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for phylogenetic tree distance data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2049\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2049\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1445\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format for distances, such as Branch Score distance, between two or more phylogenetic trees as used by the Phylip package.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format||Phylip tree distance format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2049||format_1445\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1445\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for reports on a protein family.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein family report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2052\"}], \"name\": \"Protein family report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2052\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for molecular interaction data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054\"}], \"name\": \"Protein interaction format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2054\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"STRING entry format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2304\"}, {\"name\": \"PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3158\"}, {\"name\": \"PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3242\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format (XML) for the STRING database of protein interaction.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||STRING entry format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_2304\"}, \"name\": \"STRING entry format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2304\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML Molecular Interaction Format (MIF), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3158\"}, \"name\": \"PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3158\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MIF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PSI-PAR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3243\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Protein affinity format (PSI-PAR), standardised by HUPO PSI MI. It is compatible with PSI MI XML (MIF) and uses the same XML Schema.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI XML (MIF)||PSI-PAR\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3158||format_3243\"}, \"name\": \"PSI-PAR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3243\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tabular Molecular Interaction format (MITAB), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3242\"}, \"name\": \"PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3242\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for sequence assembly data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence assembly format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2055\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2561\"}, {\"name\": \"ACE\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3001\"}, {\"name\": \"AGP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3693\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Text format for sequence assembly data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2561\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"CAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1630\"}, {\"name\": \"EXP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1631\"}, {\"name\": \"afg\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3582\"}, {\"name\": \"ELAND format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\"}, {\"name\": \"FASTG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\"}, {\"name\": \"GFA 1\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3975\"}, {\"name\": \"GFA 2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3976\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Common Assembly Format (CAF). A sequence assembly format including contigs, base-call qualities, and other metadata.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||CAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_1630\"}, \"name\": \"CAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1630\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Sequence assembly project file EXP format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||EXP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_1631\"}, \"name\": \"EXP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1631\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix EXP format\", \"EXP\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AFG is a single text-based file assembly format  that holds read and consensus information together\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||afg\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3582\"}, \"name\": \"afg\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3582\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text file format used by Eland - the read-mapping program distributed by Illumina with its sequencing analysis pipeline - which maps short Solexa sequence reads to the human reference genome.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||ELAND format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3818\"}, \"name\": \"ELAND format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ELAND\", \"eland\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"FASTG is a format for faithfully representing genome assemblies in the face of allelic polymorphism and assembly uncertainty.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||FASTG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3823\"}, \"name\": \"FASTG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"FASTG assembly graph format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||GFA 1\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3975\"}, \"name\": \"GFA 1\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3975\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||GFA 2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3976\"}, \"name\": \"GFA 2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3976\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"ACE sequence assembly format including contigs, base-call qualities, and other metadata (version Aug 1998 and onwards).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||ACE\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_3001\"}, \"name\": \"ACE\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3001\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AGP is a tabular format for a sequence assembly (a contig, a scaffold/supercontig, or a chromosome).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||AGP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_3693\"}, \"name\": \"AGP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3693\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a file of gene expression data, e.g. a gene expression matrix or profile.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058\"}], \"name\": \"Gene expression report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2058\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"dat\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1637\"}, {\"name\": \"cel\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1638\"}, {\"name\": \"CHP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1644\"}, {\"name\": \"MAGE-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3161\"}, {\"name\": \"MAGE-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3162\"}, {\"name\": \"Cytoscape input file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3477\"}, {\"name\": \"IDAT\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3578\"}, {\"name\": \"rcc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3580\"}, {\"name\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3687\"}, {\"name\": \"GCT/Res format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3709\"}, {\"name\": \"Loom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3913\"}, {\"name\": \"Zarr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3915\"}, {\"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\"}, {\"name\": \"RPKM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3980\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of raw image data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||dat\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1637\"}, \"name\": \"dat\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1637\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix image data file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of information about (raw) expression levels of the individual probes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||cel\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1638\"}, \"name\": \"cel\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1638\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix probe raw data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of information about (normalised) expression levels of the individual probes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||CHP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1644\"}, \"name\": \"CHP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1644\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix probe normalised data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"MAGE-ML XML format for microarray expression data, standardised by MGED (now FGED).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MAGE-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3161\"}, \"name\": \"MAGE-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3161\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"MAGE-TAB textual format for microarray expression data, standardised by MGED (now FGED).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MAGE-TAB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3162\"}, \"name\": \"MAGE-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3162\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of the cytoscape input file of gene expression ratios or values are specified over one or more experiments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Cytoscape input file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3477\"}, \"name\": \"Cytoscape input file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3477\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Proprietary file format for (raw) BeadArray data used by genomewide profiling platforms from Illumina Inc. This format is output directly from the scanner and stores summary intensities for each probe-type on an array.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||IDAT\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3578\"}, \"name\": \"IDAT\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3578\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Reporter Code Count-A data file (.csv) output by the Nanostring nCounter Digital Analyzer, which contains gene sample information, probe information and probe counts.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||rcc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3580\"}, \"name\": \"rcc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3580\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Investigation / Study / Assay (ISA) tab-delimited (TAB) format incorporates metadata from\\nexperiments employing a combination of technologies.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||ISA-TAB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3687\"}, \"name\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3687\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text files of GenePattern that contain a column for each sample, a row for each gene, and an expression value for each gene in each sample.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||GCT/Res format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3709\"}, \"name\": \"GCT/Res format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3709\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCT format\", \"Res format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Loom file format is based on HDF5, a standard for storing large numerical datasets. The Loom format is designed to efficiently hold large omics datasets. Typically, such data takes the form of a large matrix of numbers, along with metadata for the rows and columns.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Loom\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3913\"}, \"name\": \"Loom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3913\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Zarr format is an implementation of chunked, compressed, N-dimensional arrays for storing data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Zarr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3915\"}, \"name\": \"Zarr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3915\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Matrix Market matrix (MTX) format stores numerical or pattern matrices in a dense (array format) or sparse (coordinate format) representation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MTX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3916\"}, \"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited format for gene expression levels table, calculated as Reads Per Kilobase per Million (RPKM) mapped reads.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||RPKM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3980\"}, \"name\": \"RPKM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3980\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression levels table format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a map of (typically one) molecular sequence annotated with features.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Map format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2060\"}], \"name\": \"Map format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2060\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PlasMapper TextMap\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1861\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Map of a plasmid (circular DNA) in PlasMapper TextMap format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Map format||PlasMapper TextMap\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2060||format_1861\"}, \"name\": \"PlasMapper TextMap\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1861\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on PCR primers or hybridisation oligos in a nucleic acid sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Nucleic acid features (primers) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2061\"}], \"name\": \"Nucleic acid features (primers) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2061\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Primer3 primer\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1627\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Report format on PCR primers and hybridisation oligos as generated by Whitehead primer3 program.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Nucleic acid features (primers) format||Primer3 primer\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2061||format_1627\"}, \"name\": \"Primer3 primer\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1627\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report of general information about a specific protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2062\"}], \"name\": \"Protein report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2062\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein report format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2062||format_3951\"}, \"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"ht