of data)||Raw sequence format||ambiguous||consensus\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2097||format_1209\"}, \"name\": \"consensus\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1209\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioXSD-schema-based XML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, Web services, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BioXSD (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2352\"}, \"name\": \"BioXSD (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2352\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD XML\", \"BioXSD XML format\", \"BioXSD in XML\", \"BioXSD in XML format\", \"BioXSD+XML\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for a molecular sequence without any unknown positions or ambiguity characters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2566\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2567\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for a molecular sequence without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2567\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure nucleotide\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2568\"}, {\"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure dna\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2569\"}, {\"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure rna sequence\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2570\"}, {\"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure protein\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2607\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for a nucleotide sequence (characters ACGTU only) without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters .\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure||completely unambiguous pure nucleotide\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567||format_2568\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure nucleotide\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2568\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for a DNA sequence (characters ACGT only) without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure||completely unambiguous pure dna\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567||format_2569\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure dna\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2569\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for an RNA sequence (characters ACGU only) without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure||completely unambiguous pure rna sequence\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567||format_2570\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure rna sequence\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2570\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Alphabet for any protein sequence without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure||completely unambiguous pure protein\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567||format_2607\"}, \"name\": \"completely unambiguous pure protein\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2607\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"2bit binary format of nucleotide sequences using 2 bits per nucleotide. In addition encodes unknown nucleotides and lower-case \'masking\'.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||2bit\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3009\"}, \"name\": \"2bit\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3009\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \".nib (nibble) binary format of a nucleotide sequence using 4 bits per nucleotide (including unknown) and its lower-case \'masking\'.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||.nib\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3010\"}, \"name\": \".nib\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3010\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3772\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BioYAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3773\"}, \"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3909\"}, \"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Mash sketch is a format for sequence / sequence checksum information. To make a sketch, each k-mer in a sequence is hashed, which creates a pseudo-random identifier. By sorting these hashes, a small subset from the top of the sorted list can represent the entire sequence.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||msh\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3911\"}, \"name\": \"msh\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3911\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Mash sketch\", \"min-hash sketch\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A Docker image is a file, comprised of multiple layers, that is used to execute code in a Docker container. An image is essentially built from the instructions for a complete and executable version of an application, which relies on the host OS kernel.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||Docker image format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3973\"}, \"name\": \"Docker image format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3973\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a bibliographic reference.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848\"}], \"name\": \"Bibliographic reference format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2848\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PubMed citation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1734\"}, {\"name\": \"Medline Display Format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1735\"}, {\"name\": \"CiteXplore-core\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1736\"}, {\"name\": \"CiteXplore-all\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1737\"}, {\"name\": \"PubMed XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3848\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of bibliographic reference as used by the PubMed database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||PubMed citation\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1734\"}, \"name\": \"PubMed citation\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1734\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for abstracts of scientific articles from the Medline database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||Medline Display Format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1735\"}, \"name\": \"Medline Display Format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1735\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CiteXplore \'core\' citation format including title, journal, authors and abstract.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||CiteXplore-core\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1736\"}, \"name\": \"CiteXplore-core\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1736\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CiteXplore \'all\' citation format includes all known details such as Mesh terms and cross-references.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||CiteXplore-all\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1737\"}, \"name\": \"CiteXplore-all\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1737\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for collected entries from biobliographic databases MEDLINE and PubMed.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||PubMed XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_3848\"}, \"name\": \"PubMed XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3848\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MEDLINE XML\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of sequence variation annotation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence variation annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2921\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"VCF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3016\"}, {\"name\": \"GVF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3019\"}, {\"name\": \"BCF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3020\"}, {\"name\": \"Ensembl variation file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3499\"}, {\"name\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3622\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Variant Call Format (VCF) for sequence variation (indels, polymorphisms, structural variation).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||VCF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3016\"}, \"name\": \"VCF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3016\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Genome Variation Format (GVF). A GFF3-compatible format with defined header and attribute tags for sequence variation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||GVF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3019\"}, \"name\": \"GVF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3019\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BCF, the binary version of Variant Call Format (VCF) for sequence variation (indels, polymorphisms, structural variation).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||BCF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3020\"}, \"name\": \"BCF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3020\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Ensembl standard format for variation data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||Ensembl variation file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3499\"}, \"name\": \"Ensembl variation file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3499\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format used by the SQLite database conformant to the Gemini schema.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||Gemini SQLite format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3622\"}, \"name\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3622\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a matrix (array) of numerical values.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033\"}], \"name\": \"Matrix format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3033\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Amino acid index format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2017\"}, {\"name\": \"3D-1D scoring matrix format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2064\"}, {\"name\": \"MAT\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3626\"}, {\"name\": \"Zarr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3915\"}, {\"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for an amino acid index.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||Amino acid index format\"