\": \"mzML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3244\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"TraML (Transition Markup Language) is the format for mass spectrometry transitions, standardised by HUPO PSI MSS.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||TraML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3246\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||TraML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3246\"}], \"name\": \"TraML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3246\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"mzIdentML is the exchange format for peptides and proteins identified from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of proteomics search engines.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||mzIdentML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3247\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzIdentML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3247\"}], \"name\": \"mzIdentML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3247\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"mzQuantML is the format for quantitation values associated with peptides, proteins and small molecules from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of quantitation software for proteomics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||mzQuantML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3248\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzQuantML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3248\"}], \"name\": \"mzQuantML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3248\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GelML is the format for describing the process of gel electrophoresis, stan