namics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||BDML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3690\"}], \"name\": \"BDML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3690\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBGN-ML is an XML format for Systems Biology Graphical Notation (SBGN) diagrams of biological pathways or networks.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3692\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3692\"}], \"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Output format used by X! series search engines that is based on the XML language BIOML.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||X!Tandem XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3711\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||X!Tandem XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3711\"}], \"name\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3711\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Synthetic Biology Open Language (SBOL) is an XML format for the specification and exchange of biological design information in synthetic biology.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||SBOL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3725\"}], \"name\": \"SBOL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3725\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PMML uses XML to represent mining models. The structure of the models is described by an XML Schema.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||XML||PMML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2332||format_3726\"}], \"name\": \"PMML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/form