], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"bigBed format for large sequence annotation tracks, similar to textual BED format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bigBed\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3004\"}, \"name\": \"bigBed\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3004\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Wiggle format (WIG) of a sequence annotation track that consists of a value for each sequence position. Typically to be displayed in a genome browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||WIG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3005\"}, \"name\": \"WIG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3005\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"bigWig format for large sequence annotation tracks that consist of a value for each sequence position. Similar to textual WIG format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bigWig\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3006\"}, \"name\": \"bigWig\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3006\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PSL format of alignments, typically generated by BLAT or psLayout. Can be displayed in a genome browser like a sequence annotation track.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||PSL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3007\"}, \"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Multiple Alignment Format (MAF) supporting alignments of whole genomes with rearrangements, directions, multiple pieces to the alignment, and so forth.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||MAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3008\"}, \"name\": \"MAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3008\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"genePred table format for gene prediction tracks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||genePred\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3011\"}, \"name\": \"genePred\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3011\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Personal Genome SNP (pgSnp) format for sequence variation tracks (indels and polymorphisms), supported by the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||pgSnp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3012\"}, \"name\": \"pgSnp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3012\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GTrack is a generic and optimised tabular format for genome or sequence feature tracks. GTrack unifies the power of other track formats (e.g. GFF3, BED, WIG), and while optimised in size, adds more flexibility, customisation, and automation (\\\"machine understandability\\\").\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||GTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3164\"}, \"name\": \"GTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3164\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD/GTrack GTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack GTrack\", \"GTrack format\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite GTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack GTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The bedGraph format allows display of continuous-valued data in track format. This display type is useful for probability scores and transcriptome data\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||bedgraph\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3583\"}, \"name\": \"bedgraph\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3583\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Custom Sequence annotation track format used by Galaxy.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||customtrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3588\"}, \"name\": \"customtrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3588\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BTrack is an HDF5-based binary format for genome or sequence feature tracks and their collections, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. BTrack is a binary, compressed alternative to the GTrack and GSuite formats.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||BTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3776\"}, \"name\": \"BTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3776\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BTrack (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"BTrack format\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BTrack\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite BTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack BTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The GEN file format contains genetic data and describes SNPs.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||GEN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3812\"}, \"name\": \"GEN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3812\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genotype file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \". proBED is an adaptation of BED (format_3003), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||proBED\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3827\"}, \"name\": \"proBED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3827\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A declaration file format for UCSC browsers track dataset display charateristics.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||TrackDB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3991\"}, \"name\": \"TrackDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3991\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3772\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioYAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3773\"}, \"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||JSON||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3774\"}], \"name\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3774\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GSuite is a tabular format for collections of genome or sequence feature tracks, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. GSuite contains links to genome/sequence tracks, with additional metadata.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||GSuite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3775\"}, \"name\": \"GSuite\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3775\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD/GTrack GSuite\", \"BioXSD|GTrack GSuite\", \"GSuite (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"GSuite format\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite GSuite\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack GSuite\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BTrack is an HDF5-based binary format for genome or sequence feature tracks and their collections, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. BTrack is a binary, compressed alternative to the GTrack and GSuite formats.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||BTrack\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3776\"}, \"name\": \"BTrack\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3776\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BTrack (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"BTrack format\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BTrack\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BTrack\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite BTrack\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack BTrack\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tree structure of Protein Sequence Database Markup Language generated using Matra software.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||PSDML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3851\"}, \"name\": \"PSDML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3851\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for the UniParc database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||UniParc XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3853\"}, \"name\": \"UniParc XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3853\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for the UniRef reference clusters.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||UniRef XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3854\"}, \"name\": \"UniRef XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3854\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The NET file format is used to describe the data that underlie the net alignment annotations in the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||NET\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3983\"}, \"name\": \"NET\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3983\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of QMAP files generated for methylation data from an internal BGI pipeline.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||QMAP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3984\"}, \"name\": \"QMAP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3984\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for molecular sequence alignment information.