e\": \"Relaxed PHYLIP Interleaved\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3819\"}, {\"name\": \"Relaxed PHYLIP Sequential\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3820\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Phylip format for (aligned) sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||Phylip format variant||PHYLIP format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_2924||format_1997\"}, \"name\": \"PHYLIP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1997\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PHYLIP\", \"PHYLIP interleaved format\", \"ph\", \"phy\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylip non-interleaved format for (aligned) sequences.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||Phylip format variant||PHYLIP sequential\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_2924||format_1998\"}, \"name\": \"PHYLIP sequential\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1998\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PHYLIP sequential format\", \"phylipnon\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylip multiple alignment sequence format, less stringent than PHYLIP format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||Phylip format variant||Relaxed PHYLIP Interleaved\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_2924||format_3819\"}, \"name\": \"Relaxed PHYLIP Interleaved\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3819\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PHYLIP Interleaved format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylip multiple alignment sequence format, less stringent than PHYLIP sequential format (format_1998).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||Phylip format variant||Relaxed PHYLIP Sequential\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_2924||format_3820\"}, \"name\": \"Relaxed PHYLIP Sequential\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3820\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Relaxed PHYLIP non-interleaved\", \"Relaxed PHYLIP non-interleaved format\", \"Relaxed PHYLIP sequential format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Multiple Alignment Format (MAF) supporting alignments of whole genomes with rearrangements, directions, multiple pieces to the alignment, and so forth.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||MAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3008\"}, \"name\": \"MAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3008\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The A2M format is used as the primary format for multiple alignments of protein or nucleic-acid sequences in the SAM suite of tools. It is a small modification of FASTA format for sequences and is compatible with most tools that read FASTA.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||A2M\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3281\"}, \"name\": \"A2M\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3281\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A multiple alignment in vertical format, as used in the AMPS (Alignment of Multiple Protein Sequences) pacakge.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||BLC\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3313\"}], \"name\": \"BLC\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3313\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Block file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"EMBOSS simple sequence pair alignment format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||PO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3330\"}], \"name\": \"PO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3330\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Some format based on the GCG format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486\"}, \"name\": \"GCG format variant\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3486\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"GCG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1935\"}, {\"name\": \"GCG MSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1947\"}, {\"name\": \"RSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3485\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"GCG sequence file format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||GCG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_1935\"}, \"name\": \"GCG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1935\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCG SSF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GCG MSF (multiple sequence file) file format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||GCG MSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_1947\"}, \"name\": \"GCG MSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1947\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Rich sequence format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||GCG format variant||RSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3486||format_3485\"}, \"name\": \"RSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3485\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCG RSF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Color space FASTA format sequence variant.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||csfasta\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3589\"}, \"name\": \"csfasta\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3589\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The A2M format is used as the primary format for multiple alignments of protein or nucleic-acid sequences in the SAM suite of tools. It is a small modification of FASTA format for sequences and is compatible with most tools that read FASTA.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (text)||XMFA\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2554||format_3811\"}, \"name\": \"XMFA\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3811\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"alignment format\", \"eXtended Multi-FastA format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for molecular sequence alignment information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2555\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BioXSD (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2352\"}, {\"name\": \"HSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3845\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"BioXSD-schema-based XML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, Web services, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)||BioXSD (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555||format_2352\"}, \"name\": \"BioXSD (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2352\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD XML\", \"BioXSD XML format\", \"BioXSD in XML\", \"BioXSD in XML format\", \"BioXSD+XML\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An alignment format generated by PRANK/PRANKSTER consisting of four elements: newick, nodes, selection and model.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (XML)||HSAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2555||format_3845\"}, \"name\": \"HSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3845\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for molecular sequence alignment information that can hold sequence alignment(s) of only 2 sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920\"}], \"name\": \"Alignment format (pair only)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2920\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"srspair\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2003\"}, {\"name\": \"BAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2572\"}, {\"name\": \"SAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2573\"}, {\"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\"}, {\"name\": \"axt\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3013\"}, {\"name\": \"LAV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3014\"}, {\"name\": \"Pileup\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3015\"}, {\"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\"}, {\"name\": \"CRAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3462\"}, {\"name\": \"proBAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3826\"}, {\"name\": \"CHAIN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3982\"}, {\"name\": \"CIGAR format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3992\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Simple sequence pair (alignment) format for SRS.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||srspair\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2003\"}, \"name\": \"srspair\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2003\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BAM format, the binary, BGZF-formatted compressed version of SAM format for alignment of nucleotide sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). May contain base-call and alignment qualities and other data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||BAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2572\"}, \"name\": \"BAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2572\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Sequence Alignment/Map (SAM) format for alignment of nucleotide sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). May contain base-call and alignment qualities and other data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||SAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_2573\"}, \"name\": \"SAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2573\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PSL format of alignments, typically generated by BLAT or psLayout. Can be displayed in a genome browser like a sequence annotation track.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||PSL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3007\"}, \"name\": \"PSL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"axt format of alignments, typically produced from BLASTZ.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||axt\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3013\"}, \"name\": \"axt\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3013\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"LAV format of alignments generated by BLASTZ and LASTZ.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||LAV\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3014\"}, \"name\": \"LAV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3014\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Pileup format of alignment of sequences (e.g. sequencing reads) to (a) reference sequence(s). Contains aligned bases per base of the reference sequence(s).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||Pileup\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3015\"}, \"name\": \"Pileup\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3015\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"EBI Application Result XML is a format returned by sequence similarity search Web services at EBI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||EBI Application Result XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3157\"}, \"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Reference-based compression of alignment format\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CRAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3462\"}, \"name\": \"CRAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3462\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \". proBAM is an adaptation of BAM (format_2572), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||proBAM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3826\"}, \"name\": \"proBAM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3826\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The CHAIN format describes a pairwise alignment that allow gaps in both sequences simultaneously and is used by the UCSC Genome Browser.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CHAIN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3982\"}, \"name\": \"CHAIN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3982\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Compact Idiosyncratic Gapped Alignment Report format is a compressed (run-length encoded) pairwise alignment format. It is useful for representing long (e.g. genomic) pairwise alignments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||Alignment format (pair only)||CIGAR format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_2920||format_3992\"}, \"name\": \"CIGAR format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3992\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"CIGAR\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"RNA Markup Language.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||RNAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3311\"}, \"name\": \"RNAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3311\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3772\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioYAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3773\"}, \"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3774\"}, \"name\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3774\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Binary format used by the ARB software suite\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||ARB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3830\"}, \"name\": \"ARB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3830\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ARB binary format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A set of XML compliant markup components for describing multiple sequence alignments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Alignment format||MSAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1921||format_3849\"}, \"name\": \"MSAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3849\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format\