data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Phylip tree raw\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1425\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree raw\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1425\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree data format used by the PHYLIP program.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Phylip tree format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1435\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1435\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the TreeBASE database of phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeBASE format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1436\"}, \"name\": \"TreeBASE format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1436\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the TreeFam database of phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeFam format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1437\"}, \"name\": \"TreeFam format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1437\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree Newick (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||newick\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1910\"}, \"name\": \"newick\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"nh\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree TreeCon (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||TreeCon format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1911\"}, \"name\": \"TreeCon format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1911\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Phylogenetic tree Nexus (text) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (text)||Nexus format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2556||format_1912\"}, \"name\": \"Nexus format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1912\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format for a phylogenetic tree.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2557\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"phyloXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3159\"}, {\"name\": \"NeXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3160\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"phyloXML is a standardised XML format for phylogenetic trees, networks, and associated data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)||phyloXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557||format_3159\"}, \"name\": \"phyloXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3159\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"NeXML is a standardised XML format for rich phyloinformatic data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree format||Phylogenetic tree format (XML)||NeXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2006||format_2557||format_3160\"}, \"name\": \"NeXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3160\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a biological pathway or network.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013\"}], \"name\": \"Biological pathway or network format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2013\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"SBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2585\"}, {\"name\": \"BioPAX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3156\"}, {\"name\": \"CopasiML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3239\"}, {\"name\": \"CellML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3240\"}, {\"name\": \"sif\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3619\"}, {\"name\": \"GPML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3657\"}, {\"name\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3686\"}, {\"name\": \"SBtab\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3688\"}, {\"name\": \"BCML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3689\"}, {\"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\"}, {\"name\": \"VisML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3821\"}, {\"name\": \"GML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\"}, {\"name\": \"KGML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3847\"}, {\"name\": \"NeuroML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3971\"}, {\"name\": \"BNGL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3972\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Systems Biology Markup Language (SBML), the standard XML format for models of biological processes such as for example metabolism, cell signaling, and gene regulation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_2585\"}, \"name\": \"SBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2585\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioPAX is an exchange format for pathway data, with its data model defined in OWL.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BioPAX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3156\"}], \"name\": \"BioPAX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3156\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CopasiML, the native format of COPASI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||CopasiML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3239\"}, \"name\": \"CopasiML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3239\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"CellML, the format for mathematical models of biological and other networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||CellML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3240\"}, \"name\": \"CellML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3240\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SIF (simple interaction file) Format - a network/pathway format used for instance in cytoscape.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||sif\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3619\"}], \"name\": \"sif\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3619\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Pathway Markup Language (GPML) is an XML format used for exchanging biological pathways.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GPML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3657\"}, \"name\": \"GPML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3657\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Open Modeling EXchange format (OMEX) is a ZIPped format for encapsulating all information necessary for a modeling and simulation project in systems biology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||COMBINE OMEX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3686\"}, \"name\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3686\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBtab is a tabular format for biochemical network models.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBtab\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3688\"}, \"name\": \"SBtab\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3688\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Biological Connection Markup Language (BCML) is an XML format for biological pathways.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BCML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3689\"}, \"name\": \"BCML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3689\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SBGN-ML is an XML format for Systems Biology Graphical Notation (SBGN) diagrams of biological pathways or networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||SBGN-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3692\"}, \"name\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3692\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Default XML format of VisANT, containing all the network information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||VisML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3821\"}, \"name\": \"VisML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3821\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"VisANT xml\", \"VisANT xml format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GML (Graph Modeling Language) is a text file format supporting network data with a very easy syntax. It is used by Graphlet, Pajek, yEd, LEDA and NetworkX.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3822\"}, \"name\": \"GML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GML format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The KEGG Markup Language (KGML) is an exchange format of the KEGG pathway maps, which is converted from internally used KGML+ (KGML+SVG) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||KGML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3847\"}, \"name\": \"KGML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3847\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"KEGG Markup Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"A model description language for computational neuroscience.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||NeuroML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3971\"}, \"name\": \"NeuroML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3971\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BioNetGen is a format for the specification and simulation of rule-based models of biochemical systems, including signal transduction, metabolic, and genetic regulatory networks.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||BNGL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3972\"}, \"name\": \"BNGL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3972\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioNetGen Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a sequence-profile alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence-profile alignment format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2014\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1419\"}, {\"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1421\"}, {\"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1422\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format for alignment of molecular sequences to MEME profiles (position-dependent scoring matrices) as generated by the MAST tool from the MEME package.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1419\"}, \"name\": \"Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1419\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format used by the HMMER package for an alignment of a sequence against a hidden Markov model database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1421\"}, \"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1421\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format used by the HMMER package for of an alignment of a hidden Markov model against a sequence database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence-profile alignment format||HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2014||format_1422\"}, \"name\": \"HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1422\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a full-text scientific article.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020\"}], \"name\": \"Article format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2020\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Literature format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"pmc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1739\"}, {\"name\": \"medline\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2194\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Article format of the PubMed Central database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format||pmc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020||format_1739\"}, \"name\": \"pmc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1739\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Abstract format used by MedLine database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Article format||medline\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2020||format_2194\"}, \"name\": \"medline\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2194\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format of a report from text mining.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Text mining report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2021\"}], \"name\": \"Text mining report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2021\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"iHOP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1740\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The format of iHOP (Information Hyperlinked over Proteins) text-mining result.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Text mining report format||iHOP format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2021||format_1740\"}, \"name\": \"iHOP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1740\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for reports on enzyme kinetics.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Enzyme kinetics report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2027\"}], \"name\": \"Enzyme kinetics report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2027\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"findkm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1582\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"A report format for the kinetics of enzyme-catalysed reaction(s) in a format generated by EMBOSS findkm. This includes Michaelis Menten plot, Hanes Woolf plot, Michaelis Menten constant (Km) and maximum velocity (Vmax).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Enzyme kinetics report format||findkm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2027||format_1582\"}, \"name\": \"findkm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1582\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on a chemical compound.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030\"}], \"name\": \"Chemical data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2030\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Chemical compound annotation format\", \"Chemical structure format\", \"Small molecule report format\", \"Small molecule structure format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"HET group dictionary entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1705\"}, {\"name\": \"SDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\"}, {\"name\": \"Molfile\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\"}, {\"name\": \"Mol2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\"}, {\"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"The format of an entry from the HET group dictionary (HET groups from PDB files).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||HET group dictionary entry format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_1705\"}, \"name\": \"HET group dictionary entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1705\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"SDF is one of a family of chemical-data file formats developed by MDL Information Systems; it is intended especially for structural information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||SDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3814\"}, \"name\": \"SDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An MDL Molfile is a file format for holding information about the atoms, bonds, connectivity and coordinates of a molecule.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Molfile\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3815\"}, \"name\": \"Molfile\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Complete, portable representation of a SYBYL molecule. ASCII file which contains all the information needed to reconstruct a SYBYL molecule.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Mol2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3816\"}, \"name\": \"Mol2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3951\"}, \"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on a particular locus, gene, gene system or groups of genes.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031\"}], \"name\": \"Gene annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2031\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene features format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"est2genome format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1316\"}, {\"name\": \"OrthoXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3850\"}, {\"name\": \"WEGO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3979\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on exon-intron structure generated by EMBOSS est2genome.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||est2genome format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_1316\"}, \"name\": \"est2genome format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1316\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"OrthoXML is designed broadly to allow the storage and comparison of orthology data from any ortholog database. It establishes a structure for describing orthology relationships while still allowing flexibility for database-specific information to be encapsulated in the same format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||OrthoXML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_3850\"}, \"name\": \"OrthoXML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3850\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"WEGO native format used by the Web Gene Ontology Annotation Plot application.   Tab-delimited format with gene names and others GO IDs (columns) with one annotation record per line.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||WEGO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_3979\"}, \"name\": \"WEGO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3979\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a workflow.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032\"}], \"name\": \"Workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2032\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Taverna workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1665\"}, {\"name\": \"KNIME datatable format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3765\"}, {\"name\": \"CWL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3857\"}, {\"name\": \"gxformat2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3985\"}, {\"name\": \"Python script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3996\"}, {\"name\": \"Perl script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3998\"}, {\"name\": \"R script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3999\"}, {\"name\": \"R markdown\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4000\"}, {\"name\": \"MATLAB script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4007\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Taverna workflows.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||Taverna workflow format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_1665\"}, \"name\": \"Taverna workflow format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1665\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data table formatted such that it can be passed/streamed within the KNIME platform.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||KNIME datatable format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3765\"}], \"name\": \"KNIME datatable format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3765\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Common Workflow Language (CWL) format for description of command-line tools and workflows.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||CWL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_3857\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||CWL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3857\"}], \"name\": \"CWL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3857\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Common Workflow Language\", \"CommonWL\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"An emerging format for high-level Galaxy workflow description.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \