\"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_4000\"}, \"name\": \"R markdown\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4000\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The file format for MATLAB scripts or functions.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Workflow format||MATLAB script\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2032||format_4007\"}, \"name\": \"MATLAB script\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4007\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MATLAB\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Data format for a molecular tertiary structure.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033\"}], \"name\": \"Tertiary structure format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2033\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PDB database entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1475\"}, {\"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\"}, {\"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\"}, {\"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\"}, {\"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\"}, {\"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\"}, {\"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\"}, {\"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\"}, {\"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of an entry (or part of an entry) from the PDB database.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475\"}], \"name\": \"PDB database entry format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1475\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PDB entry format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1476\"}, {\"name\": \"mmCIF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1477\"}, {\"name\": \"PDBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1478\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbatom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1950\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbatomnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1951\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbseqresnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1952\"}, {\"name\": \"pdbseqres\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1953\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in PDB format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||PDB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1476\"}, \"name\": \"PDB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1476\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"PDB format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in mmCIF format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||mmCIF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1477\"}, \"name\": \"mmCIF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1477\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format of PDB database in PDBML (XML) format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||PDBML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1478\"}, \"name\": \"PDBML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1478\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB sequence format (ATOM lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbatom\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1950\"}, \"name\": \"pdbatom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1950\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB nucleotide sequence format (ATOM lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbatomnuc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1951\"}, \"name\": \"pdbatomnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB nucleotide sequence format (SEQRES lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbseqresnuc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1952\"}, \"name\": \"pdbseqresnuc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1952\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PDB sequence format (SEQRES lines).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PDB database entry format||pdbseqres\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_1475||format_1953\"}, \"name\": \"pdbseqres\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1953\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||XYZ\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3877\"}, \"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||mdcrd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3878\"}, \"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3880\"}, \"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||AMBER top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3881\"}, \"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3882\"}, \"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3883\"}, \"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||RST\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3886\"}, \"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||CHARMM rtf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3887\"}, \"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||trr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3910\"}, \"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Text format of a chemical formula.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035\"}], \"name\": \"Chemical formula format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2035\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"SMILES\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1196\"}, {\"name\": \"InChI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1197\"}, {\"name\": \"mf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1198\"}, {\"name\": \"InChIKey\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1199\"}, {\"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified in Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System (SMILES) line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||SMILES\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1196\"}, \"name\": \"SMILES\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1196\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"smarts\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1200\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"SMILES ARbitrary Target Specification (SMARTS) format for chemical structure specification, which is a subset of the SMILES line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||SMILES||smarts\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1196||format_1200\"}, \"name\": \"smarts\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1200\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified in IUPAC International Chemical Identifier (InChI) line notation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||InChI\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1197\"}, \"name\": \"InChI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1197\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Chemical structure specified by Molecular Formula (MF), including a count of each element in a compound.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||mf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1198\"}, \"name\": \"mf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1198\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The InChIKey (hashed InChI) is a fixed length (25 character) condensed digital representation of an InChI chemical structure specification. It uniquely identifies a chemical compound.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||InChIKey\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_1199\"}, \"name\": \"InChIKey\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1199\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_3909\"}, \"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of raw (unplotted) phylogenetic data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic character data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2036\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2037\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2038\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2039\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2040\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic continuous quantitative character data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2037\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1430\"}, {\"name\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1432\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"PHYLIP file format for continuous quantitative character data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format||Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037||format_1430\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1430\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"PHYLIP file format for phylogenetics character frequency data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format||Phylip character frequencies format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2037||format_1432\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1432\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic discrete states data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2038\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2038\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1433\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of PHYLIP discrete states data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic discrete states format||Phylip discrete states format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2038||format_1433\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1433\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic cliques data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2039\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2039\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1434\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of PHYLIP cliques data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format||Phylip cliques format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2039||format_1434\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1434\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of phylogenetic invariants data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic character data format||Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2036||format_2040\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2040\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for phylogenetic tree distance data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2049\"}], \"name\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2049\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1445\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format for distances, such as Branch Score distance, between two or more phylogenetic trees as used by the Phylip package.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format||Phylip tree distance format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2049||format_1445\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1445\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for reports on a protein family.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein family report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2052\"}], \"name\": \"Protein family report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2052\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for molecular interaction data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054\"}], \"name\": \"Protein interaction format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2054\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"STRING entry format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2304\"}, {\"name\": \"PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3158\"}, {\"name\": \"PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3242\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Entry format (XML) for the STRING database of protein interaction.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||STRING entry format (XML)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_2304\"}, \"name\": \"STRING entry format (XML)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2304\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML Molecular Interaction Format (MIF), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3158\"}, \"name\": \"PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3158\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MIF\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PSI-PAR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3243\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Protein affinity format (PSI-PAR), standardised by HUPO PSI MI. It is compatible with PSI MI XML (MIF) and uses the same XML Schema.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI XML (MIF)||PSI-PAR\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3158||format_3243\"}, \"name\": \"PSI-PAR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3243\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tabular Molecular Interaction format (MITAB), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein interaction format||PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2054||format_3242\"}, \"name\": \"PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3242\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format for sequence assembly data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence assembly format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2055\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2561\"}, {\"name\": \"ACE\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3001\"}, {\"name\": \"AGP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3693\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Text format for sequence assembly data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence assembly format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2561\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"CAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1630\"}, {\"name\": \"EXP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1631\"}, {\"name\": \"afg\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3582\"}, {\"name\": \"ELAND format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\"}, {\"name\": \"FASTG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\"}, {\"name\": \"GFA 1\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3975\"}, {\"name\": \"GFA 2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3976\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Common Assembly Format (CAF). A sequence assembly format including contigs, base-call qualities, and other metadata.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||CAF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_1630\"}, \"name\": \"CAF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1630\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Sequence assembly project file EXP format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||EXP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_1631\"}, \"name\": \"EXP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1631\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix EXP format\", \"EXP\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AFG is a single text-based file assembly format  that holds read and consensus information together\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||afg\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3582\"}, \"name\": \"afg\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3582\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text file format used by Eland - the read-mapping program distributed by Illumina with its sequencing analysis pipeline - which maps short Solexa sequence reads to the human reference genome.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||ELAND format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3818\"}, \"name\": \"ELAND format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ELAND\", \"eland\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"FASTG is a format for faithfully representing genome assemblies in the face of allelic polymorphism and assembly uncertainty.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||FASTG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3823\"}, \"name\": \"FASTG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"FASTG assembly graph format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||GFA 1\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3975\"}, \"name\": \"GFA 1\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3975\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Graphical Fragment Assembly captures sequence graphs as the product of an assembly, a representation of variation in genomes, splice graphs in genes, or even overlap between reads from long-read sequencing technology.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||GFA 2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3976\"}, \"name\": \"GFA 2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3976\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"ACE sequence assembly format including contigs, base-call qualities, and other metadata (version Aug 1998 and onwards).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||ACE\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_3001\"}, \"name\": \"ACE\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3001\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"AGP is a tabular format for a sequence assembly (a contig, a scaffold/supercontig, or a chromosome).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||AGP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_3693\"}, \"name\": \"AGP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3693\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a file of gene expression data, e.g. a gene expression matrix or profile.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058\"}], \"name\": \"Gene expression report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2058\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"dat\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1637\"}, {\"name\": \"cel\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1638\"}, {\"name\": \"CHP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1644\"}, {\"name\": \"MAGE-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3161\"}, {\"name\": \"MAGE-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3162\"}, {\"name\": \"Cytoscape input file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3477\"}, {\"name\": \"IDAT\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3578\"}, {\"name\": \"rcc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3580\"}, {\"name\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3687\"}, {\"name\": \"GCT/Res format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3709\"}, {\"name\": \"Loom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3913\"}, {\"name\": \"Zarr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3915\"}, {\"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\"}, {\"name\": \"RPKM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3980\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of raw image data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||dat\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1637\"}, \"name\": \"dat\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1637\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix image data file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of information about (raw) expression levels of the individual probes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||cel\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1638\"}, \"name\": \"cel\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1638\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix probe raw data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of Affymetrix data file of information about (normalised) expression levels of the individual probes.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||CHP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_1644\"}, \"name\": \"CHP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1644\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Affymetrix probe normalised data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"MAGE-ML XML format for microarray expression data, standardised by MGED (now FGED).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MAGE-ML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3161\"}, \"name\": \"MAGE-ML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3161\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"MAGE-TAB textual format for microarray expression data, standardised by MGED (now FGED).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MAGE-TAB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3162\"}, \"name\": \"MAGE-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3162\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of the cytoscape input file of gene expression ratios or values are specified over one or more experiments.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Cytoscape input file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3477\"}, \"name\": \"Cytoscape input file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3477\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Proprietary file format for (raw) BeadArray data used by genomewide profiling platforms from Illumina Inc. This format is output directly from the scanner and stores summary intensities for each probe-type on an array.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||IDAT\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3578\"}, \"name\": \"IDAT\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3578\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Reporter Code Count-A data file (.csv) output by the Nanostring nCounter Digital Analyzer, which contains gene sample information, probe information and probe counts.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||rcc\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3580\"}, \"name\": \"rcc\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3580\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Investigation / Study / Assay (ISA) tab-delimited (TAB) format incorporates metadata from\\nexperiments employing a combination of technologies.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||ISA-TAB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3687\"}, \"name\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3687\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text files of GenePattern that contain a column for each sample, a row for each gene, and an expression value for each gene in each sample.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||GCT/Res format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3709\"}, \"name\": \"GCT/Res format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3709\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GCT format\", \"Res format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Loom file format is based on HDF5, a standard for storing large numerical datasets. The Loom format is designed to efficiently hold large omics datasets. Typically, such data takes the form of a large matrix of numbers, along with metadata for the rows and columns.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Loom\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3913\"}, \"name\": \"Loom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3913\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Zarr format is an implementation of chunked, compressed, N-dimensional arrays for storing data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||Zarr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3915\"}, \"name\": \"Zarr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3915\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The Matrix Market matrix (MTX) format stores numerical or pattern matrices in a dense (array format) or sparse (coordinate format) representation.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MTX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3916\"}, \"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited format for gene expression levels table, calculated as Reads Per Kilobase per Million (RPKM) mapped reads.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||RPKM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3980\"}, \"name\": \"RPKM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3980\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression levels table format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a map of (typically one) molecular sequence annotated with features.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Map format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2060\"}], \"name\": \"Map format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2060\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"PlasMapper TextMap\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1861\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Map of a plasmid (circular DNA) in PlasMapper TextMap format.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Map format||PlasMapper TextMap\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2060||format_1861\"}, \"name\": \"PlasMapper TextMap\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1861\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on PCR primers or hybridisation oligos in a nucleic acid sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Nucleic acid features (primers) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2061\"}], \"name\": \"Nucleic acid features (primers) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2061\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Primer3 primer\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1627\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Report format on PCR primers and hybridisation oligos as generated by Whitehead primer3 program.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Nucleic acid features (primers) format||Primer3 primer\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2061||format_1627\"}, \"name\": \"Primer3 primer\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1627\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report of general information about a specific protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2062\"}], \"name\": \"Protein report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2062\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein report format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2062||format_3951\"}, \"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on the quality of a protein three-dimensional model.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein structure report (quality evaluation) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2065\"}], \"name\": \"Protein structure report (quality evaluation) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2065\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Pcons report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1551\"}, {\"name\": \"ProQ report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1552\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of output of the Pcons Model Quality Assessment Program (MQAP).\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein structure report (quality evaluation) format||Pcons report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2065||format_1551\"}, \"name\": \"Pcons report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1551\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of output of the ProQ protein model quality predictor.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein structure report (quality evaluation) format||ProQ report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2065||format_1552\"}, \"name\": \"ProQ report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1552\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a report on sequence hits and associated data from searching a sequence database.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066\"}], \"name\": \"Database hits (sequence) format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2066\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"FASTA search results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1332\"}, {\"name\": \"BLAST results\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1333\"}, {\"name\": \"mspcrunch\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1334\"}, {\"name\": \"Smith-Waterman format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1335\"}, {\"name\": \"dhf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1336\"}, {\"name\": \"lhf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1337\"}, {\"name\": \"InterPro hits format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1341\"}, {\"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a sequence database search using FASTA.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||FASTA search results format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1332\"}, \"name\": \"FASTA search results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1332\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a sequence database search using some variant of BLAST.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||BLAST results\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1333\"}, \"name\": \"BLAST results\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1333\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"BLAST XML results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3331\"}, {\"name\": \"BLAST XML v2 results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3836\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"XML format as produced by the NCBI Blast package\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||BLAST results||BLAST XML results format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1333||format_3331\"}, \"name\": \"BLAST XML results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3331\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"XML format as produced by the NCBI Blast package v2.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||BLAST results||BLAST XML v2 results format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1333||format_3836\"}, \"name\": \"BLAST XML v2 results format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3836\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a sequence database search using some variant of MSPCrunch.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||mspcrunch\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1334\"}, \"name\": \"mspcrunch\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1334\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a sequence database search using some variant of Smith Waterman.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||Smith-Waterman format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1335\"}, \"name\": \"Smith-Waterman format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1335\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of EMBASSY domain hits file (DHF) of hits (sequences) with domain classification information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||dhf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1336\"}, \"name\": \"dhf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1336\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of EMBASSY ligand hits file (LHF) of database hits (sequences) with ligand classification information.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||lhf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1337\"}, \"name\": \"lhf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1337\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Results format for searches of the InterPro database.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||InterPro hits format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1341\"}, \"name\": \"InterPro hits format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1341\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"InterPro protein view report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1342\"}, {\"name\": \"InterPro match table format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1343\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a search of the InterPro database showing matches of query protein sequence(s) to InterPro entries.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||InterPro hits format||InterPro protein view report format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1341||format_1342\"}, \"name\": \"InterPro protein view report format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1342\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of results of a search of the InterPro database showing matches between protein sequence(s) and signatures for an InterPro entry.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||InterPro hits format||InterPro match table format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_1341||format_1343\"}, \"name\": \"InterPro match table format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1343\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"EBI Application Result XML is a format returned by sequence similarity search Web services at EBI.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Database hits (sequence) format||EBI Application Result XML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2066||format_3157\"}, \"name\": \"EBI Application Result XML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3157\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a matrix of genetic distances between molecular sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence distance matrix format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2067\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence distance matrix format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2067\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Phylip distance matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1423\"}]}, {\"definition\": \"Format of PHYLIP phylogenetic distance matrix data.\", \"path\": {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence distance matrix format||Phylip distance matrix\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2067||format_1423\"}, \"name\": \"Phylip distance matrix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1423\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Format of a sequence motif.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence motif format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2068\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence motif format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2068\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"prosite-pattern\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1356\"}, {\"name\": \"EMBOSS sequence pattern\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1357\"}, {\"name\": \"meme-motif\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1360\"}]}, {\"defi