ory Next Generation (TNG) is a format for storage of molecular simulation data. It is designed and implemented by the GROMACS development group, and it is called to be the substitute of the XTC format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||TNG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3876\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||TNG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3876\"}], \"name\": \"TNG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3876\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Trajectory Next Generation format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3885\": {\"definition\": \"Scripps Research Institute BinPos format is a binary formatted file to store atom coordinates.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||BinPos\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3885\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||BinPos\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3885\"}], \"name\": \"BinPos\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3885\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Scripps Research Institute BinPos\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3911\": {\"definition\": \"Mash sketch is a format for sequence / sequence checksum information. To make a sketch, each k-mer in a sequence is hashed, which creates a pseudo-random identifier. By sorting these hashes, a small subset from the top of the sorted list can represent the entire sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||msh\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3911\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||msh\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3911\"}], \"name\": \"msh\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3911\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Mash sketch\", \"min-hash sketch\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\":