\"format_1915||format_2330||format_3751||format_3475||format_3162\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MAGE-TAB\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3162\"}], \"name\": \"MAGE-TAB\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3162\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3979\": {\"definition\": \"WEGO native format used by the Web Gene Ontology Annotation Plot application.   Tab-delimited format with gene names and others GO IDs (columns) with one annotation record per line.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||DSV||TSV||WEGO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3751||format_3475||format_3979\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene annotation format||WEGO\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2031||format_3979\"}], \"name\": \"WEGO\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3979\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3980\": {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited format for gene expression levels table, calculated as Reads Per Kilobase per Million (RPKM) mapped reads.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||DSV||TSV||RPKM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3751||format_3475||format_3980\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||RPKM\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3980\"}], \"name\": \"RPKM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3980\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Gene expression levels table format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3752\": {\"definition\": \"Tabular data represented as comma-separated values in a text file.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||DSV||CSV\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3751||format_3752\"}], \"name\": \"CSV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3752\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Comma-separated values\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3758\": {\"definition\": \"\\\"Raw\\\" result file from SEQUEST database search.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||SEQUEST .out file\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3758\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||SEQUEST .out file\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3758\"}], \"name\": \"SEQUEST .out file\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3758\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3775\": {\"definition\": \"GSuite is a tabular format for collections of genome or sequence feature tracks, suitable for integrative multi-track analysis. GSuite contains links to genome/sequence tracks, with additional metadata.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GSuite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3775\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||GSuite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_3775\"}], \"name\": \"GSuite\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3775\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BioXSD/GTrack GSuite\", \"BioXSD|GTrack GSuite\", \"GSuite (GTrack ecosystem of formats)\", \"GSuite format\", \"GTrack|BTrack|GSuite GSuite\", \"GTrack|GSuite|BTrack GSuite\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3777\": {\"definition\": \"The FAO/Bioversity/IPGRI Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors (MCPD) is an international standard format for exchange of germplasm information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||MCPD\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3777\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format||MCPD\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706||format_3777\"}], \"name\": \"MCPD\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3777\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Bioversity MCPD\", \"FAO MCPD\", \"MCPD format\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"IPGRI MCPD\", \"MCPD V.1\", \"MCPD V.2\"], \"children\": []}, \"format_3783\": {\"definition\": \"Native textual export format of annotated scientific text from PubTator.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||PubTator format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3783\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||PubTator format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3783\"}], \"name\": \"PubTator format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3783\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3785\": {\"definition\": \"A family of similar formats of text annotation, used by BRAT and other tools, known as BioNLP Shared Task format (BioNLP 2009 Shared Task on Event Extraction, BioNLP Shared Task 2011, BioNLP Shared Task 2013), BRAT format, BRAT standoff format, and similar.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3785\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3785\"}], \"name\": \"BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3785\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"BRAT format\", \"BRAT standoff format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3788\": {\"definition\": \"SQL (Structured Query Language) is the de-facto standard query language (format of queries) for querying and manipulating data in relational databases.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||SQL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3788\"}], \"name\": \"SQL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3788\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Structured Query Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3789\": {\"definition\": \"XQuery (XML Query) is a query language (format of queries) for querying and manipulating structured and unstructured data, usually in the form of XML, text, and with vendor-specific extensions for other data formats (JSON, binary, etc.).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||XQuery\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3789\"}], \"name\": \"XQuery\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3789\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"XML Query\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3790\": {\"definition\": \"SPARQL (SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language) is a semantic query language for querying and manipulating data stored in Resource Description Framework (RDF) format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||SPARQL\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3790\"}], \"name\": \"SPARQL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3790\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"SPARQL Protocol and RDF Query Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3812\": {\"definition\": \"The GEN file format contains genetic data and describes SNPs.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GEN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3812\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||GEN\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3812\"}], \"name\": \"GEN\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3812\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Genotype file format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3813\": {\"definition\": \"The SAMPLE file format contains information about each individual i.e. individual IDs, covariates, phenotypes and missing data proportions, from a GWAS study.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||SAMPLE file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3813\"}], \"name\": \"SAMPLE file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3813\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3814\": {\"definition\": \"SDF is one of a family of chemical-data file formats developed by MDL Information Systems; it is intended especially for structural information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||SDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3814\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||SDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3814\"}], \"name\": \"SDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3814\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3815\": {\"definition\": \"An MDL Molfile is a file format for holding information about the atoms, bonds, connectivity and coordinates of a molecule.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||Molfile\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3815\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Molfile\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3815\"}], \"name\": \"Molfile\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3815\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3816\": {\"definition\": \"Complete, portable representation of a SYBYL molecule. ASCII file which contains all the information needed to reconstruct a SYBYL molecule.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||Mol2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3816\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||Mol2\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3816\"}], \"name\": \"Mol2\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3816\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3817\": {\"definition\": \"format for the LaTeX document preparation system\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||latex\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3817\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||latex\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3817\"}], \"name\": \"latex\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3817\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"LaTeX format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3818\": {\"definition\": \"Tab-delimited text file format used by Eland - the read-mapping program distributed by Illumina with its sequencing analysis pipeline - which maps short Solexa sequence reads to the human reference genome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||ELAND format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3818\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||ELAND format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3818\"}], \"name\": \"ELAND format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3818\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ELAND\", \"eland\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3822\": {\"definition\": \"GML (Graph Modeling Language) is a text file format supporting network data with a very easy syntax. It is used by Graphlet, Pajek, yEd, LEDA and NetworkX.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3822\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network format||GML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2013||format_3822\"}], \"name\": \"GML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3822\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"GML format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3823\": {\"definition\": \"FASTG is a format for faithfully representing genome assemblies in the face of allelic polymorphism and assembly uncertainty.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||FASTG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3823\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence assembly format||Sequence assembly format (text)||FASTG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2055||format_2561||format_3823\"}], \"name\": \"FASTG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3823\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"FASTG assembly graph format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3827\": {\"definition\": \". proBED is an adaptation of BED (format_3003), which was extended to meet specific requirements entailed by proteomics data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||proBED\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3827\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence feature annotation format||Sequence annotation track format||proBED\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_1920||format_2919||format_3827\"}], \"name\": \"proBED\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3827\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3829\": {\"definition\": \"GenePix Results (GPR) text file format developed by Axon Instruments that is used to save GenePix Results data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GPR\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3829\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw microarray data format||GPR\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3828||format_3829\"}], \"name\": \"GPR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3829\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3859\": {\"definition\": \"A standardized file format for data exchange in mass spectrometry, initially developed for infrared spectrometry.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||JCAMP-DX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3859\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||JCAMP-DX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3859\"}], \"name\": \"JCAMP-DX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3859\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3877\": {\"definition\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||XYZ\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3877\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||XYZ\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3877\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||XYZ\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3877\"}], \"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3878\": {\"definition\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||mdcrd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3878\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||mdcrd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3878\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||mdcrd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3878\"}], \"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3880\": {\"definition\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GROMACS top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3880\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3880\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||GROMACS top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3880\"}], \"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3881\": {\"definition\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||AMBER top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3881\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||AMBER top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3881\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||AMBER top\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3881\"}], \"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3882\": {\"definition\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||PSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3882\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||PSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3882\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||PSF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3882\"}], \"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3883\": {\"definition\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||GROMACS itp\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3883\"}], \"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3886\": {\"definition\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||RST\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3886\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||RST\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3886\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||RST\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3886\"}], \"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3887\": {\"definition\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||CHARMM rtf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3887\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||CHARMM rtf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3887\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||CHARMM rtf\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3887\"}], \"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3888\": {\"definition\": \"AMBER frcmod (Force field Modification) is a file format to store any modification to the standard force field needed for a particular molecule to be properly represented in the simulation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||AMBER frcmod\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3888\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||AMBER frcmod\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3888\"}], \"name\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3888\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3889\": {\"definition\": \"AMBER Object File Format library files (OFF library files) store residue libraries (forcefield residue parameters).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||AMBER off\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3889\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||AMBER off\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3889\"}], \"name\": \"AMBER off\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3889\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"AMBER Object File Format\", \"AMBER lib\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3906\": {\"definition\": \"MReData is a text based data standard for processed NMR data. It is relying on SDF molecule data and allows to store assignments of NMR peaks to molecule features.  The NMR-extracted data (or \\\"NMReDATA\\\") includes: Chemical shift,scalar coupling, 2D correlation, assignment, etc.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||NMReDATA\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3906\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NMR data format||NMReDATA\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3824||format_3906\"}], \"name\": \"NMReDATA\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3906\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3909\": {\"definition\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3909\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical formula format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2035||format_3909\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BpForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3909\"}], \"name\": \"BpForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3909\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3910\": {\"definition\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||trr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3910\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Tertiary structure format||trr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2033||format_3910\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||trr\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3910\"}], \"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3916\": {\"definition\": \"The Matrix Market matrix (MTX) format stores numerical or pattern matrices in a dense (array format) or sparse (coordinate format) representation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||MTX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3916\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Gene expression report format||MTX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2058||format_3916\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||MTX\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_3916\"}], \"name\": \"MTX\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3916\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3951\": {\"definition\": \"BcForms is a format for abstractly describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes as a collection of subunits and crosslinks. Each subunit can be described with BpForms (http://edamontology.org/format_3909) or SMILES (http://edamontology.org/data_2301). BcForms uses an ontology of crosslinks to abstract the chemical details of crosslinks from the descriptions of complexes (see https://bpforms.org/crosslink.html).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Textual format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2330||format_3951\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Chemical data format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2030||format_3951\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein report format||BcForms\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2062||format_3951\"}], \"name\": \"BcForms\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3951\", \"e