ry format (binary)||HDF5||Loom\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3590||format_3913\"}], \"name\": \"Loom\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3913\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3591\": {\"definition\": \"A versatile bitmap format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||TIFF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3591\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||TIFF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3591\"}], \"name\": \"TIFF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3591\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"tiff\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3592\": {\"definition\": \"Standard bitmap storage format in the Microsoft Windows environment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||BMP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3592\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||BMP\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3592\"}], \"name\": \"BMP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3592\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"bmp\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3593\": {\"definition\": \"IM is a format used by LabEye and other applications based on the IFUNC image processing library.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||im\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3593\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||im\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3593\"}], \"name\": \"im\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3593\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3594\": {\"definition\": \"Photo CD format, which is the highest resolution format for images on a CD.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||pcd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3594\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pcd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3594\"}], \"name\": \"pcd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3594\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3595\": {\"definition\": \"PCX is an image file format that uses a simple form of run-length encoding. It is lossless.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||pcx\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3595\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pcx\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3595\"}], \"name\": \"pcx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3595\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3596\": {\"definition\": \"The PPM format is a lowest common denominator color image file format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||ppm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3596\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||ppm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3596\"}], \"name\": \"ppm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3596\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3597\": {\"definition\": \"PSD (Photoshop Document) is a proprietary file that allows the user to work with the images\' individual layers even after the file has been saved.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||psd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3597\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||psd\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3597\"}], \"name\": \"psd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3597\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3598\": {\"definition\": \"X BitMap is a plain text binary image format used by the X Window System used for storing cursor and icon bitmaps used in the X GUI.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||xbm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3598\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||xbm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3598\"}], \"name\": \"xbm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3598\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3599\": {\"definition\": \"X PixMap (XPM) is an image file format used by the X Window System, it is intended primarily for creating icon pixmaps, and supports transparent pixels.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||xpm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3599\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||xpm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3599\"}], \"name\": \"xpm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3599\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3600\": {\"definition\": \"RGB file format is the native raster graphics file format for Silicon Graphics workstations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||rgb\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3600\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||rgb\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3600\"}], \"name\": \"rgb\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3600\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3601\": {\"definition\": \"The PBM format is a lowest common denominator monochrome file format. It serves as the common language of a large family of bitmap image conversion filters.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||pbm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3601\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pbm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3601\"}], \"name\": \"pbm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3601\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3602\": {\"definition\": \"The PGM format is a lowest common denominator grayscale file format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||pgm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3602\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pgm\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3602\"}], \"name\": \"pgm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3602\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3603\": {\"definition\": \"PNG is a file format for image compression.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||PNG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3603\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||PNG\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3603\"}], \"name\": \"PNG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3603\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3605\": {\"definition\": \"Sun Raster is a raster graphics file format used on SunOS by Sun Microsystems\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||rast\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3605\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||rast\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3605\"}], \"name\": \"rast\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3605\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3615\": {\"definition\": \"Blocked GNU Zip format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||bgzip\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3615\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||bgzip\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3615\"}], \"name\": \"bgzip\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3615\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3616\": {\"definition\": \"TAB-delimited genome position file index format.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||tabix\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3616\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||tabix\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3616\"}], \"name\": \"tabix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3616\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3620\": {\"definition\": \"MS Excel spreadsheet format consisting of a set of XML documents stored in a ZIP-compressed file.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||xlsx\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3620\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||xlsx\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3620\"}], \"name\": \"xlsx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3620\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ObjTables\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3977\"}]}, \"format_3977\": {\"definition\": \"ObjTables is a toolkit for creating re-usable datasets that are both human and machine-readable, combining the ease of spreadsheets (e.g., Excel workbooks) with the rigor of schemas (classes, their attributes, the type of each attribute, and the possible relationships between instances of classes). ObjTables consists of a format for describing schemas for spreadsheets, numerous data types for science, a syntax for indicating the class and attribute represented by each table and column in a workbook, and software for using schemas to rigorously validate, merge, split, compare, and revision datasets.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||xlsx||ObjTables\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3620||format_3977\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||xlsx||ObjTables\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3620||format_3977\"}], \"name\": \"ObjTables\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3977\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3621\": {\"definition\": \"Data format used by the SQLite database.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||SQLite format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3621\"}], \"name\": \"SQLite format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3621\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3622\"}]}, \"format_3622\": {\"definition\": \"Data format used by the SQLite database conformant to the Gemini schema.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||SQLite format||Gemini SQLite format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3621||format_3622\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||Gemini SQLite format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3622\"}], \"name\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3622\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3624\": {\"definition\": \"An index of a genome database, indexed for use by the snpeff tool.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||snpeffdb\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3624\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||snpeffdb\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3624\"}], \"name\": \"snpeffdb\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3624\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3650\": {\"definition\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||netCDF\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3650\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrome