ntology.org/format_3993\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"stl\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3994\": {\"definition\": \"U3D (Universal 3D) is a compressed file format and data structure for 3D computer graphics. It contains 3D model information such as triangle meshes, lighting, shading, motion data, lines and points with color and structure.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||U3D\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3994\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||U3D\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3994\"}], \"name\": \"U3D\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3994\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Universal 3D\", \"Universal 3D format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3995\": {\"definition\": \"Bitmap image format used for storing textures.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||Texture file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3995\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Texture file format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3995\"}], \"name\": \"Texture file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3995\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3997\": {\"definition\": \"A digital multimedia container format most commonly used to store video and audio.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Binary format||MPEG-4\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2333||format_3997\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||MPEG-4\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3997\"}], \"name\": \"MPEG-4\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3997\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"MP4\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_4001\": {\"definition\": \"An open file format from the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative (NIfTI) commonly used to store brain imaging data obtained using Magneti