: \"snpeffdb\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3624\"}, {\"name\": \"Tabix index file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3700\"}]}, \"format_3507\": {\"definition\": \"Format of documents including word processor, spreadsheet and presentation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507\"}], \"name\": \"Document format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3507\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"xls\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3468\"}, {\"name\": \"docx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3506\"}, {\"name\": \"PDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3508\"}, {\"name\": \"xlsx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3620\"}, {\"name\": \"latex\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3817\"}]}, \"format_3547\": {\"definition\": \"Format used for images and image metadata.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547\"}], \"name\": \"Image format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3547\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"DICOM format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3548\"}, {\"name\": \"nii\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3549\"}, {\"name\": \"mhd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3550\"}, {\"name\": \"nrrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3551\"}, {\"name\": \"JPG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3579\"}, {\"name\": \"TIFF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3591\"}, {\"name\": \"BMP\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3592\"}, {\"name\": \"im\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3593\"}, {\"name\": \"pcd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3594\"}, {\"name\": \"pcx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3595\"}, {\"name\": \"ppm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3596\"}, {\"name\": \"psd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3597\"}, {\"name\": \"xbm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3598\"}, {\"name\": \"xpm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3599\"}, {\"name\": \"rgb\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3600\"}, {\"name\": \"pbm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3601\"}, {\"name\": \"pgm\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3602\"}, {\"name\": \"PNG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3603\"}, {\"name\": \"SVG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3604\"}, {\"name\": \"rast\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3605\"}, {\"name\": \"bgzip\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3615\"}, {\"name\": \"tabix\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3616\"}, {\"name\": \"OME-TIFF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3727\"}, {\"name\": \"pptx\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3838\"}, {\"name\": \"Vega\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3969\"}, {\"name\": \"Vega-lite\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3970\"}, {\"name\": \"WMV\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3986\"}, {\"name\": \"LSM\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3988\"}, {\"name\": \"AVI\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3990\"}, {\"name\": \"Stereolithography format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3993\"}, {\"name\": \"U3D\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3994\"}, {\"name\": \"Texture file format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3995\"}, {\"name\": \"MPEG-4\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3997\"}, {\"name\": \"NIFTI format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_4001\"}]}, \"format_3969\": {\"definition\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Vega\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3969\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||JSON||Vega\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3969\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||Vega\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3969\"}], \"name\": \"Vega\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3969\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3970\": {\"definition\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Vega-lite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3970\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||JSON||Vega-lite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3970\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||Vega-lite\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3970\"}], \"name\": \"Vega-lite\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3970\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3606\": {\"definition\": \"Textual report format for sequence quality for reports from sequencing machines.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3606\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"qual\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3607\"}]}, \"format_3617\": {\"definition\": \"Data format for graph data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Graph format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3617\"}], \"name\": \"Graph format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3617\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"xgmml\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3618\"}, {\"name\": \"K-mer countgraph\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3665\"}]}, \"format_3618\": {\"definition\": \"XML-based format used to store graph descriptions within Galaxy.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Graph format||xgmml\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3617||format_3618\"}], \"name\": \"xgmml\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3618\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3706\": {\"definition\": \"Data format for biodiversity data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706\"}], \"name\": \"Biodiversity data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3706\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"ABCD format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3708\"}, {\"name\": \"BIOM format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3746\"}, {\"name\": \"MCPD\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3777\"}]}, \"format_3708\": {\"definition\": \"Exchange format of the Access to Biological Collections Data (ABCD) Schema; a standard for the access to and exchange of data about specimens and observations (primary biodiversity data).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format||ABCD format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706||format_3708\"}], \"name\": \"ABCD format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3708\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"ABCD\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3748\": {\"definition\": \"A linked data format enables publishing structured data as linked data (Linked Data), so that the data can be interlinked and become more useful through semantic queries.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748\"}], \"name\": \"Linked data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3748\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"RDF format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_2376\"}, {\"name\": \"JSON-LD\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3749\"}]}, \"format_3780\": {\"definition\": \"Data format of an annotated text, e.g. with recognised entities, concepts, and relations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780\"}], \"name\": \"Annotated text format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3780\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"OSCAR format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_1741\"}, {\"name\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3781\"}, {\"name\": \"BioC\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3782\"}, {\"name\": \"PubTator format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3783\"}, {\"name\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3784\"}, {\"name\": \"BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3785\"}]}, \"format_3781\": {\"definition\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||PubAnnotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3781\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||JSON||PubAnnotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3781\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||PubAnnotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3781\"}], \"name\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3781\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3787\": {\"definition\": \"A query language (format) for structured database queries.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Query language\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3787\"}], \"name\": \"Query language\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3787\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Query format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3824\": {\"definition\": \"Data format for raw data from a nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy experiment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NMR data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3824\"}], \"name\": \"NMR data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3824\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"NMR peak assignment data\", \"NMR processed data format\", \"NMR raw data format\", \"Processed NMR data format\", \"Raw NMR data format\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"nmrML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3825\"}, {\"name\": \"NMReDATA\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3906\"}]}, \"format_3828\": {\"definition\": \"Data format for raw microarray data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw microarray data format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3828\"}], \"name\": \"Raw microarray data format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3828\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Microarray data format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"GPR\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3829\"}]}, \"format_3841\": {\"definition\": \"Data format used in Natural Language Processing.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841\"}], \"name\": \"NLP format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3841\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Natural Language Processing format\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"NLP annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3862\"}]}, \"format_3862\": {\"definition\": \"An NLP format used for annotated textual documents.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format||NLP annotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841||format_3862\"}], \"name\": \"NLP annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3862\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"NLP corpus format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3863\"}]}, \"format_3863\": {\"definition\": \"NLP format used by a specific type of corpus (collection of texts).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format||NLP annotation format||NLP corpus format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841||format_3862||format_3863\"}], \"name\": \"NLP corpus format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3863\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"format_3865\": {\"definition\": \"A \\\"placeholder\\\" concept for formats of annotated RNA data, including e.g. microRNA and RNA-Seq data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||RNA annotation format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3865\"}], \"name\": \"RNA annotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3865\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"miRNA data format\", \"microRNA data format\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"mirGFF3\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3864\"}]}, \"format_3866\": {\"definition\": \"File format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866\"}], \"name\": \"Trajectory format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3866\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"CG trajectory formats\", \"MD trajectory formats\", \"NA trajectory formats\", \"Protein trajectory formats\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"Trajectory format (binary)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3867\"}, {\"name\": \"Trajectory format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3868\"}]}, \"format_3867\": {\"definition\": \"Binary file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867\"}], \"name\": \"Trajectory format (binary)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3867\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"HDF5\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3590\"}, {\"name\": \"netCDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3650\"}, {\"name\": \"HDF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3873\"}, {\"name\": \"PCAzip\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3874\"}, {\"name\": \"XTC\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3875\"}, {\"name\": \"TNG\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3876\"}, {\"name\": \"BinPos\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3885\"}]}, \"format_3868\": {\"definition\": \"Textual file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868\"}], \"name\": \"Trajectory format (text)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3868\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"XYZ\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3877\"}, {\"name\": \"mdcrd\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3878\"}, {\"name\": \"RST\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3886\"}, {\"name\": \"trr\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3910\"}]}, \"format_3879\": {\"definition\": \"Format of topology files; containing the static information of a structure molecular system that is needed for a molecular simulation.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879\"}], \"name\": \"Topology format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3879\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [\"CG topology format\", \"MD topology format\", \"NA topology format\", \"Protein topology format\"], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"GROMACS top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3880\"}, {\"name\": \"AMBER top\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3881\"}, {\"name\": \"PSF\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3882\"}, {\"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3887\"}]}, \"format_3884\": {\"definition\": \"Format of force field parameter files, which store the set of parameters (charges, masses, radii, bond lengths, bond dihedrals, etc.) that are essential for the proper description and simulation of a molecular system.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884\"}], \"name\": \"FF parameter format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3884\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3883\"}, {\"name\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3888\"}, {\"name\": \"AMBER off\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3889\"}]}, \"format_3464\": {\"definition\": \"JavaScript Object Notation format; a lightweight, text-based format to represent tree-structured data using key-value pairs.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||JSON\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3464\"}, {\"name\": \"Format||YAML||JSON\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464\"}], \"name\": \"JSON\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3464\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"JSON-LD\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3749\"}, {\"name\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3772\"}, {\"name\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3774\"}, {\"name\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3781\"}, {\"name\": \"Vega\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3969\"}, {\"name\": \"Vega-lite\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3970\"}]}, \"format_3750\": {\"definition\": \"YAML (YAML Ain\'t Markup Language) is a human-readable tree-structured data serialisation language.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Format||YAML\", \"key\": \"format_1915||format_3750\"}], \"name\": \"YAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3750\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"YAML Ain\'t Markup Language\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": [{\"name\": \"JSON\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3464\"}, {\"name\": \"BioYAML\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3773\"}, {\"name\": \"CWL\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/format_3857\"}]}}','2025-08-27 12:52:46.779166');
INSERT INTO `elixir_ontology` VALUES (43,'min_EDAM_Format','{\"t\": \"Format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1915\"}, \"d\": \"A defined way or layout of representing and structuring data in a computer file, blob, string, message, or elsewhere. The main focus in EDAM lies on formats as means of structuring data exchanged between different tools or resources. The serialisation, compression, or encoding of concrete data formats/models is not in scope of EDAM. Format \'is format of\' Data.\", \"es\": [\"Exchange format\", \"Data format\"], \"ns\": [\"File format\"], \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Textual format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2330\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"SMILES\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1196\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"smarts\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1200\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"SMILES ARbitrary Target Specification (SMARTS) format for chemical structure specification, which is a subset of the SMILES line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified in Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System (SMILES) line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"InChI\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1197\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified in IUPAC International Chemical Identifier (InChI) line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mf\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1198\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified by Molecular Formula (MF), including a count of each element in a compound.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"InChIKey\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1199\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The InChIKey (hashed InChI) is a fixed length (25 character) condensed digital representation of an InChI chemical s