tain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3883\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RST\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3886\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3887\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"trr\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3910\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for a molecular tertiary structure.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Chemical formula format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2035\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"SMILES\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1196\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"smarts\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1200\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"SMILES ARbitrary Target Specification (SMARTS) format for chemical structure specification, which is a subset of the SMILES line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified in Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System (SMILES) line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"InChI\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1197\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified in IUPAC International Chemical Identifier (InChI) line notation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mf\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1198\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Chemical structure specified by Molecular Formula (MF), including a count of each element in a compound.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"InChIKey\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1199\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The InChIKey (hashed InChI) is a fixed length (25 character) condensed digital representation of an InChI chemical structure specification. It uniquely identifies a chemical compound.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BpForms\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3909\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Text format of a chemical formula.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylogenetic character data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2036\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Phylogenetic continuous quantitative character format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2037\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1430\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PHYLIP file format for continuous quantitative character data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1432\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PHYLIP file format for phylogenetics character frequency data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of phylogenetic continuous quantitative character data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylogenetic discrete states format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2038\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1433\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of PHYLIP discrete states data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of phylogenetic discrete states data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (cliques) format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2039\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1434\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of PHYLIP cliques data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of phylogenetic cliques data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (invariants) format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2040\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of phylogenetic invariants data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of raw (unplotted) phylogenetic data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Phylogenetic tree report (tree distances) format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2049\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1445\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for distances, such as Branch Score distance, between two or more phylogenetic trees as used by the Phylip package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for phylogenetic tree distance data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Protein family report format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2052\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for reports on a protein family.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Protein interaction format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2054\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"STRING entry format (XML)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2304\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Entry format (XML) for the STRING database of protein interaction.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PSI MI XML (MIF)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3158\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"PSI-PAR\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3243\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Protein affinity format (PSI-PAR), standardised by HUPO PSI MI. It is compatible with PSI MI XML (MIF) and uses the same XML Schema.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"MIF\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"XML Molecular Interaction Format (MIF), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PSI MI TAB (MITAB)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3242\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Tabular Molecular Interaction format (MITAB), standardised by HUPO PSI MI.\", \"hi\": [