SD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BpForms\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3909\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"msh\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3911\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Mash sketch\", \"min-hash sketch\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Mash sketch is a format for sequence / sequence checksum information. To make a sketch, each k-mer in a sequence is hashed, which creates a pseudo-random identifier. By sorting these hashes, a small subset from the top of the sorted list can represent the entire sequence.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Docker image format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3973\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A Docker image is a file, comprised of multiple layers, that is used to execute code in a Docker container. An image is essentially built from the instructions for a complete and executable version of an application, which relies on the host OS kernel.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of a raw molecular sequence (i.e. the alphabet used).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Bibliographic reference format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2848\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"PubMed citation\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1734\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of bibliographic reference as used by the PubMed database.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Medline Display Format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1735\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for abstracts of scientific articles from the Medline database.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CiteXplore-core\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1736\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"CiteXplore \'core\' citation format including title, journal, authors and abstract.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CiteXplore-all\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1737\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"CiteXplore \'all\' citation format includes all known details such as Mesh terms and cross-references.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PubMed XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3848\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"MEDLINE XML\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"XML format for collected entries from biobliographic databases MEDLINE and PubMed.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of a bibliographic reference.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Sequence variation annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2921\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"VCF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3016\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Variant Call Format (VCF) for sequence variation (indels, polymorphisms, structural variation).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GVF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3019\"}, \"ch\": [