alization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega-lite\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3970\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"WMV\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3986\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Windows Media Video format\", \"Windows movie file format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The proprietary native video format of various Microsoft programs such as Windows Media Player.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"LSM\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3988\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Zeiss\' proprietary image format based on TIFF.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"AVI\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3990\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Audio Video Interleaved\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Audio Video Interleaved (AVI) format is a multimedia container format for AVI files, that allows synchronous audio-with-video playback.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Stereolithography format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3993\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"stl\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"STL is a file format native to the stereolithography CAD software created by 3D Systems.  The format is used to save and share surface-rendered 3D images and also for 3D printing.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"U3D\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3994\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Universal 3D\", \"Universal 3D format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"U3D (Universal 3D) is a compressed file format and data structure for 3D computer graphics. It contains 3D model information such as triangle meshes, lighting, shading, motion data, lines and points with color and structure.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Texture file format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3995\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Bitmap image format used for storing textures.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MPEG-4\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3997\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"MP4\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A digital multimedia container format most commonly used to store video and audio.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"NIFTI format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_4001\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"NIFTI\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"An open file format from the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative (NIfTI) commonly used to store brain imaging data obtained using Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) methods.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format used for images and image metadata.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3606\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"qual\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3607\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"qualsolexa\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3608\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) for Solexa/Illumina 1.0 format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qualillumina\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3609\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no 