ctivity and animation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pepXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3655\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Open data format for the storage, exchange, and processing of peptide sequence assignments of MS/MS scans, intended to provide a common data output format for many different MS/MS search engines and subsequent peptide-level analyses.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GPML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3657\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Graphical Pathway Markup Language (GPML) is an XML format used for exchanging biological pathways.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"imzML metadata file\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3682\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"imzML metadata is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging metadata.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qcML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3683\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3684\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SED-ML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3685\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Simulation Experiment Description Markup Language (SED-ML) is an XML format for encoding simulation setups, according to the MIASE (Minimum Information About a Simulation Experiment) requirements.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BCML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3689\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Biological Connection Markup Language (BCML) is an XML format for biological pathways.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BDML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3690\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Biological Dynamics Markup Language (BDML) is an XML format for quantitative data describing biological dynamics.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SBGN-ML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3692\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"SBGN-ML is an XML format for Systems Biology Graphical Notation (SBGN) diagrams of biological pathways or networks.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3711\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Output format used by X! series search engines that is based on the XML language BIOML.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SBOL\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3725\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Synthetic Biology Open Language (SBOL) is an XML format for the specification and exchange of biological design information in synthetic biology.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PMML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3726\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PMML uses XML to represent mining models. The structure of the models is described by an XML Schema.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"protXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3747\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format for storage, exchange, and processing of protein identifications created from ms/ms-derived peptide sequence data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"idXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3764\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \