ical values.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Protein domain classification format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3097\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Raw SCOP domain classification format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3098\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of raw SCOP domain classification data files.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Raw CATH domain classification format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3099\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of raw CATH domain classification data files.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CATH domain report format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3100\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of summary of domain classification information for a CATH domain.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"InterProScan XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3846\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Output xml file from the InterProScan sequence analysis application.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of data concerning the classification of the sequences and/or structures of protein structural domain(s).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Biological pathway or network report format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3166\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"SBRML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3155\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Systems Biology Result Markup Language (SBRML), the standard XML format for simulated or calculated results (e.g. trajectories) of systems biology models.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CopasiML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3239\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"CopasiML, the native format of COPASI.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for a report of information derived from a biological pathway or network.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Experiment annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3167\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Microarray experiment data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2056\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"affymetrix-exp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1641\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Affymetrix experimental conditions data file format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Affymetrix data file format for information about experimental conditions and protocols.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for information about a microarray experimental per se (not the data generated from that experiment).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GCDML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3163\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GCDML XML format for genome and metagenome metadata according to MIGS/MIMS/MIMARKS information standards, standardised by the Genomic Standards Consortium (GSC).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GelML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3249\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GelML is the format for describing the process of gel electrophoresis, standardised by HUPO PSI PS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"spML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3250\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"spML is the format for describing proteomics sample processing, other than using gels, prior to mass spectrometric protein identification, standardised by HUPO PSI PS. It may also be applicable for metabolomics.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qcML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3683\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3684\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SED-ML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3685\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Simulation Experiment Description Markup Language (SED-ML) is an XML format for encoding simulation setups, according to the MIASE (Minimum Information About a Simulation Experiment) requirements.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3686\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Open Modeling EXchange format (OMEX) is a ZIPped format for encapsulating all information necessary for a modeling and simulation project in systems biology.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3687\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The Investigation / Study / Assay (ISA) tab-delimited (TAB) format incorporates metadata from\\nexperiments employing a combination of technologies.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for annotation on a laboratory experiment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Mass spectrometry data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3245\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"mzML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3244\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"mzML format for raw spectrometer output data, standardised by HUPO PSI MSS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"TraML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3246\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"TraML (Transition Markup Language) is the format for mass spectrometry transitions, standardised by HUPO PSI MSS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mzIdentML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3247\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"mzIdentML is the exchange format for peptides and proteins identified from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of proteomics search engines.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mzQuantML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3248\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"mzQuantML is the format for quantitation values associated with peptides, proteins and small molecules from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of quantitation software for proteomics.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"netCDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3650\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"ANDI-MS\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MGF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3651\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Mascot Generic Format.  Encodes multiple MS/MS spectra in a single file.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"dta\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3652\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Spectral data format file where each spectrum is written to a separate file.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pkl\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3653\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Spectral data file similar to dta.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mzXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3654\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Common file format for proteomics mass spectrometric data developed at the Seattle Proteome Center/Institute for Systems Biology.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pepXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3655\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Open data format for the storage, exchange, and processing of peptide sequence assignments of MS/MS scans, intended to provide a common data output format for many different MS/MS search engines and subsequent peptide-level analyses.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mzTab\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3681\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"mzTab is a tab-delimited format for mass spectrometry-based proteomics and metabolomics results.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"imzML metadata file\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3682\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"imzML metadata is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging metadata.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qcML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3683\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3684\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MSF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3702\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Magellan storage file format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Proprietary mass-spectrometry format of Thermo Scientific\'s ProteomeDiscoverer software.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"WIFF format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3710\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"wiff\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Mass spectrum file format from QSTAR and QTRAP instruments (ABI/Sciex).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3711\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Output format used by X! series search engines that is based on the XML language BIOML.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Thermo RAW\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3712\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Proprietary file format for mass spectrometry data from Thermo Scientific.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Mascot .dat file\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3713\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"\\\"Raw\\\" result file from Mascot database search.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MaxQuant APL peaklist format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3714\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"MaxQuant APL\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of peak list files from Andromeda search engine (MaxQuant) that consist of arbitrarily many spectra.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"protXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3747\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format for storage, exchange, and processing of protein identifications created from ms/ms-derived peptide sequence data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SEQUEST .out file\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3758\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"\\\"Raw\\\" result file from SEQUEST database search.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"idXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3764\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"XML file format for files containing information about peptide identifications from mass spectrometry data analysis carried out with OpenMS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"consensusXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3832\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"OpenMS format for grouping features in one map or across several maps.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"featureXML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3833\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"OpenMS format for quantitation results (LC/MS features).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mzData\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3834\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Now deprecated data format of the HUPO Proteomics Standards Initiative.  Replaced by mzML (format_3244).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"TIDE TXT\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3835\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format supported by the Tide tool for identifying peptides from tandem mass spectra.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"ibd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3839\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"ibd is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Waters RAW\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3858\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Proprietary file format for mass spectrometry data from Waters.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JCAMP-DX\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3859\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A standardized file format for data exchange in mass spectrometry, initially developed for infrared spectrometry.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format for mass pectra and derived data, include peptide sequences etc.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Individual genetic data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3287\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"PED/MAP\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3288\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"MAP\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3285\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Plink MAP\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The MAP file describes SNPs and is used by the Plink package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PED\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3286\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Plink PED\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The PED file describes individuals and genetic data and is used by the Plink package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Plink PED/MAP\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The PED/MAP file describes data used by the Plink package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for a metadata on an individual and their genetic data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Data index format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3326\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"BAI\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3327\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BAM indexing format\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"ebwt\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3484\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Bowtie index format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Bowtie format for indexed reference genome for \\\"small\\\" genomes.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"ebwtl\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3491\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Bowtie long index format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Bowtie format for indexed reference genome for \\\"large\\\" genomes.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"snpeffdb\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3624\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"An index of a genome database, indexed for use by the snpeff tool.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Tabix index file format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3700\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Index file format used by the samtools package to index TAB-delimited genome position files.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of a data index of some type.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Document format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3507\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"xls\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3468\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Microsoft Excel format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Microsoft Excel spreadsheet format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"docx\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3506\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Microsoft Word format\", \"doc\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Microsoft Word format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3508\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Portable Document Format\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"xlsx\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3620\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"ObjTables\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3977\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"ObjTables is a toolkit for creating re-usable datasets that are both human and machine-readable, combining the ease of spreadsheets (e.g., Excel workbooks) with the rigor of schemas (classes, their attributes, the type of each attribute, and the possible relationships between instances of classes). ObjTables consists of a format for describing schemas for spreadsheets, numerous data types for science, a syntax for indicating the class and attribute represented by each table and column in a workbook, and software for using schemas to rigorously validate, merge, split, compare, and revision datasets.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"MS Excel spreadsheet format consisting of a set of XML documents stored in a ZIP-compressed file.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"latex\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3817\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"LaTeX format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"format for the LaTeX document preparation system\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of documents including word processor, spreadsheet and presentation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Image format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3547\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"DICOM format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3548\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Medical image format corresponding to the Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) standard.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"nii\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3549\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"NIfTI-1 format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Medical image and metadata format of the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mhd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3550\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Metalmage format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Text-based tagged file format for medical images generated using the MetaImage software package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"nrrd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3551\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Nearly Raw Rasta Data format designed to support scientific visualisation and image processing involving N-dimensional raster data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JPG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3579\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"JPEG\", \"jpeg\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Joint Picture Group file format for lossy graphics file.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"TIFF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3591\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"tiff\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A versatile bitmap format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BMP\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3592\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"bmp\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Standard bitmap storage format in the Microsoft Windows environment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"im\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3593\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"IM is a format used by LabEye and other applications based on the IFUNC image processing library.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pcd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3594\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Photo CD format, which is the highest resolution format for images on a CD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pcx\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3595\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PCX is an image file format that uses a simple form of run-length encoding. It is lossless.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"ppm\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3596\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The PPM format is a lowest common denominator color image file format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"psd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3597\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PSD (Photoshop Document) is a proprietary file that allows the user to work with the images\' individual layers even after the file has been saved.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"xbm\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3598\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"X BitMap is a plain text binary image format used by the X Window System used for storing cursor and icon bitmaps used in the X GUI.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"xpm\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3599\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"X PixMap (XPM) is an image file format used by the X Window System, it is intended primarily for creating icon pixmaps, and supports transparent pixels.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"rgb\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3600\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"RGB file format is the native raster graphics file format for Silicon Graphics workstations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pbm\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3601\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The PBM format is a lowest common denominator monochrome file format. It serves as the common language of a large family of bitmap image conversion filters.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pgm\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3602\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The PGM format is a lowest common denominator grayscale file format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PNG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3603\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PNG is a file format for image compression.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"SVG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3604\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Scalable Vector Graphics\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) is an XML-based vector image format for two-dimensional graphics with support for interactivity and animation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"rast\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3605\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Sun Raster is a raster graphics file format used on SunOS by Sun Microsystems\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"bgzip\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3615\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Blocked GNU Zip format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"tabix\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3616\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"TAB-delimited genome position file index format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"OME-TIFF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3727\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Image file format used by the Open Microscopy Environment (OME).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"pptx\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3838\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Microsoft Powerpoint format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3969\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega-lite\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3970\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"WMV\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3986\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Windows Media Video format\", \"Windows movie file format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The proprietary native video format of various Microsoft programs such as Windows Media Player.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"LSM\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3988\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Zeiss\' proprietary image format based on TIFF.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"AVI\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3990\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Audio Video Interleaved\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Audio Video Interleaved (AVI) format is a multimedia container format for AVI files, that allows synchronous audio-with-video playback.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Stereolithography format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3993\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"stl\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"STL is a file format native to the stereolithography CAD software created by 3D Systems.  The format is used to save and share surface-rendered 3D images and also for 3D printing.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"U3D\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3994\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Universal 3D\", \"Universal 3D format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"U3D (Universal 3D) is a compressed file format and data structure for 3D computer graphics. It contains 3D model information such as triangle meshes, lighting, shading, motion data, lines and points with color and structure.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Texture file format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3995\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Bitmap image format used for storing textures.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MPEG-4\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3997\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"MP4\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A digital multimedia container format most commonly used to store video and audio.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"NIFTI format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_4001\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"NIFTI\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"An open file format from the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative (NIfTI) commonly used to store brain imaging data obtained using Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) methods.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format used for images and image metadata.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3606\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"qual\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3607\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"qualsolexa\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3608\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) for Solexa/Illumina 1.0 format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qualillumina\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3609\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) from Illumina 1.5 and before Illumina 1.8.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qualsolid\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3610\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) for SOLiD data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"qual454\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3611\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) from 454 sequencers.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Textual report format for sequence quality for reports from sequencing machines.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Graph format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3617\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"xgmml\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3618\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"XML-based format used to store graph descriptions within Galaxy.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"K-mer countgraph\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3665\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A list of k-mers and their occurences in a dataset. Can also be used as an implicit De Bruijn graph.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for graph data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Biodiversity data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3706\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"ABCD format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3708\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"ABCD\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Exchange format of the Access to Biological Collections Data (ABCD) Schema; a standard for the access to and exchange of data about specimens and observations (primary biodiversity data).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BIOM format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3746\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BIological Observation Matrix format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The BIological Observation Matrix (BIOM) is a format for representing biological sample by observation contingency tables in broad areas of comparative omics. The primary use of this format is to represent OTU tables and metagenome tables.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"MCPD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3777\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Bioversity MCPD\", \"FAO MCPD\", \"MCPD format\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors format\"], \"ns\": [\"IPGRI MCPD\", \"MCPD V.1\", \"MCPD V.2\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The FAO/Bioversity/IPGRI Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors (MCPD) is an international standard format for exchange of germplasm information.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for biodiversity data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Linked data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3748\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"RDF format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2376\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"OWL format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2197\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3252\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A human-readable encoding for the Web Ontology Language (OWL).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3253\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A syntax for writing OWL class expressions.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"OWL/XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3262\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [\"OWL\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"OWL ontology XML serialisation format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Web Ontology Language (OWL) model.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Turtle\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3255\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The Terse RDF Triple Language (Turtle) is a human-friendly serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"N-Triples\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3256\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A plain text serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs, and a subset of the Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Notation3\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3257\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"N3\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A shorthand non-XML serialisation of Resource Description Framework model, designed with human-readability in mind.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RDF/XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3261\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Resource Description Framework (RDF) XML format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JSON-LD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3749\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3771\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"UniProt RDF\", \"UniProt RDF format\", \"UniProtKB RDF format\"], \"ns\": [\"UniProt RDF/XML\", \"UniProt RDF/XML format\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML format\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"UniProtKB RDF sequence features format is an RDF format available for downloading UniProt entries (in RDF/XML).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"N-Quads\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3956\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. It includes information about the graph each triple belongs to.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Resource Description Framework format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Resource Description Framework (RDF) model.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JSON-LD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3749\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A linked data format enables publishing structured data as linked data (Linked Data), so that the data can be interlinked and become more useful through semantic queries.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Annotated text format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3780\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"OSCAR format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_1741\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"OSCAR format of annotated chemical text.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3781\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioC\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3782\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioC is a standardised XML format for sharing and integrating text data and annotations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PubTator format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3783\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Native textual export format of annotated scientific text from PubTator.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3785\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BRAT format\", \"BRAT standoff format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A family of similar formats of text annotation, used by BRAT and other tools, known as BioNLP Shared Task format (BioNLP 2009 Shared Task on Event Extraction, BioNLP Shared Task 2011, BioNLP Shared Task 2013), BRAT format, BRAT standoff format, and similar.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format of an annotated text, e.g. with recognised entities, concepts, and relations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Query language\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3787\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Query format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A query language (format) for structured database queries.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"NMR data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3824\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"nmrML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3825\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"nmrML is an MSI supported XML-based open access format for metabolomics NMR raw and processed spectral data. It is accompanies by an nmrCV (controlled vocabulary) to allow ontology-based annotations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"NMReDATA\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3906\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"MReData is a text based data standard for processed NMR data. It is relying on SDF molecule data and allows to store assignments of NMR peaks to molecule features.  The NMR-extracted data (or \\\"NMReDATA\\\") includes: Chemical shift,scalar coupling, 2D correlation, assignment, etc.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy data format\"], \"ns\": [\"NMR peak assignment data\", \"NMR processed data format\", \"NMR raw data format\", \"Processed NMR data format\", \"Raw NMR data format\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for raw data from a nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy experiment.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Raw microarray data format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3828\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"GPR\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3829\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GenePix Results (GPR) text file format developed by Axon Instruments that is used to save GenePix Results data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Microarray data format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format for raw microarray data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"NLP format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3841\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"NLP annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3862\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"NLP corpus format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3863\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"NLP format used by a specific type of corpus (collection of texts).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"An NLP format used for annotated textual documents.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Natural Language Processing format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Data format used in Natural Language Processing.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RNA annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3865\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"mirGFF3\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3864\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"miRTop format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"mirGFF3 is a common format for microRNA data resulting from small-RNA RNA-Seq workflows.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [\"miRNA data format\", \"microRNA data format\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A \\\"placeholder\\\" concept for formats of annotated RNA data, including e.g. microRNA and RNA-Seq data.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Trajectory format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3866\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Trajectory format (binary)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3867\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"HDF5\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3590\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Loom\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3913\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The Loom file format is based on HDF5, a standard for storing large numerical datasets. The Loom format is designed to efficiently hold large omics datasets. Typically, such data takes the form of a large matrix of numbers, along with metadata for the rows and columns.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"h5\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"HDF5 is a data model, library, and file format for storing and managing data, based on Hierarchical Data Format (HDF).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"netCDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3650\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"ANDI-MS\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"HDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3873\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"HDF is the name of a set of file formats and libraries designed to store and organize large amounts of numerical data, originally developed at the National Center for Supercomputing Applications at the University of Illinois.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PCAzip\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3874\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"PCAZip format is a binary compressed file to store atom coordinates based on Essential Dynamics (ED) and Principal Component Analysis (PCA).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"XTC\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3875\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Portable binary format for trajectories produced by GROMACS package.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"TNG\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3876\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Trajectory Next Generation format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Trajectory Next Generation (TNG) is a format for storage of molecular simulation data. It is designed and implemented by the GROMACS development group, and it is called to be the substitute of the XTC format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BinPos\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3885\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Scripps Research Institute BinPos\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Scripps Research Institute BinPos format is a binary formatted file to store atom coordinates.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Binary file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Trajectory format (text)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3868\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"XYZ\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3877\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"mdcrd\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3878\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RST\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3886\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"trr\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3910\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Textual file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [\"CG trajectory formats\", \"MD trajectory formats\", \"NA trajectory formats\", \"Protein trajectory formats\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"File format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Topology format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3879\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"GROMACS top\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3880\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"AMBER top\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3881\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PSF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3882\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3883\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3887\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [\"CG topology format\", \"MD topology format\", \"NA topology format\", \"Protein topology format\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of topology files; containing the static information of a structure molecular system that is needed for a molecular simulation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"FF parameter format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3884\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3883\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3888\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER frcmod (Force field Modification) is a file format to store any modification to the standard force field needed for a particular molecule to be properly represented in the simulation.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"AMBER off\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3889\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"AMBER Object File Format\", \"AMBER lib\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"AMBER Object File Format library files (OFF library files) store residue libraries (forcefield residue parameters).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Format of force field parameter files, which store the set of parameters (charges, masses, radii, bond lengths, bond dihedrals, etc.) that are essential for the proper description and simulation of a molecular system.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Format (typed)\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A placeholder concept for visual navigation by dividing data formats by the content of the data that is represented.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RDF format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2376\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"OWL format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_2197\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3252\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A human-readable encoding for the Web Ontology Language (OWL).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3253\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A syntax for writing OWL class expressions.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"OWL/XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3262\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [\"OWL\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"OWL ontology XML serialisation format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Web Ontology Language (OWL) model.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Turtle\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3255\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"The Terse RDF Triple Language (Turtle) is a human-friendly serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"N-Triples\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3256\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A plain text serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs, and a subset of the Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Notation3\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3257\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"N3\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A shorthand non-XML serialisation of Resource Description Framework model, designed with human-readability in mind.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"RDF/XML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3261\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Resource Description Framework (RDF) XML format.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JSON-LD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3749\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3771\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"UniProt RDF\", \"UniProt RDF format\", \"UniProtKB RDF format\"], \"ns\": [\"UniProt RDF/XML\", \"UniProt RDF/XML format\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML format\"], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"UniProtKB RDF sequence features format is an RDF format available for downloading UniProt entries (in RDF/XML).\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"N-Quads\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3956\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. It includes information about the graph each triple belongs to.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"Resource Description Framework format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Resource Description Framework (RDF) model.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"JSON\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3464\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"JSON-LD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3749\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3772\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3774\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3781\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3969\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega-lite\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3970\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JavaScript Object Notation format; a lightweight, text-based format to represent tree-structured data using key-value pairs.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"YAML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3750\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"JSON\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3464\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"JSON-LD\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3749\"}, \"ch\": [{\"t\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3784\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3772\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3774\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3781\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3969\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"Vega-lite\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3970\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"JavaScript Object Notation format; a lightweight, text-based format to represent tree-structured data using key-value pairs.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"BioYAML\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3773\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, {\"t\": \"CWL\", \"data\": {\"uri\": \"format_3857\"}, \"ch\": [], \"es\": [\"Common Workflow Language\", \"CommonWL\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"Common Workflow Language (CWL) format for description of command-line tools and workflows.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}], \"es\": [\"YAML Ain\'t Markup Language\"], \"ns\": [], \"rb\": [], \"co\": [], \"d\": \"YAML (YAML Ain\'t Markup Language) is a human-readable tree-structured data serialisation language.\", \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}]}','2025-08-27 12:52:46.813063');
INSERT INTO `elixir_ontology` VALUES (45,'min_flat_EDAM_Format','[{\"d\": \"A defined way or layout of representing and structuring data in a computer file, blob, string, message, or elsewhere. The main focus in EDAM lies on formats as means of structuring data exchanged between different tools or resources. The serialisation, compression, or encoding of concrete data formats/models is not in scope of EDAM. Format \'is format of\' Data.\", \"n\": \"Format\", \"ns\": [\"File format\"], \"u\": \"format_1915\", \"es\": [\"Exchange format\", \"Data format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Textual format\", \"u\": \"format_2330\"}, {\"n\": \"HTML\", \"u\": \"format_2331\"}, {\"n\": \"XML\", \"u\": \"format_2332\"}, {\"n\": \"Binary format\", \"u\": \"format_2333\"}, {\"n\": \"Format (by type of data)\", \"u\": \"format_2350\"}, {\"n\": \"RDF format\", \"u\": \"format_2376\"}, {\"n\": \"JSON\", \"u\": \"format_3464\"}, {\"n\": \"YAML\", \"u\": \"format_3750\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format\", \"k\": \"format_1915\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Textual format.\", \"n\": \"Textual format\", \"ns\": [\"Plain text format\", \"txt\"], \"u\": \"format_2330\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"SMILES\", \"u\": \"format_1196\"}, {\"n\": \"InChI\", \"u\": \"format_1197\"}, {\"n\": \"mf\", \"u\": \"format_1198\"}, {\"n\": \"InChIKey\", \"u\": \"format_1199\"}, {\"n\": \"nucleotide\", \"u\": \"format_1207\"}, {\"n\": \"protein\", \"u\": \"format_1208\"}, {\"n\": \"EMBL feature location\", \"u\": \"format_1248\"}, {\"n\": \"quicktandem\", \"u\": \"format_1295\"}, {\"n\": \"Sanger inverted repeats\", \"u\": \"format_1296\"}, {\"n\": \"EMBOSS repeat\", \"u\": \"format_1297\"}, {\"n\": \"est2genome format\", \"u\": \"format_1316\"}, {\"n\": \"restrict format\", \"u\": \"format_1318\"}, {\"n\": \"restover format\", \"u\": \"format_1319\"}, {\"n\": \"REBASE restriction sites\", \"u\": \"format_1320\"}, {\"n\": \"FASTA search results format\", \"u\": \"format_1332\"}, {\"n\": \"BLAST results\", \"u\": \"format_1333\"}, {\"n\": \"mspcrunch\", \"u\": \"format_1334\"}, {\"n\": \"Smith-Waterman format\", \"u\": \"format_1335\"}, {\"n\": \"dhf\", \"u\": \"format_1336\"}, {\"n\": \"lhf\", \"u\": \"format_1337\"}, {\"n\": \"InterPro hits format\", \"u\": \"format_1341\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER Dirichlet prior\", \"u\": \"format_1349\"}, {\"n\": \"MEME Dirichlet prior\", \"u\": \"format_1350\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER emission and transition\", \"u\": \"format_1351\"}, {\"n\": \"prosite-pattern\", \"u\": \"format_1356\"}, {\"n\": \"EMBOSS sequence pattern\", \"u\": \"format_1357\"}, {\"n\": \"meme-motif\", \"u\": \"format_1360\"}, {\"n\": \"prosite-profile\", \"u\": \"format_1366\"}, {\"n\": \"JASPAR format\", \"u\": \"format_1367\"}, {\"n\": \"MEME background Markov model\", \"u\": \"format_1369\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER format\", \"u\": \"format_1370\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER-aln\", \"u\": \"format_1391\"}, {\"n\": \"DIALIGN format\", \"u\": \"format_1392\"}, {\"n\": \"daf\", \"u\": \"format_1393\"}, {\"n\": \"Sequence-MEME profile alignment\", \"u\": \"format_1419\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER profile alignment (sequences versus HMMs)\", \"u\": \"format_1421\"}, {\"n\": \"HMMER profile alignment (HMM versus sequences)\", \"u\": \"format_1422\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip distance matrix\", \"u\": \"format_1423\"}, {\"n\": \"ClustalW dendrogram\", \"u\": \"format_1424\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip tree raw\", \"u\": \"format_1425\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip continuous quantitative characters\", \"u\": \"format_1430\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip character frequencies format\", \"u\": \"format_1432\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip discrete states format\", \"u\": \"format_1433\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip cliques format\", \"u\": \"format_1434\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip tree format\", \"u\": \"format_1435\"}, {\"n\": \"TreeBASE format\", \"u\": \"format_1436\"}, {\"n\": \"TreeFam format\", \"u\": \"format_1437\"}, {\"n\": \"Phylip tree distance format\", \"u\": \"format_1445\"}, {\"n\": \"dssp\", \"u\": \"format_1454\"}, {\"n\": \"hssp\", \"