rmat_2570\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Alphabet for any protein sequence without unknown positions, ambiguity or non-sequence characters.\", \"n\": \"completely unambiguous pure protein\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2607\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||completely unambiguous||completely unambiguous pure||completely unambiguous pure protein\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_2566||format_2567||format_2607\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"2bit binary format of nucleotide sequences using 2 bits per nucleotide. In addition encodes unknown nucleotides and lower-case \'masking\'.\", \"n\": \"2bit\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3009\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||2bit\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3009\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \".nib (nibble) binary format of a nucleotide sequence using 4 bits per nucleotide (including unknown) and its lower-case \'masking\'.\", \"n\": \".nib\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3010\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||.nib\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3010\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"n\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3772\", \"es\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3772\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BioYAML is a BioXSD-schema-based YAML format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web APIs, human readability and editting, and object-oriented programming.\", \"n\": \"BioYAML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3773\", \"es\": [\"BioXSD BioYAML\", \"BioXSD BioYAML format\", \"BioXSD YAML\", \"BioXSD YAML format\", \"BioXSD in YAML\", \"BioXSD in YAML format\", \"BioXSD+YAML\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioYAML\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioYAML\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioYAML (BioXSD)\", \"BioYAML format\", \"BioYAML format (BioXSD)\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BioYAML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3773\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BpForms is a string format for concretely representing the primary structures of biopolymers, including DNA, RNA, and proteins that include non-canonical nucleic and amino acids. See https://www.bpforms.org for more information.\", \"n\": \"BpForms\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3909\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||BpForms\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3909\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Mash sketch is a format for sequence / sequence checksum information. To make a sketch, each k-mer in a sequence is hashed, which creates a pseudo-random identifier. By sorting these hashes, a small subset from the top of the sorted list can represent the entire sequence.\", \"n\": \"msh\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3911\", \"es\": [\"Mash sketch\", \"min-hash sketch\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||msh\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3911\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A Docker image is a file, comprised of multiple layers, that is used to execute code in a Docker container. An image is essentially built from the instructions for a complete and executable version of an application, which relies on the host OS kernel.\", \"n\": \"Docker image format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3973\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw sequence format||Docker image format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2571||format_3973\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of a bibliographic reference.\", \"n\": \"Bibliographic reference format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2848\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"PubMed citation\", \"u\": \"format_1734\"}, {\"n\": \"Medline Display Format\", \"u\": \"format_1735\"}, {\"n\": \"CiteXplore-core\", \"u\": \"format_1736\"}, {\"n\": \"CiteXplore-all\", \"u\": \"format_1737\"}, {\"n\": \"PubMed XML\", \"u\": \"format_3848\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of bibliographic reference as used by the PubMed database.\", \"n\": \"PubMed citation\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1734\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||PubMed citation\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1734\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format for abstracts of scientific articles from the Medline database.\", \"n\": \"Medline Display Format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1735\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||Medline Display Format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1735\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"CiteXplore \'core\' citation format including title, journal, authors and abstract.\", \"n\": \"CiteXplore-core\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1736\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||CiteXplore-core\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1736\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"CiteXplore \'all\' citation format includes all known details such as Mesh terms and cross-references.\", \"n\": \"CiteXplore-all\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1737\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||CiteXplore-all\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_1737\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"XML format for collected entries from biobliographic databases MEDLINE and PubMed.\", \"n\": \"PubMed XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3848\", \"es\": [\"MEDLINE XML\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Bibliographic reference format||PubMed XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2848||format_3848\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of sequence variation annotation.\", \"n\": \"Sequence variation annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2921\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"VCF\", \"u\": \"format_3016\"}, {\"n\": \"GVF\", \"u\": \"format_3019\"}, {\"n\": \"BCF\", \"u\": \"format_3020\"}, {\"n\": \"Ensembl variation file format\", \"u\": \"format_3499\"}, {\"n\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"u\": \"format_3622\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Variant Call Format (VCF) for sequence variation (indels, polymorphisms, structural variation).\", \"n\": \"VCF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3016\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||VCF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3016\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Genome Variation Format (GVF). A GFF3-compatible format with defined header and attribute tags for sequence variation.\", \"n\": \"GVF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3019\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||GVF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3019\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BCF, the binary version of Variant Call Format (VCF) for sequence variation (indels, polymorphisms, structural variation).\", \"n\": \"BCF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3020\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||BCF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3020\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Ensembl standard format for variation data.\", \"n\": \"Ensembl variation file format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3499\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||Ensembl variation file format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3499\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format used by the SQLite database conformant to the Gemini schema.\", \"n\": \"Gemini SQLite format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3622\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence variation annotation format||Gemini SQLite format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_2921||format_3622\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of a matrix (array) of numerical values.\", \"n\": \"Matrix format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3033\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Amino acid index format\", \"u\": \"format_2017\"}, {\"n\": \"3D-1D scoring matrix format\", \"u\": \"format_2064\"}, {\"n\": \"MAT\", \"u\": \"format_3626\"}, {\"n\": \"Zarr\", \"u\": \"format_3915\"}, {\"n\": \"MTX\", \"u\": \"format_3916\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for an amino acid index.\", \"n\": \"Amino acid index format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2017\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"aaindex\", \"u\": \"format_1504\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||Amino acid index format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_2017\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Amino acid index format used by the AAindex database.\", \"n\": \"aaindex\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1504\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||Amino acid index format||aaindex\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_2017||format_1504\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of a matrix of 3D-1D scores (amino acid environment probabilities).\", \"n\": \"3D-1D scoring matrix format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2064\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||3D-1D scoring matrix format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_2064\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Binary format used by MATLAB files to store workspace variables.\", \"n\": \"MAT\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3626\", \"es\": [\".mat file format\", \"MAT file format\", \"MATLAB file format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||MAT\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_3626\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Zarr format is an implementation of chunked, compressed, N-dimensional arrays for storing data.\", \"n\": \"Zarr\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3915\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||Zarr\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_3915\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Matrix Market matrix (MTX) format stores numerical or pattern matrices in a dense (array format) or sparse (coordinate format) representation.\", \"n\": \"MTX\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3916\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Matrix format||MTX\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3033||format_3916\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of data concerning the classification of the sequences and/or structures of protein structural domain(s).\", \"n\": \"Protein domain classification format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3097\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Raw SCOP domain classification format\", \"u\": \"format_3098\"}, {\"n\": \"Raw CATH domain classification format\", \"u\": \"format_3099\"}, {\"n\": \"CATH domain report format\", \"u\": \"format_3100\"}, {\"n\": \"InterProScan XML\", \"u\": \"format_3846\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein domain classification format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3097\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of raw SCOP domain classification data files.\", \"n\": \"Raw SCOP domain classification format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3098\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein domain classification format||Raw SCOP domain classification format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3097||format_3098\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of raw CATH domain classification data files.\", \"n\": \"Raw CATH domain classification format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3099\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein domain classification format||Raw CATH domain classification format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3097||format_3099\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of summary of domain classification information for a CATH domain.\", \"n\": \"CATH domain report format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3100\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein domain classification format||CATH domain report format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3097||format_3100\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Output xml file from the InterProScan sequence analysis application.\", \"n\": \"InterProScan XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3846\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Protein domain classification format||InterProScan XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3097||format_3846\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for a report of information derived from a biological pathway or network.\", \"n\": \"Biological pathway or network report format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3166\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"SBRML\", \"u\": \"format_3155\"}, {\"n\": \"CopasiML\", \"u\": \"format_3239\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network report format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3166\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Systems Biology Result Markup Language (SBRML), the standard XML format for simulated or calculated results (e.g. trajectories) of systems biology models.\", \"n\": \"SBRML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3155\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network report format||SBRML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3166||format_3155\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"CopasiML, the native format of COPASI.\", \"n\": \"CopasiML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3239\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biological pathway or network report format||CopasiML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3166||format_3239\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for annotation on a laboratory experiment.\", \"n\": \"Experiment annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3167\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Microarray experiment data format\", \"u\": \"format_2056\"}, {\"n\": \"GCDML\", \"u\": \"format_3163\"}, {\"n\": \"GelML\", \"u\": \"format_3249\"}, {\"n\": \"spML\", \"u\": \"format_3250\"}, {\"n\": \"qcML\", \"u\": \"format_3683\"}, {\"n\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"u\": \"format_3684\"}, {\"n\": \"SED-ML\", \"u\": \"format_3685\"}, {\"n\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"u\": \"format_3686\"}, {\"n\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"u\": \"format_3687\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format for information about a microarray experimental per se (not the data generated from that experiment).\", \"n\": \"Microarray experiment data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2056\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"affymetrix-exp\", \"u\": \"format_1641\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||Microarray experiment data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_2056\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Affymetrix data file format for information about experimental conditions and protocols.\", \"n\": \"affymetrix-exp\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1641\", \"es\": [\"Affymetrix experimental conditions data file format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||Microarray experiment data format||affymetrix-exp\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_2056||format_1641\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GCDML XML format for genome and metagenome metadata according to MIGS/MIMS/MIMARKS information standards, standardised by the Genomic Standards Consortium (GSC).\", \"n\": \"GCDML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3163\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||GCDML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3163\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GelML is the format for describing the process of gel electrophoresis, standardised by HUPO PSI PS.\", \"n\": \"GelML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3249\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||GelML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3249\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"spML is the format for describing proteomics sample processing, other than using gels, prior to mass spectrometric protein identification, standardised by HUPO PSI PS. It may also be applicable for metabolomics.\", \"n\": \"spML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3250\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||spML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3250\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"n\": \"qcML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3683\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||qcML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3683\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"n\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3684\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||PRIDE XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3684\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Simulation Experiment Description Markup Language (SED-ML) is an XML format for encoding simulation setups, according to the MIASE (Minimum Information About a Simulation Experiment) requirements.\", \"n\": \"SED-ML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3685\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||SED-ML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3685\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Open Modeling EXchange format (OMEX) is a ZIPped format for encapsulating all information necessary for a modeling and simulation project in systems biology.\", \"n\": \"COMBINE OMEX\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3686\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||COMBINE OMEX\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3686\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Investigation / Study / Assay (ISA) tab-delimited (TAB) format incorporates metadata from\\nexperiments employing a combination of technologies.\", \"n\": \"ISA-TAB\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3687\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Experiment annotation format||ISA-TAB\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3167||format_3687\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format for mass pectra and derived data, include peptide sequences etc.\", \"n\": \"Mass spectrometry data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3245\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"mzML\", \"u\": \"format_3244\"}, {\"n\": \"TraML\", \"u\": \"format_3246\"}, {\"n\": \"mzIdentML\", \"u\": \"format_3247\"}, {\"n\": \"mzQuantML\", \"u\": \"format_3248\"}, {\"n\": \"netCDF\", \"u\": \"format_3650\"}, {\"n\": \"MGF\", \"u\": \"format_3651\"}, {\"n\": \"dta\", \"u\": \"format_3652\"}, {\"n\": \"pkl\", \"u\": \"format_3653\"}, {\"n\": \"mzXML\", \"u\": \"format_3654\"}, {\"n\": \"pepXML\", \"u\": \"format_3655\"}, {\"n\": \"mzTab\", \"u\": \"format_3681\"}, {\"n\": \"imzML metadata file\", \"u\": \"format_3682\"}, {\"n\": \"qcML\", \"u\": \"format_3683\"}, {\"n\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"u\": \"format_3684\"}, {\"n\": \"MSF\", \"u\": \"format_3702\"}, {\"n\": \"WIFF format\", \"u\": \"format_3710\"}, {\"n\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"u\": \"format_3711\"}, {\"n\": \"Thermo RAW\", \"u\": \"format_3712\"}, {\"n\": \"Mascot .dat file\", \"u\": \"format_3713\"}, {\"n\": \"MaxQuant APL peaklist format\", \"u\": \"format_3714\"}, {\"n\": \"protXML\", \"u\": \"format_3747\"}, {\"n\": \"SEQUEST .out file\", \"u\": \"format_3758\"}, {\"n\": \"idXML\", \"u\": \"format_3764\"}, {\"n\": \"consensusXML\", \"u\": \"format_3832\"}, {\"n\": \"featureXML\", \"u\": \"format_3833\"}, {\"n\": \"mzData\", \"u\": \"format_3834\"}, {\"n\": \"TIDE TXT\", \"u\": \"format_3835\"}, {\"n\": \"ibd\", \"u\": \"format_3839\"}, {\"n\": \"Waters RAW\", \"u\": \"format_3858\"}, {\"n\": \"JCAMP-DX\", \"u\": \"format_3859\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"mzML format for raw spectrometer output data, standardised by HUPO PSI MSS.\", \"n\": \"mzML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3244\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3244\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"TraML (Transition Markup Language) is the format for mass spectrometry transitions, standardised by HUPO PSI MSS.\", \"n\": \"TraML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3246\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||TraML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3246\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"mzIdentML is the exchange format for peptides and proteins identified from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of proteomics search engines.\", \"n\": \"mzIdentML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3247\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzIdentML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3247\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"mzQuantML is the format for quantitation values associated with peptides, proteins and small molecules from mass spectra, standardised by HUPO PSI PI. It can be used for outputs of quantitation software for proteomics.\", \"n\": \"mzQuantML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3248\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzQuantML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3248\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"n\": \"netCDF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3650\", \"es\": [\"ANDI-MS\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||netCDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3650\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Mascot Generic Format.  Encodes multiple MS/MS spectra in a single file.\", \"n\": \"MGF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3651\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||MGF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3651\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Spectral data format file where each spectrum is written to a separate file.\", \"n\": \"dta\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3652\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||dta\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3652\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Spectral data file similar to dta.\", \"n\": \"pkl\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3653\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||pkl\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3653\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Common file format for proteomics mass spectrometric data developed at the Seattle Proteome Center/Institute for Systems Biology.\", \"n\": \"mzXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3654\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3654\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Open data format for the storage, exchange, and processing of peptide sequence assignments of MS/MS scans, intended to provide a common data output format for many different MS/MS search engines and subsequent peptide-level analyses.\", \"n\": \"pepXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3655\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||pepXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3655\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"mzTab is a tab-delimited format for mass spectrometry-based proteomics and metabolomics results.\", \"n\": \"mzTab\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3681\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzTab\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3681\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"imzML metadata is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging metadata.\", \"n\": \"imzML metadata file\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3682\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||imzML metadata file\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3682\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"qcML is an XML format for quality-related data of mass spectrometry and other high-throughput measurements.\", \"n\": \"qcML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3683\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||qcML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3683\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PRIDE XML is an XML format for mass spectra, peptide and protein identifications, and metadata about a corresponding measurement, sample, experiment.\", \"n\": \"PRIDE XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3684\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||PRIDE XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3684\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Proprietary mass-spectrometry format of Thermo Scientific\'s ProteomeDiscoverer software.\", \"n\": \"MSF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3702\", \"es\": [\"Magellan storage file format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||MSF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3702\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Mass spectrum file format from QSTAR and QTRAP instruments (ABI/Sciex).\", \"n\": \"WIFF format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3710\", \"es\": [\"wiff\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||WIFF format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3710\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Output format used by X! series search engines that is based on the XML language BIOML.\", \"n\": \"X!Tandem XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3711\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||X!Tandem XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3711\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Proprietary file format for mass spectrometry data from Thermo Scientific.\", \"n\": \"Thermo RAW\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3712\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||Thermo RAW\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3712\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"\\\"Raw\\\" result file from Mascot database search.\", \"n\": \"Mascot .dat file\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3713\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||Mascot .dat file\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3713\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of peak list files from Andromeda search engine (MaxQuant) that consist of arbitrarily many spectra.\", \"n\": \"MaxQuant APL peaklist format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3714\", \"es\": [\"MaxQuant APL\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||MaxQuant APL peaklist format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3714\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format for storage, exchange, and processing of protein identifications created from ms/ms-derived peptide sequence data.\", \"n\": \"protXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3747\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||protXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3747\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"\\\"Raw\\\" result file from SEQUEST database search.\", \"n\": \"SEQUEST .out file\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3758\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||SEQUEST .out file\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3758\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"XML file format for files containing information about peptide identifications from mass spectrometry data analysis carried out with OpenMS.\", \"n\": \"idXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3764\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||idXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3764\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"OpenMS format for grouping features in one map or across several maps.\", \"n\": \"consensusXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3832\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||consensusXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3832\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"OpenMS format for quantitation results (LC/MS features).\", \"n\": \"featureXML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3833\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||featureXML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3833\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Now deprecated data format of the HUPO Proteomics Standards Initiative.  Replaced by mzML (format_3244).\", \"n\": \"mzData\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3834\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||mzData\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3834\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format supported by the Tide tool for identifying peptides from tandem mass spectra.\", \"n\": \"TIDE TXT\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3835\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||TIDE TXT\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3835\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"ibd is a data format for mass spectrometry imaging data.\", \"n\": \"ibd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3839\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||ibd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3839\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Proprietary file format for mass spectrometry data from Waters.\", \"n\": \"Waters RAW\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3858\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||Waters RAW\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3858\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A standardized file format for data exchange in mass spectrometry, initially developed for infrared spectrometry.\", \"n\": \"JCAMP-DX\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3859\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Mass spectrometry data format||JCAMP-DX\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3245||format_3859\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for a metadata on an individual and their genetic data.\", \"n\": \"Individual genetic data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3287\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"PED/MAP\", \"u\": \"format_3288\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Individual genetic data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3287\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The PED/MAP file describes data used by the Plink package.\", \"n\": \"PED/MAP\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3288\", \"es\": [\"Plink PED/MAP\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"MAP\", \"u\": \"format_3285\"}, {\"n\": \"PED\", \"u\": \"format_3286\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Individual genetic data format||PED/MAP\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3287||format_3288\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The MAP file describes SNPs and is used by the Plink package.\", \"n\": \"MAP\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3285\", \"es\": [\"Plink MAP\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Individual genetic data format||PED/MAP||MAP\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3287||format_3288||format_3285\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The PED file describes individuals and genetic data and is used by the Plink package.\", \"n\": \"PED\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3286\", \"es\": [\"Plink PED\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Individual genetic data format||PED/MAP||PED\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3287||format_3288||format_3286\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of a data index of some type.\", \"n\": \"Data index format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3326\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"BAI\", \"u\": \"format_3327\"}, {\"n\": \"ebwt\", \"u\": \"format_3484\"}, {\"n\": \"ebwtl\", \"u\": \"format_3491\"}, {\"n\": \"snpeffdb\", \"u\": \"format_3624\"}, {\"n\": \"Tabix index file format\", \"u\": \"format_3700\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BAM indexing format\", \"n\": \"BAI\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3327\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||BAI\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3327\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Bowtie format for indexed reference genome for \\\"small\\\" genomes.\", \"n\": \"ebwt\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3484\", \"es\": [\"Bowtie index format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||ebwt\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3484\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Bowtie format for indexed reference genome for \\\"large\\\" genomes.\", \"n\": \"ebwtl\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3491\", \"es\": [\"Bowtie long index format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||ebwtl\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3491\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"An index of a genome database, indexed for use by the snpeff tool.\", \"n\": \"snpeffdb\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3624\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||snpeffdb\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3624\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Index file format used by the samtools package to index TAB-delimited genome position files.\", \"n\": \"Tabix index file format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3700\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Data index format||Tabix index file format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3326||format_3700\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of documents including word processor, spreadsheet and presentation.\", \"n\": \"Document format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3507\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"xls\", \"u\": \"format_3468\"}, {\"n\": \"docx\", \"u\": \"format_3506\"}, {\"n\": \"PDF\", \"u\": \"format_3508\"}, {\"n\": \"xlsx\", \"u\": \"format_3620\"}, {\"n\": \"latex\", \"u\": \"format_3817\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Microsoft Excel spreadsheet format.\", \"n\": \"xls\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3468\", \"es\": [\"Microsoft Excel format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||xls\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3468\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Microsoft Word format.\", \"n\": \"docx\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3506\", \"es\": [\"Microsoft Word format\", \"doc\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||docx\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3506\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Portable Document Format\", \"n\": \"PDF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3508\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||PDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3508\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"MS Excel spreadsheet format consisting of a set of XML documents stored in a ZIP-compressed file.\", \"n\": \"xlsx\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3620\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"ObjTables\", \"u\": \"format_3977\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||xlsx\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3620\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"ObjTables is a toolkit for creating re-usable datasets that are both human and machine-readable, combining the ease of spreadsheets (e.g., Excel workbooks) with the rigor of schemas (classes, their attributes, the type of each attribute, and the possible relationships between instances of classes). ObjTables consists of a format for describing schemas for spreadsheets, numerous data types for science, a syntax for indicating the class and attribute represented by each table and column in a workbook, and software for using schemas to rigorously validate, merge, split, compare, and revision datasets.\", \"n\": \"ObjTables\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3977\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||xlsx||ObjTables\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3620||format_3977\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"format for the LaTeX document preparation system\", \"n\": \"latex\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3817\", \"es\": [\"LaTeX format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Document format||latex\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3507||format_3817\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format used for images and image metadata.\", \"n\": \"Image format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3547\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"DICOM format\", \"u\": \"format_3548\"}, {\"n\": \"nii\", \"u\": \"format_3549\"}, {\"n\": \"mhd\", \"u\": \"format_3550\"}, {\"n\": \"nrrd\", \"u\": \"format_3551\"}, {\"n\": \"JPG\", \"u\": \"format_3579\"}, {\"n\": \"TIFF\", \"u\": \"format_3591\"}, {\"n\": \"BMP\", \"u\": \"format_3592\"}, {\"n\": \"im\", \"u\": \"format_3593\"}, {\"n\": \"pcd\", \"u\": \"format_3594\"}, {\"n\": \"pcx\", \"u\": \"format_3595\"}, {\"n\": \"ppm\", \"u\": \"format_3596\"}, {\"n\": \"psd\", \"u\": \"format_3597\"}, {\"n\": \"xbm\", \"u\": \"format_3598\"}, {\"n\": \"xpm\", \"u\": \"format_3599\"}, {\"n\": \"rgb\", \"u\": \"format_3600\"}, {\"n\": \"pbm\", \"u\": \"format_3601\"}, {\"n\": \"pgm\", \"u\": \"format_3602\"}, {\"n\": \"PNG\", \"u\": \"format_3603\"}, {\"n\": \"SVG\", \"u\": \"format_3604\"}, {\"n\": \"rast\", \"u\": \"format_3605\"}, {\"n\": \"bgzip\", \"u\": \"format_3615\"}, {\"n\": \"tabix\", \"u\": \"format_3616\"}, {\"n\": \"OME-TIFF\", \"u\": \"format_3727\"}, {\"n\": \"pptx\", \"u\": \"format_3838\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega\", \"u\": \"format_3969\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega-lite\", \"u\": \"format_3970\"}, {\"n\": \"WMV\", \"u\": \"format_3986\"}, {\"n\": \"LSM\", \"u\": \"format_3988\"}, {\"n\": \"AVI\", \"u\": \"format_3990\"}, {\"n\": \"Stereolithography format\", \"u\": \"format_3993\"}, {\"n\": \"U3D\", \"u\": \"format_3994\"}, {\"n\": \"Texture file format\", \"u\": \"format_3995\"}, {\"n\": \"MPEG-4\", \"u\": \"format_3997\"}, {\"n\": \"NIFTI format\", \"u\": \"format_4001\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Medical image format corresponding to the Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) standard.\", \"n\": \"DICOM format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3548\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||DICOM format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3548\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Medical image and metadata format of the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative.\", \"n\": \"nii\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3549\", \"es\": [\"NIfTI-1 format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||nii\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3549\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Text-based tagged file format for medical images generated using the MetaImage software package.\", \"n\": \"mhd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3550\", \"es\": [\"Metalmage format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||mhd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3550\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Nearly Raw Rasta Data format designed to support scientific visualisation and image processing involving N-dimensional raster data.\", \"n\": \"nrrd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3551\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||nrrd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3551\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Joint Picture Group file format for lossy graphics file.\", \"n\": \"JPG\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3579\", \"es\": [\"JPEG\", \"jpeg\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||JPG\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3579\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A versatile bitmap format.\", \"n\": \"TIFF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3591\", \"es\": [\"tiff\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||TIFF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3591\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Standard bitmap storage format in the Microsoft Windows environment.\", \"n\": \"BMP\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3592\", \"es\": [\"bmp\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||BMP\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3592\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"IM is a format used by LabEye and other applications based on the IFUNC image processing library.\", \"n\": \"im\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3593\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||im\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3593\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Photo CD format, which is the highest resolution format for images on a CD.\", \"n\": \"pcd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3594\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pcd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3594\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PCX is an image file format that uses a simple form of run-length encoding. It is lossless.\", \"n\": \"pcx\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3595\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pcx\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3595\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The PPM format is a lowest common denominator color image file format.\", \"n\": \"ppm\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3596\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||ppm\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3596\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PSD (Photoshop Document) is a proprietary file that allows the user to work with the images\' individual layers even after the file has been saved.\", \"n\": \"psd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3597\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||psd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3597\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"X BitMap is a plain text binary image format used by the X Window System used for storing cursor and icon bitmaps used in the X GUI.\", \"n\": \"xbm\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3598\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||xbm\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3598\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"X PixMap (XPM) is an image file format used by the X Window System, it is intended primarily for creating icon pixmaps, and supports transparent pixels.\", \"n\": \"xpm\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3599\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||xpm\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3599\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"RGB file format is the native raster graphics file format for Silicon Graphics workstations.\", \"n\": \"rgb\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3600\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||rgb\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3600\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The PBM format is a lowest common denominator monochrome file format. It serves as the common language of a large family of bitmap image conversion filters.\", \"n\": \"pbm\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3601\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pbm\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3601\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The PGM format is a lowest common denominator grayscale file format.\", \"n\": \"pgm\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3602\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pgm\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3602\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PNG is a file format for image compression.\", \"n\": \"PNG\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3603\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||PNG\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3603\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) is an XML-based vector image format for two-dimensional graphics with support for interactivity and animation.\", \"n\": \"SVG\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3604\", \"es\": [\"Scalable Vector Graphics\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||SVG\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3604\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Sun Raster is a raster graphics file format used on SunOS by Sun Microsystems\", \"n\": \"rast\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3605\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||rast\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3605\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Blocked GNU Zip format.\", \"n\": \"bgzip\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3615\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||bgzip\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3615\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"TAB-delimited genome position file index format.\", \"n\": \"tabix\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3616\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||tabix\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3616\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Image file format used by the Open Microscopy Environment (OME).\", \"n\": \"OME-TIFF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3727\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||OME-TIFF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3727\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Microsoft Powerpoint format.\", \"n\": \"pptx\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3838\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||pptx\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3838\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"n\": \"Vega\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3969\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Vega\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3969\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||Vega\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3969\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||Vega\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3969\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"n\": \"Vega-lite\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3970\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Vega-lite\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3970\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||Vega-lite\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3970\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||Vega-lite\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3970\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The proprietary native video format of various Microsoft programs such as Windows Media Player.\", \"n\": \"WMV\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3986\", \"es\": [\"Windows Media Video format\", \"Windows movie file format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||WMV\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3986\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Zeiss\' proprietary image format based on TIFF.\", \"n\": \"LSM\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3988\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||LSM\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3988\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Audio Video Interleaved (AVI) format is a multimedia container format for AVI files, that allows synchronous audio-with-video playback.\", \"n\": \"AVI\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3990\", \"es\": [\"Audio Video Interleaved\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||AVI\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3990\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"STL is a file format native to the stereolithography CAD software created by 3D Systems.  The format is used to save and share surface-rendered 3D images and also for 3D printing.\", \"n\": \"Stereolithography format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3993\", \"es\": [\"stl\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Stereolithography format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3993\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"U3D (Universal 3D) is a compressed file format and data structure for 3D computer graphics. It contains 3D model information such as triangle meshes, lighting, shading, motion data, lines and points with color and structure.\", \"n\": \"U3D\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3994\", \"es\": [\"Universal 3D\", \"Universal 3D format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||U3D\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3994\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Bitmap image format used for storing textures.\", \"n\": \"Texture file format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3995\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||Texture file format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3995\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A digital multimedia container format most commonly used to store video and audio.\", \"n\": \"MPEG-4\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3997\", \"es\": [\"MP4\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||MPEG-4\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_3997\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"An open file format from the Neuroimaging Informatics Technology Initiative (NIfTI) commonly used to store brain imaging data obtained using Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) methods.\", \"n\": \"NIFTI format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_4001\", \"es\": [\"NIFTI\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Image format||NIFTI format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3547||format_4001\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Textual report format for sequence quality for reports from sequencing machines.\", \"n\": \"Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3606\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"qual\", \"u\": \"format_3607\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences).\", \"n\": \"qual\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3607\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"qualsolexa\", \"u\": \"format_3608\"}, {\"n\": \"qualillumina\", \"u\": \"format_3609\"}, {\"n\": \"qualsolid\", \"u\": \"format_3610\"}, {\"n\": \"qual454\", \"u\": \"format_3611\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)||qual\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606||format_3607\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) for Solexa/Illumina 1.0 format.\", \"n\": \"qualsolexa\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3608\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)||qual||qualsolexa\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606||format_3607||format_3608\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) from Illumina 1.5 and before Illumina 1.8.\", \"n\": \"qualillumina\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3609\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)||qual||qualillumina\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606||format_3607||format_3609\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) for SOLiD data.\", \"n\": \"qualsolid\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3610\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)||qual||qualsolid\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606||format_3607||format_3610\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"FASTQ format subset for Phred sequencing quality score data only (no sequences) from 454 sequencers.\", \"n\": \"qual454\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3611\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Sequence quality report format (text)||qual||qual454\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3606||format_3607||format_3611\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for graph data.\", \"n\": \"Graph format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3617\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"xgmml\", \"u\": \"format_3618\"}, {\"n\": \"K-mer countgraph\", \"u\": \"format_3665\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Graph format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3617\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"XML-based format used to store graph descriptions within Galaxy.\", \"n\": \"xgmml\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3618\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Graph format||xgmml\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3617||format_3618\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A list of k-mers and their occurences in a dataset. Can also be used as an implicit De Bruijn graph.\", \"n\": \"K-mer countgraph\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3665\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Graph format||K-mer countgraph\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3617||format_3665\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for biodiversity data.\", \"n\": \"Biodiversity data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3706\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"ABCD format\", \"u\": \"format_3708\"}, {\"n\": \"BIOM format\", \"u\": \"format_3746\"}, {\"n\": \"MCPD\", \"u\": \"format_3777\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Exchange format of the Access to Biological Collections Data (ABCD) Schema; a standard for the access to and exchange of data about specimens and observations (primary biodiversity data).\", \"n\": \"ABCD format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3708\", \"es\": [\"ABCD\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format||ABCD format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706||format_3708\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The BIological Observation Matrix (BIOM) is a format for representing biological sample by observation contingency tables in broad areas of comparative omics. The primary use of this format is to represent OTU tables and metagenome tables.\", \"n\": \"BIOM format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3746\", \"es\": [\"BIological Observation Matrix format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format||BIOM format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706||format_3746\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The FAO/Bioversity/IPGRI Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors (MCPD) is an international standard format for exchange of germplasm information.\", \"n\": \"MCPD\", \"ns\": [\"IPGRI MCPD\", \"MCPD V.1\", \"MCPD V.2\"], \"u\": \"format_3777\", \"es\": [\"Bioversity MCPD\", \"FAO MCPD\", \"MCPD format\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors\", \"Multi-Crop Passport Descriptors format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Biodiversity data format||MCPD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3706||format_3777\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A linked data format enables publishing structured data as linked data (Linked Data), so that the data can be interlinked and become more useful through semantic queries.\", \"n\": \"Linked data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3748\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"RDF format\", \"u\": \"format_2376\"}, {\"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"u\": \"format_3749\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Resource Description Framework (RDF) model.\", \"n\": \"RDF format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2376\", \"es\": [\"Resource Description Framework format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"OWL format\", \"u\": \"format_2197\"}, {\"n\": \"Turtle\", \"u\": \"format_3255\"}, {\"n\": \"N-Triples\", \"u\": \"format_3256\"}, {\"n\": \"Notation3\", \"u\": \"format_3257\"}, {\"n\": \"RDF/XML\", \"u\": \"format_3261\"}, {\"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"u\": \"format_3749\"}, {\"n\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"u\": \"format_3771\"}, {\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}, {\"n\": \"N-Quads\", \"u\": \"format_3956\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Web Ontology Language (OWL) model.\", \"n\": \"OWL format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2197\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"u\": \"format_3252\"}, {\"n\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"u\": \"format_3253\"}, {\"n\": \"OWL/XML\", \"u\": \"format_3262\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||OWL format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_2197\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A human-readable encoding for the Web Ontology Language (OWL).\", \"n\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3252\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||OWL format||OWL Functional Syntax\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_2197||format_3252\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A syntax for writing OWL class expressions.\", \"n\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3253\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||OWL format||Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_2197||format_3253\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"OWL ontology XML serialisation format.\", \"n\": \"OWL/XML\", \"ns\": [\"OWL\"], \"u\": \"format_3262\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||OWL format||OWL/XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_2197||format_3262\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Terse RDF Triple Language (Turtle) is a human-friendly serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs.\", \"n\": \"Turtle\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3255\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||Turtle\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3255\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A plain text serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs, and a subset of the Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) format.\", \"n\": \"N-Triples\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3256\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||N-Triples\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3256\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A shorthand non-XML serialisation of Resource Description Framework model, designed with human-readability in mind.\", \"n\": \"Notation3\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3257\", \"es\": [\"N3\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||Notation3\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3257\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Resource Description Framework (RDF) XML format.\", \"n\": \"RDF/XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3261\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||RDF/XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3261\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3749\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||JSON-LD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3749\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||JSON-LD||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3749||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"UniProtKB RDF sequence features format is an RDF format available for downloading UniProt entries (in RDF/XML).\", \"n\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"ns\": [\"UniProt RDF/XML\", \"UniProt RDF/XML format\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML format\"], \"u\": \"format_3771\", \"es\": [\"UniProt RDF\", \"UniProt RDF format\", \"UniProtKB RDF format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||UniProtKB RDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3771\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. It includes information about the graph each triple belongs to.\", \"n\": \"N-Quads\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3956\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||RDF format||N-Quads\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_2376||format_3956\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3749\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||JSON-LD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_3749\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Linked data format||JSON-LD||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3748||format_3749||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format of an annotated text, e.g. with recognised entities, concepts, and relations.\", \"n\": \"Annotated text format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3780\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"OSCAR format\", \"u\": \"format_1741\"}, {\"n\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3781\"}, {\"n\": \"BioC\", \"u\": \"format_3782\"}, {\"n\": \"PubTator format\", \"u\": \"format_3783\"}, {\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}, {\"n\": \"BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"u\": \"format_3785\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"OSCAR format of annotated chemical text.\", \"n\": \"OSCAR format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_1741\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||OSCAR format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_1741\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"n\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3781\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||PubAnnotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3781\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||PubAnnotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3781\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||PubAnnotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464||format_3781\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BioC is a standardised XML format for sharing and integrating text data and annotations.\", \"n\": \"BioC\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3782\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||BioC\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3782\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Native textual export format of annotated scientific text from PubTator.\", \"n\": \"PubTator format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3783\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||PubTator format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3783\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A family of similar formats of text annotation, used by BRAT and other tools, known as BioNLP Shared Task format (BioNLP 2009 Shared Task on Event Extraction, BioNLP Shared Task 2011, BioNLP Shared Task 2013), BRAT format, BRAT standoff format, and similar.\", \"n\": \"BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3785\", \"es\": [\"BRAT format\", \"BRAT standoff format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Annotated text format||BioNLP Shared Task format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3780||format_3785\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A query language (format) for structured database queries.\", \"n\": \"Query language\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3787\", \"es\": [\"Query format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Query language\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3787\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for raw data from a nuclear magnetic resonance (NMR) spectroscopy experiment.\", \"n\": \"NMR data format\", \"ns\": [\"NMR peak assignment data\", \"NMR processed data format\", \"NMR raw data format\", \"Processed NMR data format\", \"Raw NMR data format\"], \"u\": \"format_3824\", \"es\": [\"Nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy data format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"nmrML\", \"u\": \"format_3825\"}, {\"n\": \"NMReDATA\", \"u\": \"format_3906\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NMR data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3824\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"nmrML is an MSI supported XML-based open access format for metabolomics NMR raw and processed spectral data. It is accompanies by an nmrCV (controlled vocabulary) to allow ontology-based annotations.\", \"n\": \"nmrML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3825\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NMR data format||nmrML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3824||format_3825\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"MReData is a text based data standard for processed NMR data. It is relying on SDF molecule data and allows to store assignments of NMR peaks to molecule features.  The NMR-extracted data (or \\\"NMReDATA\\\") includes: Chemical shift,scalar coupling, 2D correlation, assignment, etc.\", \"n\": \"NMReDATA\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3906\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NMR data format||NMReDATA\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3824||format_3906\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format for raw microarray data.\", \"n\": \"Raw microarray data format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3828\", \"es\": [\"Microarray data format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"GPR\", \"u\": \"format_3829\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw microarray data format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3828\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GenePix Results (GPR) text file format developed by Axon Instruments that is used to save GenePix Results data.\", \"n\": \"GPR\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3829\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Raw microarray data format||GPR\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3828||format_3829\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Data format used in Natural Language Processing.\", \"n\": \"NLP format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3841\", \"es\": [\"Natural Language Processing format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"NLP annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3862\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"An NLP format used for annotated textual documents.\", \"n\": \"NLP annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3862\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"NLP corpus format\", \"u\": \"format_3863\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format||NLP annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841||format_3862\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"NLP format used by a specific type of corpus (collection of texts).\", \"n\": \"NLP corpus format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3863\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||NLP format||NLP annotation format||NLP corpus format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3841||format_3862||format_3863\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A \\\"placeholder\\\" concept for formats of annotated RNA data, including e.g. microRNA and RNA-Seq data.\", \"n\": \"RNA annotation format\", \"ns\": [\"miRNA data format\", \"microRNA data format\"], \"u\": \"format_3865\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"mirGFF3\", \"u\": \"format_3864\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||RNA annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3865\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"mirGFF3 is a common format for microRNA data resulting from small-RNA RNA-Seq workflows.\", \"n\": \"mirGFF3\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3864\", \"es\": [\"miRTop format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||RNA annotation format||mirGFF3\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3865||format_3864\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"File format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"n\": \"Trajectory format\", \"ns\": [\"CG trajectory formats\", \"MD trajectory formats\", \"NA trajectory formats\", \"Protein trajectory formats\"], \"u\": \"format_3866\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Trajectory format (binary)\", \"u\": \"format_3867\"}, {\"n\": \"Trajectory format (text)\", \"u\": \"format_3868\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Binary file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"n\": \"Trajectory format (binary)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3867\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"HDF5\", \"u\": \"format_3590\"}, {\"n\": \"netCDF\", \"u\": \"format_3650\"}, {\"n\": \"HDF\", \"u\": \"format_3873\"}, {\"n\": \"PCAzip\", \"u\": \"format_3874\"}, {\"n\": \"XTC\", \"u\": \"format_3875\"}, {\"n\": \"TNG\", \"u\": \"format_3876\"}, {\"n\": \"BinPos\", \"u\": \"format_3885\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"HDF5 is a data model, library, and file format for storing and managing data, based on Hierarchical Data Format (HDF).\", \"n\": \"HDF5\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3590\", \"es\": [\"h5\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Loom\", \"u\": \"format_3913\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||HDF5\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3590\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Loom file format is based on HDF5, a standard for storing large numerical datasets. The Loom format is designed to efficiently hold large omics datasets. Typically, such data takes the form of a large matrix of numbers, along with metadata for the rows and columns.\", \"n\": \"Loom\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3913\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||HDF5||Loom\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3590||format_3913\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format used by netCDF software  library for writing and reading chromatography-MS data files.  Also used to store trajectory atom coordinates information, such as the ones obtained by Molecular Dynamics simulations.\", \"n\": \"netCDF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3650\", \"es\": [\"ANDI-MS\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||netCDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3650\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"HDF is the name of a set of file formats and libraries designed to store and organize large amounts of numerical data, originally developed at the National Center for Supercomputing Applications at the University of Illinois.\", \"n\": \"HDF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3873\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||HDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3873\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"PCAZip format is a binary compressed file to store atom coordinates based on Essential Dynamics (ED) and Principal Component Analysis (PCA).\", \"n\": \"PCAzip\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3874\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||PCAzip\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3874\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Portable binary format for trajectories produced by GROMACS package.\", \"n\": \"XTC\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3875\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||XTC\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3875\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Trajectory Next Generation (TNG) is a format for storage of molecular simulation data. It is designed and implemented by the GROMACS development group, and it is called to be the substitute of the XTC format.\", \"n\": \"TNG\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3876\", \"es\": [\"Trajectory Next Generation format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||TNG\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3876\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Scripps Research Institute BinPos format is a binary formatted file to store atom coordinates.\", \"n\": \"BinPos\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3885\", \"es\": [\"Scripps Research Institute BinPos\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (binary)||BinPos\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3867||format_3885\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Textual file format to store trajectory information for a 3D structure .\", \"n\": \"Trajectory format (text)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3868\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"XYZ\", \"u\": \"format_3877\"}, {\"n\": \"mdcrd\", \"u\": \"format_3878\"}, {\"n\": \"RST\", \"u\": \"format_3886\"}, {\"n\": \"trr\", \"u\": \"format_3910\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The XYZ chemical file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.). Basic information stored for each atom in the system are x, y and z coordinates and atom element/atomic number.\", \"n\": \"XYZ\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3877\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||XYZ\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3877\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"AMBER trajectory (also called mdcrd), with 10 coordinates per line and format F8.3 (fixed point notation with field width 8 and 3 decimal places).\", \"n\": \"mdcrd\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3878\", \"es\": [\"AMBER trajectory format\", \"inpcrd\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||mdcrd\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3878\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"AMBER coordinate/restart file with 6 coordinates per line and decimal format F12.7 (fixed point notation with field width 12 and 7 decimal places)\", \"n\": \"RST\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3886\", \"es\": [\"restrt\", \"rst7\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||RST\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3886\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of trr files that contain the trajectory of a simulation experiment used by GROMACS.\", \"n\": \"trr\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3910\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Trajectory format||Trajectory format (text)||trr\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3866||format_3868||format_3910\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of topology files; containing the static information of a structure molecular system that is needed for a molecular simulation.\", \"n\": \"Topology format\", \"ns\": [\"CG topology format\", \"MD topology format\", \"NA topology format\", \"Protein topology format\"], \"u\": \"format_3879\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"GROMACS top\", \"u\": \"format_3880\"}, {\"n\": \"AMBER top\", \"u\": \"format_3881\"}, {\"n\": \"PSF\", \"u\": \"format_3882\"}, {\"n\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"u\": \"format_3883\"}, {\"n\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"u\": \"format_3887\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GROMACS MD package top textual files define an entire structure system topology, either directly, or by including itp files.\", \"n\": \"GROMACS top\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3880\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||GROMACS top\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3880\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"AMBER Prmtop file (version 7) is a structure topology text file divided in several sections designed to be parsed easily using simple Fortran code. Each section contains particular topology information, such as atom name, charge, mass, angles, dihedrals, etc.\", \"n\": \"AMBER top\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3881\", \"es\": [\"AMBER Parm\", \"AMBER Parm7\", \"Parm7\", \"Prmtop\", \"Prmtop7\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||AMBER top\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3881\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"X-Plor Protein Structure Files (PSF) are structure topology files used by NAMD and CHARMM molecular simulations programs. PSF files contain six main sections of interest: atoms, bonds, angles, dihedrals, improper dihedrals (force terms used to maintain planarity) and cross-terms.\", \"n\": \"PSF\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3882\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||PSF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3882\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"n\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3883\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||GROMACS itp\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3883\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of CHARMM Residue Topology Files (RTF), which define groups by including the atoms, the properties of the group, and bond and charge information.\", \"n\": \"CHARMM rtf\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3887\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||Topology format||CHARMM rtf\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3879||format_3887\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Format of force field parameter files, which store the set of parameters (charges, masses, radii, bond lengths, bond dihedrals, etc.) that are essential for the proper description and simulation of a molecular system.\", \"n\": \"FF parameter format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3884\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"u\": \"format_3883\"}, {\"n\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"u\": \"format_3888\"}, {\"n\": \"AMBER off\", \"u\": \"format_3889\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"GROMACS itp files (include topology) contain structure topology information, and are tipically included in GROMACS topology files (GROMACS top). Itp files are used to define individual (or multiple) components of a topology as a separate file. This is particularly useful if there is a molecule that is used frequently, and also reduces the size of the system topology file, splitting it in different parts.\", \"n\": \"GROMACS itp\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3883\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||GROMACS itp\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3883\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"AMBER frcmod (Force field Modification) is a file format to store any modification to the standard force field needed for a particular molecule to be properly represented in the simulation.\", \"n\": \"AMBER frcmod\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3888\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||AMBER frcmod\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3888\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"AMBER Object File Format library files (OFF library files) store residue libraries (forcefield residue parameters).\", \"n\": \"AMBER off\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3889\", \"es\": [\"AMBER Object File Format\", \"AMBER lib\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||Format (by type of data)||FF parameter format||AMBER off\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2350||format_3884||format_3889\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Resource Description Framework (RDF) model.\", \"n\": \"RDF format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2376\", \"es\": [\"Resource Description Framework format\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"OWL format\", \"u\": \"format_2197\"}, {\"n\": \"Turtle\", \"u\": \"format_3255\"}, {\"n\": \"N-Triples\", \"u\": \"format_3256\"}, {\"n\": \"Notation3\", \"u\": \"format_3257\"}, {\"n\": \"RDF/XML\", \"u\": \"format_3261\"}, {\"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"u\": \"format_3749\"}, {\"n\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"u\": \"format_3771\"}, {\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}, {\"n\": \"N-Quads\", \"u\": \"format_3956\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A serialisation format conforming to the Web Ontology Language (OWL) model.\", \"n\": \"OWL format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_2197\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"u\": \"format_3252\"}, {\"n\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"u\": \"format_3253\"}, {\"n\": \"OWL/XML\", \"u\": \"format_3262\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||OWL format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_2197\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A human-readable encoding for the Web Ontology Language (OWL).\", \"n\": \"OWL Functional Syntax\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3252\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||OWL format||OWL Functional Syntax\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_2197||format_3252\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A syntax for writing OWL class expressions.\", \"n\": \"Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3253\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||OWL format||Manchester OWL Syntax\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_2197||format_3253\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"OWL ontology XML serialisation format.\", \"n\": \"OWL/XML\", \"ns\": [\"OWL\"], \"u\": \"format_3262\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||OWL format||OWL/XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_2197||format_3262\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"The Terse RDF Triple Language (Turtle) is a human-friendly serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs.\", \"n\": \"Turtle\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3255\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||Turtle\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3255\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A plain text serialisation format for RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs, and a subset of the Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) format.\", \"n\": \"N-Triples\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3256\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||N-Triples\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3256\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A shorthand non-XML serialisation of Resource Description Framework model, designed with human-readability in mind.\", \"n\": \"Notation3\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3257\", \"es\": [\"N3\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||Notation3\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3257\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Resource Description Framework (RDF) XML format.\", \"n\": \"RDF/XML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3261\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||RDF/XML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3261\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3749\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||JSON-LD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3749\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||JSON-LD||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3749||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"UniProtKB RDF sequence features format is an RDF format available for downloading UniProt entries (in RDF/XML).\", \"n\": \"UniProtKB RDF\", \"ns\": [\"UniProt RDF/XML\", \"UniProt RDF/XML format\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML\", \"UniProtKB RDF/XML format\"], \"u\": \"format_3771\", \"es\": [\"UniProt RDF\", \"UniProt RDF format\", \"UniProtKB RDF format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||UniProtKB RDF\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3771\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"N-Quads is a line-based, plain text format for encoding an RDF dataset. It includes information about the graph each triple belongs to.\", \"n\": \"N-Quads\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3956\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||RDF format||N-Quads\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_2376||format_3956\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JavaScript Object Notation format; a lightweight, text-based format to represent tree-structured data using key-value pairs.\", \"n\": \"JSON\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3464\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"u\": \"format_3749\"}, {\"n\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"u\": \"format_3772\"}, {\"n\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"u\": \"format_3774\"}, {\"n\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3781\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega\", \"u\": \"format_3969\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega-lite\", \"u\": \"format_3970\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||JSON\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464\"}, {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3749\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||JSON-LD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3749\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"A format of text annotation using the linked-data Open Annotation Data Model, serialised typically in RDF or JSON-LD.\", \"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3784\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||JSON-LD||Open Annotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3749||format_3784\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BioJSON is a BioXSD-schema-based JSON format of sequence-based data and some other common data - sequence records, alignments, feature records, references to resources, and more - optimised for integrative bioinformatics, web applications and APIs, and object-oriented programming.\", \"n\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3772\", \"es\": [\"BioJSON (BioXSD data model)\", \"BioJSON format (BioXSD)\", \"BioXSD BioJSON\", \"BioXSD BioJSON format\", \"BioXSD JSON\", \"BioXSD JSON format\", \"BioXSD in JSON\", \"BioXSD in JSON format\", \"BioXSD+JSON\", \"BioXSD/GTrack BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|BioJSON|BioYAML BioJSON\", \"BioXSD|GTrack BioJSON\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3772\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"BioJSON is a JSON format of single multiple sequence alignments, with their annotations, features, and custom visualisation and application settings for the Jalview workbench.\", \"n\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3774\", \"es\": [\"BioJSON format (Jalview)\", \"JSON (Jalview)\", \"JSON format (Jalview)\", \"Jalview BioJSON\", \"Jalview BioJSON format\", \"Jalview JSON\", \"Jalview JSON format\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3774\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON format of annotated scientific text used by PubAnnotations and other tools.\", \"n\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3781\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||PubAnnotation format\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3781\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Vega is a visualization grammar, a declarative language for creating, saving, and sharing interactive visualization designs. With Vega, you can describe the visual appearance and interactive behavior of a visualization in a JSON format, and generate web-based views using Canvas or SVG.\", \"n\": \"Vega\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3969\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||Vega\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3969\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"Vega-Lite is a high-level grammar of interactive graphics. It provides a concise JSON syntax for rapidly generating visualizations to support analysis. Vega-Lite specifications can be compiled to Vega specifications.\", \"n\": \"Vega-lite\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3970\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||JSON||Vega-lite\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3464||format_3970\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"YAML (YAML Ain\'t Markup Language) is a human-readable tree-structured data serialisation language.\", \"n\": \"YAML\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3750\", \"es\": [\"YAML Ain\'t Markup Language\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"JSON\", \"u\": \"format_3464\"}, {\"n\": \"BioYAML\", \"u\": \"format_3773\"}, {\"n\": \"CWL\", \"u\": \"format_3857\"}], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Format||YAML\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750\"}], \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JavaScript Object Notation format; a lightweight, text-based format to represent tree-structured data using key-value pairs.\", \"n\": \"JSON\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3464\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"u\": \"format_3749\"}, {\"n\": \"BioJSON (BioXSD)\", \"u\": \"format_3772\"}, {\"n\": \"BioJSON (Jalview)\", \"u\": \"format_3774\"}, {\"n\": \"PubAnnotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3781\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega\", \"u\": \"format_3969\"}, {\"n\": \"Vega-lite\", \"u\": \"format_3970\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||format_3464\"}, \"hi\": null, \"ht\": null, \"ho\": null}, {\"d\": \"JSON-LD, or JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data, is a method of encoding Linked Data using JSON.\", \"n\": \"JSON-LD\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"format_3749\", \"es\": [\"JavaScript Object Notation for Linked Data\"], \"ch\": [{\"n\": \"Open Annotation format\", \"u\": \"format_3784\"}], \"p\": {\"n\": \"Format||YAML||JSON||JSON-LD\", \"k\": \"format_1915||format_3750||forma