etry\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0134\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein microarray data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein microarrays\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0135\"}], \"name\": \"Protein microarrays\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0135\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The study of the hydrophobic, hydrophilic and charge properties of a protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein hydropathy\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0137\"}], \"name\": \"Protein hydropathy\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0137\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Enzyme or chemical cleavage sites and proteolytic or mass calculations on a protein sequence.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein cleavage sites and proteolysis\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0141\"}], \"name\": \"Protein cleavage sites and proteolysis\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0141\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The comparison of two or more protein structures.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein structure comparison\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0143\"}], \"name\": \"Protein structure comparison\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0143\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The processing and analysis of inter-atomic or inter-residue interactions in protein (3D) structures.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein residue interactions\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0144\"}], \"name\": \"Protein residue interactions\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0144\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein-protein interactions, individual interactions and networks, protein complexes, protein functional coupling etc.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein-protein interactions\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0147\"}], \"name\": \"Protein-protein interactions\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0147\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein-ligand (small molecule) interactions.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein-ligand interactions\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0148\"}], \"name\": \"Protein-ligand interactions\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0148\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Protein-DNA/RNA interactions.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein-nucleic acid interactions\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0149\"}], \"name\": \"Protein-nucleic acid interactions\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0149\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The design of proteins with specific properties, typically by designing changes (via site-directed mutagenesis) to an existing protein.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein design\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0150\"}], \"name\": \"Protein design\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0150\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"G-protein coupled receptors (GPCRs).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||G protein-coupled receptors (GPCR)\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0151\"}], \"name\": \"G protein-coupled receptors (GPCR)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0151\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Edit, convert or otherwise change a molecular sequence, either randomly or specifically.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Sequence editing\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0156\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence editing\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0156\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Conserved patterns (motifs) in molecular sequences, that (typically) describe functional or other key sites.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Sequence motifs\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0158\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence motifs\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0158\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"Motifs\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The comparison of two or more molecular sequences, for example sequence alignment and clustering.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Sequence comparison\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0159\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence comparison\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0159\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"Search and retrieve molecular sequences that are similar to a sequence-based query (typically a simple sequence).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Sequence database search\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0163\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence database search\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0163\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The comparison and grouping together of molecular sequences on the basis of their similarities.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Sequence clustering\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0164\"}], \"name\": \"Sequence clustering\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0164\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The processing, analysis or use of some type of structural (3D) profile or template; a computational entity (typically a numerical matrix) that is derived from and represents a structure or structure alignment.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Structural (3D) profiles\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0167\"}], \"name\": \"Structural (3D) profiles\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0167\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The prediction, modelling, recognition or design of protein secondary or tertiary structure or other structural features.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein structure prediction\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0172\"}], \"name\": \"Protein structure prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0172\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The folding of nucleic acid molecules and the prediction or design of nucleic acid (typically RNA) sequences with specific conformations.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Nucleic acid structure prediction\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0173\"}], \"name\": \"Nucleic acid structure prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0173\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The prediction of three-dimensional structure of a (typically protein) sequence from first principles, using a physics-based or empirical scoring function and without using explicit structural templates.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Ab initio structure prediction\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0174\"}], \"name\": \"Ab initio structure prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0174\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The modelling of the three-dimensional structure of a protein using known sequence and structural data.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Homology modelling\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0175\"}], \"name\": \"Homology modelling\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0175\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The modelling the structure of proteins in complex with small molecules or other macromolecules.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Molecular docking\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0177\"}], \"name\": \"Molecular docking\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0177\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The prediction of secondary or supersecondary structure of protein sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein secondary structure prediction\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0178\"}], \"name\": \"Protein secondary structure prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0178\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The prediction of tertiary structure of protein sequences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein tertiary structure prediction\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0179\"}], \"name\": \"Protein tertiary structure prediction\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0179\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, {\"definition\": \"The recognition (prediction and assignment) of known protein structural domains or folds in protein sequence(s).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Protein fold recognition\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0180\"}]