omparing short sequences (reads) to each other.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Transcriptome assembly (de novo)\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||operation_3259\"}], \"name\": \"Transcriptome assembly (de novo)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3259\", \"exact_synonyms\": [\"de novo transcriptome assembly\"], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"operation_3260\": {\"definition\": \"Infer a transcriptome sequence by mapping short reads to a reference genome.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Transcriptome assembly (mapping)\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||operation_3260\"}], \"name\": \"Transcriptome assembly (mapping)\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3260\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"operation_3289\": {\"definition\": \"Search for and retrieve a data identifier of some kind, e.g. a database entry accession.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||ID retrieval\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||operation_3289\"}], \"name\": \"ID retrieval\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3289\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"operation_3353\": {\"definition\": \"Compare two or more ontologies, e.g. identify differences.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Ontology comparison\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||operation_3353\"}], \"name\": \"Ontology comparison\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/operation_3353\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"operation_3430\": {\"definition\": \"Predict, recognise and identify functional or other key sites within nucleic acid sequences, typically by scanning for known motifs, patterns and regular expressions.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Nucleic acid sequence feature detection\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||operatio