ology.org/topic_0606\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0608\": {\"definition\": \"General cell culture or data on a specific cell lines.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Cell and tissue culture\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0608\"}], \"name\": \"Cell and tissue culture\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0608\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0612\": {\"definition\": \"The cell cycle including key genes and proteins.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Cell cycle\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0612\"}], \"name\": \"Cell cycle\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0612\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0613\": {\"definition\": \"The physicochemical, biochemical or structural properties of amino acids or peptides.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Peptides and amino acids\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0613\"}], \"name\": \"Peptides and amino acids\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0613\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0616\": {\"definition\": \"A specific organelle, or organelles in general, typically the genes and proteins (or genome and proteome).\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Organelles\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0616\"}], \"name\": \"Organelles\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0616\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms\": [], \"children\": []}, \"topic_0617\": {\"definition\": \"Ribosomes, typically of ribosome-related genes and proteins.\", \"path\": [{\"name\": \"Deprecated||Ribosomes\", \"key\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||topic_0617\"}], \"name\": \"Ribosomes\", \"uri\": \"http://edamontology.org/topic_0617\", \"exact_synonyms\": [], \"narrow_synonyms