ym or abbreviation of the gene name.\", \"n\": \"Gene name (Arabidopsis)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"data_1890\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Deprecated||Gene name (Arabidopsis)\", \"k\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||data_1890\"}], \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, \"data_1892\": {\"d\": \"Name of a gene from the GeneFarm database.\", \"n\": \"Gene name (GeneFarm)\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"data_1892\", \"es\": [\"GeneFarm gene ID\"], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Deprecated||Gene name (GeneFarm)\", \"k\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||data_1892\"}], \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, \"data_1906\": {\"d\": \"A stretch of DNA that is closely linked to the genes underlying a quantitative trait (a phenotype that varies in degree and depends upon the interactions between multiple genes and their environment).\", \"n\": \"Quantitative trait locus\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"data_1906\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Deprecated||Quantitative trait locus\", \"k\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||data_1906\"}], \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, \"data_2009\": {\"d\": \"A name for a genetic locus conforming to a scheme that names loci (such as predicted genes) depending on their position in a molecular sequence, for example a completely sequenced genome or chromosome.\", \"n\": \"Ordered locus name\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"data_2009\", \"es\": [], \"ch\": [], \"p\": [{\"n\": \"Deprecated||Ordered locus name\", \"k\": \"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#deprecatedclass||data_2009\"}], \"hi\": [], \"ho\": [], \"ht\": []}, \"data_2018\": {\"d\": \"A human-readable collection of information which (typically) is generated or collated by hand and which describes a biological entity, phenomena or associated primary (e.g. sequence or structural) data, as distinct from the primary data itself and computer-generated reports derived from it.\", \"n\": \"Annotation\", \"ns\": [], \"u\": \"data_2018\", \"es\": [],